1
00:00:00,767 --> 00:00:03,967
♪ IN THE NOT-TOO-DISTANT
FUTURE ♪

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,467
♪ SOMEWHERE IN TIME AND SPACE ♪

3
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:10,500
♪ MIKE NELSON
AND HIS ROBOT PALS ♪

4
00:00:10,533 --> 00:00:13,633
♪ ARE CAUGHT
IN AN ENDLESS CHASE ♪

5
00:00:13,667 --> 00:00:16,833
♪ PURSUED BY A WOMAN
WHOSE NAME IS PEARL ♪

6
00:00:16,867 --> 00:00:19,867
♪ AN EVIL GAL
WHO WANTS TO RULE THE WORLD ♪

7
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:22,967
♪ SHE THREW A FEW THINGS
IN HER PURSE ♪

8
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,300
♪ AND IN HER ROCKET SHIP
SHE HUNTS HIM
ALL ACROSS THE UNIVERSE ♪

9
00:00:26,333 --> 00:00:29,133
[PEARL]
I'LL GET YOU!

10
00:00:29,167 --> 00:00:32,467
♪ I'LL SEND HIM CHEESY MOVIES ♪

11
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:35,467
- ♪ THE WORST I CAN FIND ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

12
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:38,533
♪ HE'LL HAVE TO SIT
AND WATCH THEM ALL ♪

13
00:00:38,567 --> 00:00:41,467
- ♪ AND I'LL MONITOR HIS MIND ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

14
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:44,800
♪ NOW, KEEP IN MIND
MIKE CAN'T CONTROL ♪

15
00:00:44,833 --> 00:00:47,367
- ♪ WHERE THE MOVIES
BEGIN OR END ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

16
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:50,867
♪ HE'LL TRY TO KEEP HIS SANITY ♪

17
00:00:50,900 --> 00:00:53,900
♪ WITH THE HELP
OF HIS ROBOT FRIENDS ♪

18
00:00:57,200 --> 00:00:58,800
YOU'RE ON.

19
00:00:58,833 --> 00:00:59,967
OH, MY STARS!

20
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,633
CHECK ME OUT.

21
00:01:01,667 --> 00:01:03,467
I'M DIFFERENT.

22
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:06,633
♪ IF YOU'RE WONDERING
HOW HE EATS AND BREATHES ♪

23
00:01:06,667 --> 00:01:09,633
- ♪ AND OTHER SCIENCE FACTS ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

24
00:01:09,667 --> 00:01:12,333
♪ JUST REPEAT TO YOURSELF,
"IT'S JUST A SHOW ♪

25
00:01:12,367 --> 00:01:15,700
♪ "I SHOULD REALLY JUST RELAX ♪

26
00:01:15,733 --> 00:01:20,667
♪ FOR MYSTERY SCIENCE
THEATER 3000" ♪

27
00:01:33,833 --> 00:01:35,800
- [CROW DOING VOICE WARM-UP]
- [TOM SERVO CLEARS THROAT]

28
00:01:35,833 --> 00:01:37,367
HI, EVERYONE.
MIKE NELSON HERE.

29
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:39,367
NOT A LOT OF TIME TO TALK.
YOU SEE, CROW

30
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:42,167
CHALLENGED TOM SERVO AND I
TO AN ANDY ROONEY-OFF.

31
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:45,800
- NO ONE QUESTIONS MY ABILITY
TO IMITATE ANDY ROONEY.
- ♪♪ [VOCALIZING]

32
00:01:45,833 --> 00:01:48,633
QUIET. IT'S TIME
FOR THE COMPULSORY ROUND.

33
00:01:48,667 --> 00:01:51,667
EACH OF YOU WILL HAVE
TEN SECONDS TO ANDY ROONEY.

34
00:01:51,700 --> 00:01:53,667
- YOUR TOPIC: SOUP.
- SOUP.

35
00:01:53,700 --> 00:01:55,800
CROW, BEGIN.

36
00:01:55,833 --> 00:01:57,500
- [AS ANDY ROONEY]
UH, SOUP IS FUNNY.
- [TIMER TICKING]

37
00:01:57,533 --> 00:01:59,500
IT'S NOT REALLY A MEAL,

38
00:01:59,533 --> 00:02:02,000
NOR IS IT REALLY A FIRST COURSE,

39
00:02:02,033 --> 00:02:04,467
'CAUSE IT'S MOSTLY MADE
OF WATER.

40
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:07,667
I FIND SOUP TO BE
THE MOST WATERY OF FOODS.

41
00:02:07,700 --> 00:02:09,500
- [GYPSY] MICHAEL J. NELSON.
- OKAY.

42
00:02:09,533 --> 00:02:11,967
- [BELL DINGS]
- [AS ANDY ROONEY] SOME SOUPS
HAVE BEANS IN THEM,

43
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:14,967
AND THERE ARE BEANS
THAT ARE AS WATERY AS SOUPS,

44
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:16,633
BUT THEY'RE NOT SOUPS.

45
00:02:16,667 --> 00:02:18,833
I DON'T TRUST SOUPS
ON THE WHOLE

46
00:02:18,867 --> 00:02:20,800
NO MORE THAN I TRUST STEWS.

47
00:02:20,833 --> 00:02:22,800
- [GYPSY] TOM SERVO.
- [BELL DINGS]

48
00:02:22,833 --> 00:02:24,800
[AS ANDY ROONEY]
THERE ARE FRENCH SOUPS
WITH BREAD IN THEM.

49
00:02:24,833 --> 00:02:27,800
I DON'T REALLY UNDERSTAND THAT.
TO ME, IT'S ARBITRARY.

50
00:02:27,833 --> 00:02:30,800
WHETHER YOU PUT BREAD IN A SOUP
OR SOUP IN A BREAD,

51
00:02:30,833 --> 00:02:32,800
YOU STILL HAVE SLOPPY BREAD.

52
00:02:32,833 --> 00:02:34,133
- FREESTYLE.
- [BELL DINGS]

53
00:02:34,167 --> 00:02:36,467
[OVERLAPPING ANDY ROONEY
IMITATIONS]

54
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:38,333
[TIMER CLICKING]

55
00:02:41,500 --> 00:02:43,333
- TIME!
- [BELL DINGS]

56
00:02:43,367 --> 00:02:46,167
- THE RESULTS WHEN WE RETURN.
- [AS ANDY ROONEY]
RESULTS ARE FUNNY.

57
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:47,867
[OVERLAPPING ANDY ROONEY
IMITATIONS]

58
00:02:54,333 --> 00:02:55,967
[OVERLAPPING ANDY ROONEY
IMITATIONS CONTINUE]

59
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,867
I SAY...

60
00:02:57,900 --> 00:03:00,633
I SAY THE WINNER IS...

61
00:03:00,667 --> 00:03:02,033
YOU GUYS, SHUT UP!

62
00:03:02,067 --> 00:03:03,833
- WHOA.
- GEEZ!

63
00:03:03,867 --> 00:03:05,633
[AS ANDY ROONEY]
EVER NOTICE
WHEN GYPSY GETS MAD...

64
00:03:05,667 --> 00:03:08,300
[OVERLAPPING ANDY ROONEY
IMITATIONS]

65
00:03:08,333 --> 00:03:11,333
OH, THE HELL WITH
EVERY LAST ONE OF YOU!

66
00:03:11,367 --> 00:03:13,867
[AS ANDY ROONEY]
OH, HEY, PEARL'S CALLING.

67
00:03:13,900 --> 00:03:15,700
YOU EVER NOTICE SOMETIMES
WHEN SHE CALLS,

68
00:03:15,733 --> 00:03:17,833
THE LIGHT FLASHES FAST,

69
00:03:17,867 --> 00:03:20,500
AND OTHER TIMES
IT FLASHES SLOW,

70
00:03:20,533 --> 00:03:22,867
AND OTHER TIMES
IT'S KIND OF A SLOW-FAST?

71
00:03:22,900 --> 00:03:24,367
- KIND OF A SLOW-FAST--
- I NOTICE THAT
PEARL SOMETIMES--

72
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:27,067
[MIKE, ROBOTS CONTINUE
ANDY ROONEY IMITATIONS]

73
00:03:28,833 --> 00:03:30,367
OH, I GET IT.

74
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:33,167
YOU'RE "IMPRESSIONATING"
MICKEY ROONEY.

75
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:35,467
CUTE.
OKAY, LOOK, NEL-BURGER.

76
00:03:35,500 --> 00:03:37,800
WE'RE REALLY BUSY.
WE'RE JUST GETTING MOVED IN.

77
00:03:37,833 --> 00:03:41,300
I'M GONNA RULE THE WORLD,
AND I DO NOT HAVE TIME
TO GET INTO IT RIGHT NOW.

78
00:03:41,333 --> 00:03:44,800
SO JUST A BRIEF OVERVIEW.
I'M GONNA RULE THE WORLD.

79
00:03:44,833 --> 00:03:47,133
THAT ABOUT COVERS IT.

80
00:03:47,167 --> 00:03:50,133
WHAT SHOULD I DO
WITH THIS BOX OF "LIVER ATS"?

81
00:03:50,167 --> 00:03:52,133
OH, THAT'S MY BOX
OF LIVE RATS.

82
00:03:52,167 --> 00:03:53,700
PUT THEM IN THE BASEMENT.

83
00:03:53,733 --> 00:03:55,500
RATS! OH, GOODNESS!

84
00:03:55,533 --> 00:03:58,300
[LAUGHS]
IT'S HERE, IT'S HERE!

85
00:03:58,333 --> 00:04:00,467
- OHH, GOODY!
- YOUR ORDER FROM SPIEGEL
JUST ARRIVED.

86
00:04:00,500 --> 00:04:03,300
MY WORLD DOMINATION
STARTER KIT.

87
00:04:03,333 --> 00:04:05,500
- LOVELY.
- YES, CONTAINED IN THIS BOX

88
00:04:05,533 --> 00:04:08,300
IS THE VERY MEANS BY WHICH I,
PEARL FORRESTER,

89
00:04:08,333 --> 00:04:10,467
WILL TAKE OVER THE PUNY,
WHIMPERING WORLD

90
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:13,367
AND COMMAND ITS INHABITANTS
TO KISS MY GRITS.

91
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:16,200
THIS RED-HOT METAL
OF DESTRUCTION,

92
00:04:16,233 --> 00:04:19,000
THE COLD, BLUE STEEL
OF THIS...

93
00:04:19,033 --> 00:04:20,967
THIS WHAT?
WHAT IS THIS?

94
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:23,033
- WHERE ARE THE DIRECTIONS?
- OH, HERE THEY ARE.

95
00:04:23,067 --> 00:04:24,967
UH, "CONGRATULATIONS
ON YOUR PURCHASE

96
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,967
"OF A DOOMSDAY MACHINE.

97
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,533
SOME ASSEMBLY REQUIRED."

98
00:04:29,567 --> 00:04:32,300
- OH, WELL, THEY DIDN'T
SEND THE THING--
- OH, GREAT.

99
00:04:32,333 --> 00:04:34,500
- ...FOR THIS THING.
- THEY DIDN'T SEND THE THING--

100
00:04:34,533 --> 00:04:37,633
- OH, IT SAYS RIGHT HERE--
"THING SHIPS SEPARATELY."
- IT'S NOT IN HERE, BUT...

101
00:04:37,667 --> 00:04:39,833
- OH, FOR THE LOVE OF--
- I CAN'T BELIEVE--

102
00:04:39,867 --> 00:04:42,133
- HELP ME! RATS! RATS!
EVERYBODY, RATS!
- [RATS SCREECHING]

103
00:04:42,167 --> 00:04:44,033
- WILL YOU TAKE THAT THING?
- OH, NO! NO!

104
00:04:44,067 --> 00:04:45,833
- THANK YOU VERY MUCH.
- HELP ME!

105
00:04:45,867 --> 00:04:47,467
- OW! OW! OW!
- NO THING, HUH?

106
00:04:47,500 --> 00:04:49,500
- COOL.
- COOL, MAN.

107
00:04:49,533 --> 00:04:51,167
MUST'VE BEEN SENT HERE
BY MISTAKE.

108
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:54,133
- WE GOTTA GET RID OF IT.
- NO! IT'S OURS!

109
00:04:54,167 --> 00:04:55,800
WELL, CROW, IT'S DANGEROUS.

110
00:04:55,833 --> 00:04:57,867
- BUT WE LOVE IT.
- COME ON, MIKE.

111
00:04:57,900 --> 00:05:00,667
- IT'S OUR GLOWING THING.
WE GET TO KEEP IT! [CRYING]
- YEAH. COME ON.

112
00:05:00,700 --> 00:05:03,967
YOU GUYS!

113
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:09,000
I REALLY NEED THAT THING
FOR MY THING.

114
00:05:09,033 --> 00:05:11,300
YOU KNOW, SOMETIMES I FEEL

115
00:05:11,333 --> 00:05:14,833
LIKE YOU GUYS DON'T WANT ME
TO TAKE OVER THE WORLD.

116
00:05:16,233 --> 00:05:19,467
WELL, NEVER MIND
HOW YOU'VE HURT ME.

117
00:05:19,500 --> 00:05:22,467
I STILL WANT YOU
TO HAVE YOUR MOVIE.

118
00:05:22,500 --> 00:05:24,667
IT'S CALLED PHANTOM PLANET.

119
00:05:24,700 --> 00:05:26,200
YOU'RE WELCOME.

120
00:05:26,233 --> 00:05:29,133
- OH! OH, RATS!
- [RATS SQUEALING]

121
00:05:29,167 --> 00:05:31,133
OH, THEY'RE KILLING ME.
OW!

122
00:05:31,167 --> 00:05:34,133
BOBO, YOU HARM A SINGLE
ONE OF GOD'S PRECIOUS CREATURES,

123
00:05:34,167 --> 00:05:36,133
SO HELP ME, I'LL KILL YOU.

124
00:05:36,167 --> 00:05:39,700
OH, IT GOT ME IN THE EYE!
OH! OH, BOY! OW! OW!

125
00:05:39,733 --> 00:05:42,467
- [TOM SERVO CRYING]
- I THINK I'D BETTER
SEND THIS BACK TO PEARL.

126
00:05:42,500 --> 00:05:44,533
NO! DON'T LET HER TAKE
OUR THING AWAY!

127
00:05:44,567 --> 00:05:46,800
WE'LL TAKE CARE OF IT
AND FEED IT AND STUFF!

128
00:05:46,833 --> 00:05:48,967
- [CRYING CONTINUES]
- SERVO, WHATEVER IT IS,
IT'S VERY DANGEROUS.

129
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:52,467
OH, SO RADIOACTIVE
IMMEDIATELY EQUALS BAD TO YOU.

130
00:05:52,500 --> 00:05:54,467
- [ALARM BLARING]
- WE'LL TALK ABOUT IT LATER.

131
00:05:54,500 --> 00:05:57,333
- IT'S MOVIE TIME.
- I CAN'T BELIEVE THE WAY
YOU OVERREACT SOMETIMES, MIKE.

132
00:06:09,067 --> 00:06:10,800
[MAN ON RADIO]
TEN, NINE--

133
00:06:10,833 --> 00:06:12,300
- ALL GREEN. EIGHT--
- I LIKED THAT THING.

134
00:06:12,333 --> 00:06:14,033
- SEVEN, SIX--
- IT'S GOTTA GO BACK.

135
00:06:14,067 --> 00:06:15,467
- OKAY.
- ...FIVE--

136
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:17,533
- IT'S A VOCAL LEADER.
- ...FOUR, THREE,

137
00:06:17,567 --> 00:06:20,467
TWO, ONE, ZERO.

138
00:06:20,500 --> 00:06:24,133
GRANDPA TRIED TO USE
THE MICROWAVE AGAIN.

139
00:06:24,167 --> 00:06:27,700
PAT BUCHANAN'S FIRST DAY
AS PRESIDENT.

140
00:06:27,733 --> 00:06:31,533
[MALE NARRATOR]
SINCE THE SPLITTING OF THE ATOM
ONLY A FEW DECADES AGO

141
00:06:31,567 --> 00:06:34,667
AND THROUGH HIS
GOD-GIVEN GENIUS OF SCIENCE,

142
00:06:34,700 --> 00:06:37,467
MAN, AT LAST, HAS SUCCEEDED

143
00:06:37,500 --> 00:06:39,333
IN PENETRATING
FURTHER AND FURTHER

144
00:06:39,367 --> 00:06:41,967
INTO THE UNKNOWN VASTNESS
OF SPACE.

145
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:43,967
THE MOON HAS BECOME
THE LAUNCHING BASE

146
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:45,333
FOR ADVANCED EXPLORATION.

147
00:06:45,367 --> 00:06:47,700
- OF THE MOON.
- FROM THIS PIVOTAL POINT,

148
00:06:47,733 --> 00:06:50,800
ASTRONAUTS,
AT THE RISK OF THEIR LIVES,

149
00:06:50,833 --> 00:06:53,467
SET OUT TO CONQUER
NATURE'S MYSTERIOUS FORCES.

150
00:06:53,500 --> 00:06:56,800
- LIKE THIS GRANOLA.
- YET MANY QUESTIONS
REMAINED UNANSWERED.

151
00:06:56,833 --> 00:06:59,300
- THEY DO?
- WHAT IS HIS EARTH

152
00:06:59,333 --> 00:07:02,700
IN RELATION
TO THE INCONCEIVABLE NUMBER
OF OTHER WORLDS?

153
00:07:02,733 --> 00:07:05,367
- OH, PHILOSOPH--
- IS HIS SPEED
TRULY THE FASTEST?

154
00:07:05,400 --> 00:07:07,500
- OH, I THINK THAT--
- HIS ACHIEVEMENTS THE GREATEST?

155
00:07:07,533 --> 00:07:11,467
- WELL, IT'S DIFFICULT--
- OR IS HE A MERE UNIMPORTANT
PIECE OF DRIFTWOOD--

156
00:07:11,500 --> 00:07:13,800
- WELL, THERE ARE SEVERAL--
- ...FLOATING IN THE VAST
OCEAN OF THE UNIVERSE?

157
00:07:13,833 --> 00:07:15,967
YOU KNOW, IS HE A LOSER?

158
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:18,467
COULD THERE BE LIFE
SIMILAR TO OUR OWN
ON OTHER PLANETS?

159
00:07:18,500 --> 00:07:20,700
- [MUTTERS]
- IS IT NOT POSSIBLE

160
00:07:20,733 --> 00:07:24,000
THAT ATMOSPHERIC CONDITIONS
OF RELATIVE ENVIRONMENTS

161
00:07:24,033 --> 00:07:26,167
CONTROL THEIR SHAPES AND FORCE?

162
00:07:26,200 --> 00:07:29,700
- STOP ASKING THINGS.
- IF SO, WOULD THEY BE GIANTS?

163
00:07:29,733 --> 00:07:31,300
- OR--
- PUNKS.

164
00:07:31,333 --> 00:07:33,300
...COULD PERHAPS
THE OPPOSITE BE TRUE?

165
00:07:33,333 --> 00:07:34,700
- [GASPS]
- COULD THEIR INTELLECT

166
00:07:34,733 --> 00:07:36,467
HAVE REACHED
A SCIENTIFIC LEVEL

167
00:07:36,500 --> 00:07:38,700
FAR ABOVE MAN'S DREAMS?

168
00:07:38,733 --> 00:07:41,833
- MMM.
- WHAT, THEN, WILL
THE FUTURE REVEAL?

169
00:07:41,867 --> 00:07:45,133
- UM, LYCRA.
- THIS STORY YOU ARE
ABOUT TO WITNESS

170
00:07:45,167 --> 00:07:46,967
- ...IS ONLY--
- A FIRST DRAFT.

171
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:47,800
...THE BEGINNING.

172
00:07:47,833 --> 00:07:49,633
WELL, THAT SAID,

173
00:07:49,667 --> 00:07:52,367
ENJOY YOUR CRAPPY SCI-FI MOVIE.

174
00:07:52,400 --> 00:07:55,667
EH, SOMEHOW THE ANSWER
TO ALL ITS QUESTIONS

175
00:07:55,700 --> 00:07:57,833
IS BIG WHITE GUYS IN JUMPSUITS.

176
00:07:57,867 --> 00:07:58,833
[CHUCKLING]
YEAH.

177
00:07:58,867 --> 00:08:00,800
- [MIKE] HEY.
- OH. SORRY.

178
00:08:00,833 --> 00:08:03,633
[EQUIPMENT BEEPING]

179
00:08:03,667 --> 00:08:05,000
LOG ENTRY.

180
00:08:05,033 --> 00:08:07,133
PEGASUS III.

181
00:08:07,167 --> 00:08:09,667
- MARCH 16, 1980.
- OH, OUR OLD FUTURE.

182
00:08:09,700 --> 00:08:11,300
CAPTAIN LEONARD, PILOT.

183
00:08:11,333 --> 00:08:13,300
LIEUTENANT WEBB, NAVIGATOR.

184
00:08:13,333 --> 00:08:14,667
THIS IS THE SEVENTH
AND LAST DAY

185
00:08:14,700 --> 00:08:16,300
OF SPACE RECONNAISSANCE
RESEARCH.

186
00:08:16,333 --> 00:08:17,967
FLIGHT 361

187
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:20,033
FROM THE UNITED STATES
AIR FORCE LUNAR BASE 1.

188
00:08:20,067 --> 00:08:22,133
WE'RE REALLY SICK OF EACH OTHER.

189
00:08:22,167 --> 00:08:24,667
WE ARE 21,000 MILES FROM BASE.

190
00:08:24,700 --> 00:08:26,667
BEARING AT 2-7-0 DEGREES--

191
00:08:26,700 --> 00:08:28,167
WE'RE CRANKY AND A LITTLE TIRED.

192
00:08:28,200 --> 00:08:31,033
...2, 3 MINUTES.

193
00:08:31,067 --> 00:08:34,500
AZIMUTH AT PLUS 46 DEGREES,

194
00:08:34,533 --> 00:08:36,800
4-6 DEGREES,

195
00:08:36,833 --> 00:08:38,700
5-0 MINUTES ECLIPTIC.

196
00:08:38,733 --> 00:08:40,967
CREW CUT AT .5 INCHES.

197
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:44,300
- ON ROUTINE SUCCESSIVE
APPROXIMATION
- [BEEPING]

198
00:08:44,333 --> 00:08:48,000
BY TRAJECTORY COMPUTER
USING DATA FROM
THE SPACE POSITION RECORDER.

199
00:08:48,033 --> 00:08:51,033
EARL, ARE YOU GONNA SHUT UP
FOR EVEN 30 SECONDS
ON THIS TRIP?

200
00:08:51,067 --> 00:08:53,633
- IT'S QUIET
AND LONELY OUT HERE.
- THANKS, EARL. WHAT AM I?

201
00:08:53,667 --> 00:08:57,200
AND, FRANKLY, WE'LL BE HAPPY
TO GET BACK TO
THAT DREARY OLD MOON.

202
00:08:57,233 --> 00:09:00,233
MAKES YOU FEEL REALLY HUGE
AND SIGNIFICANT, DOESN'T IT?

203
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:05,467
- WE'RE ALMOST A DEGREE
OFF TRAJECTORY, CAPTAIN.
- [BEEPING]

204
00:09:05,500 --> 00:09:07,300
EQUIPMENT CHECK'S OKAY.

205
00:09:07,333 --> 00:09:09,467
MUST BE AN OUTSIDE
ACCELERATION FORCE.

206
00:09:09,500 --> 00:09:11,800
WHAT DO YOU KNOW?
YOU'RE JUST AN INTERN.

207
00:09:11,833 --> 00:09:15,200
SO YOU CAN JUST TAKE
A SHARP LEFT IN SPACE.

208
00:09:15,233 --> 00:09:18,633
- SOMETHING APPROACHING FAST!
- IT LOOKS CRUNCHY.

209
00:09:18,667 --> 00:09:21,200
- I'M SETTING UP
FOR EVASIVE PATTERN.
- [MOCK CRYING]

210
00:09:21,233 --> 00:09:25,867
A LARGE PLANETOID OBJECT
IS ON A DIRECT COLLISION COURSE
WITH US.

211
00:09:25,900 --> 00:09:28,300
WE ARE UNDER 11 Gs
EXTERIOR ACCELERATION

212
00:09:28,333 --> 00:09:29,833
AND HAVE NO CONTROL WHATSOEVER.

213
00:09:29,867 --> 00:09:31,333
SORRY.
CAN WE NOT TAPE THIS?

214
00:09:31,367 --> 00:09:33,033
I'M PANICKING RIGHT NOW.

215
00:09:34,867 --> 00:09:37,833
THOSE NOOKS AND CRANNIES
REALLY HOLD THE BUTTER.

216
00:09:41,500 --> 00:09:43,633
DAMN, IT'S DEEP-FRIED.

217
00:09:43,667 --> 00:09:46,700
CAPTAIN, WE'RE GONNA HIT!

218
00:09:46,733 --> 00:09:48,867
- WEIRD. WE'RE IN SPACE,
AND I CAN HEAR YOU SCREAM.
- AAHHH!

219
00:09:50,400 --> 00:09:52,667
THE PHANTOM PLANET
IS QUILTED FOR SOFTNESS.

220
00:09:52,700 --> 00:09:54,800
[BLEATING]

221
00:09:54,833 --> 00:09:57,300
- SHEEP.
- AH.

222
00:09:57,333 --> 00:10:00,667
STARRING THESE PROUD
REPRESENTATIVES OF THE 1950s!

223
00:10:00,700 --> 00:10:03,467
YES, THEY ALL DROVE CHEVYS,
THEY ALL VOTED FOR EISENHOWER,

224
00:10:03,500 --> 00:10:06,667
AND THEY ALL THOUGHT SPEEDY
THE ALKA-SELTZER WAS HILARIOUS.

225
00:10:09,033 --> 00:10:10,467
[JOEL MUTTERING]

226
00:10:10,500 --> 00:10:13,333
OH, RICHARD KIEL.
A REAL STAR FOR ONCE.

227
00:10:16,500 --> 00:10:20,633
LET US NOW PROCLAIM THE MYSTERY
OF DELORES FAITH.

228
00:10:20,667 --> 00:10:22,800
♪♪ [TOM SERVO HUMMING
ALONG WITH SOUNDTRACK]

229
00:10:22,833 --> 00:10:25,733
HONEY BUNCHES OF DEATH.

230
00:10:29,700 --> 00:10:32,033
OH, IT WAS NICE OF THE CREDITS
TO LET THOSE THINGS THROUGH.

231
00:10:32,067 --> 00:10:33,533
YEAH.

232
00:10:35,033 --> 00:10:36,800
OH, THE GUY WHO DID
INTERPLANETARY SOUND

233
00:10:36,833 --> 00:10:38,300
WAS NAMED WALTER DICK.

234
00:10:38,333 --> 00:10:40,167
SEE? WALTER DICK.

235
00:10:40,200 --> 00:10:41,967
SO? HOW IS THAT SIGNIFICANT?

236
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:44,967
WELL, NOTHING.
JUST HIS NAME IS WALTER... DICK.

237
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:46,733
- [CHUCKLES]
- WELL, THANKS, CROW.

238
00:10:48,500 --> 00:10:50,133
AH.

239
00:10:50,167 --> 00:10:52,367
SO THE CREDITS ARE JUST GONNA
GET TINIER AND TINIER

240
00:10:52,400 --> 00:10:54,167
UNTIL THE MOVIE'S OVER THEN.

241
00:10:56,033 --> 00:10:58,000
WELL, MOVIE, I SURE HOPE
YOU CAN JUSTIFY

242
00:10:58,033 --> 00:11:00,300
ALL THIS PERSONNEL IN THE FILM.

243
00:11:00,333 --> 00:11:02,500
STUPID UNIVERSE,
QUIT EXPANDING!

244
00:11:04,233 --> 00:11:07,033
ATTACK OF
THE KILLER PEANUT BRITTLE.

245
00:11:08,400 --> 00:11:10,167
WOW. BIG.

246
00:11:12,533 --> 00:11:14,500
HEY, THE SAME GUY
WHO WROTE THE MESSIAH.

247
00:11:14,533 --> 00:11:17,167
FRED GEBHARDT WROTE
THE MESSIAH?

248
00:11:17,200 --> 00:11:18,967
NO, THE NAME BEFORE--
HANDEL--

249
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:21,033
[SCOFFS]
NEVER MIND.

250
00:11:21,067 --> 00:11:24,033
NO. COME ON.
YOU'RE JUST RECYCLING NAMES
AT THIS POINT, MOVIE.

251
00:11:24,067 --> 00:11:26,467
I GUESS FOCUS GROUPS
DEMANDED MORE CREDITS.

252
00:11:26,500 --> 00:11:28,467
WHAT HAPPENED TO THE FLUFFY,
ABSORBENT CREDITS?

253
00:11:28,500 --> 00:11:30,700
I LIKED THOSE.

254
00:11:30,733 --> 00:11:34,300
TODAY, THE MOON NARROWLY MISSED
HITTING A MAN'S EYE
LIKE A BIG PIZZA PIE.

255
00:11:34,333 --> 00:11:37,367
SCIENTISTS BELIEVE
THAT'S AMORE.

256
00:11:37,400 --> 00:11:40,167
HONEY, GET YOUR MOON MODEL
OUT OF THE LIVING ROOM.

257
00:11:42,833 --> 00:11:45,167
THEY MAKE THEM USE
THE DOGGIE DOOR.

258
00:11:45,200 --> 00:11:48,467
SIR, I'VE BEEN TESTING
THE PRESSURE EQUIPMENT
FOR THE MARS PROJECT.

259
00:11:48,500 --> 00:11:51,133
FORGET ABOUT THAT NOW, CHAPMAN.
YOU LEAVE TOMORROW MORNING.

260
00:11:51,167 --> 00:11:53,500
THE GENERAL WANTS SOMEONE
WITH YOUR EXPERIENCE.

261
00:11:53,533 --> 00:11:55,867
- I DON'T KNOW WHETHER
TO FEEL FLATTERED OR NOT.
- DON'T.

262
00:11:55,900 --> 00:11:57,533
WHAT EXACTLY
WILL I BE LOOKING FOR?

263
00:11:57,567 --> 00:12:00,133
- UH, FLOATING SPACE MONSTERS?
- [CHUCKLING]

264
00:12:00,167 --> 00:12:02,467
THIS IS NO JOKE, FRANK.
I WISH IT WERE.

265
00:12:02,500 --> 00:12:04,633
- DON'T MAKE ME HURT YOU.
- SORRY, SIR.

266
00:12:04,667 --> 00:12:06,867
YOU KNOW HOW RUMORS
MOVE AROUND THIS BASE.

267
00:12:06,900 --> 00:12:10,333
WELL, THAT'S ONE OF THE THINGS
WE HOPE THAT YOU'LL DISPEL.

268
00:12:10,367 --> 00:12:12,467
- WELL, YOU'RE THE COLONEL.
- I'M THE WEIRD GUY.

269
00:12:12,500 --> 00:12:13,833
I'LL TAKE A CRACK
AT ANYTHING ONCE.

270
00:12:13,867 --> 00:12:16,333
I'M GLAD YOU SAID THAT, SOLDIER.

271
00:12:16,367 --> 00:12:18,667
AND THAT'S ABOUT
ALL YOU'LL GET, FRANK--
ONE CRACK.

272
00:12:18,700 --> 00:12:20,967
ALL I NEED, SIR.

273
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:22,667
- ♪♪ [DRAMATIC SOUNDTRACK MUSIC]
- GEEZ! JUST BLAST OFF,
I GUESS.

274
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:25,867
DON'T WAIT FOR A COUNTDOWN
OR ANYTHING. GEEZ!

275
00:12:25,900 --> 00:12:28,467
DOES THIS TEPID LITTLE SCENE
REALLY DESERVE...

276
00:12:28,500 --> 00:12:32,133
♪♪ [IMITATING DRAMATIC
SOUNDTRACK MUSIC]

277
00:12:32,167 --> 00:12:35,967
18,000 MILES OUT
AT 2-7-0 DEGREES AZIMUTH

278
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:38,800
AND 4-7 DEGREES ECLIPTIC.

279
00:12:38,833 --> 00:12:41,300
SPEED: 4.6 MILES PER SECOND.

280
00:12:41,333 --> 00:12:42,667
[SINGSONG VOICE]
I'M NOT LISTENING.

281
00:12:42,700 --> 00:12:44,800
- CHECK. COMPUTER GUIDANCE ON.
- [BUTTON CLICKS]

282
00:12:44,833 --> 00:12:47,000
- STABILITY COURSE ON.
- [BUTTON CLICKS]

283
00:12:47,033 --> 00:12:49,533
- DIRECTIONAL ROCKETS PORT OFF.
- [BUTTON CLICKS]

284
00:12:49,567 --> 00:12:51,967
- DIRECTIONAL ROCKETS
STARBOARD OFF.
- [BUTTON CLICKS]

285
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:53,367
- TEST AUTOMATIC.
- CHECK.

286
00:12:53,400 --> 00:12:55,967
- PARTY TAPE. CHECK.
- [EQUIPMENT BEEPING]

287
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:57,967
- THAT DOES IT, CAPTAIN.
- HONEY.

288
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:00,133
- YOU CAN RELAX A BIT NOW.
- SWEETIE.

289
00:13:00,167 --> 00:13:02,633
TAKEOFF'S ALWAYS THE SAME.

290
00:13:02,667 --> 00:13:04,967
MY HEART POUNDS
LIKE A SLEDGEHAMMER.

291
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:07,300
♪♪ [IMITATING BEGINNING
OF PETER GABRIEL'S
"SLEDGEHAMMER"]

292
00:13:07,333 --> 00:13:09,467
- HOW ABOUT THE SCREEN?
- SORRY.

293
00:13:09,500 --> 00:13:10,967
[BUTTONS CLICKING]

294
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:12,833
THE MOON IS FUDGE-DIPPED.

295
00:13:12,867 --> 00:13:16,633
[CHAPMAN]
NEVER FAILS TO FASCINATE ME
FROM UP HERE.

296
00:13:16,667 --> 00:13:18,633
YOU KNOW, CAPTAIN,

297
00:13:18,667 --> 00:13:20,333
EVERY YEAR OF MY LIFE,

298
00:13:20,367 --> 00:13:22,500
- I GROW MORE
AND MORE CONVINCED...
- [SCOFFS]

299
00:13:22,533 --> 00:13:25,300
THAT THE WISEST AND BEST
IS TO FIX OUR ATTENTION

300
00:13:25,333 --> 00:13:27,833
ON THE GOOD
AND ON THE BEAUTIFUL--

301
00:13:27,867 --> 00:13:30,800
- DON'T HIT HIM.
- ...IF YOU'LL JUST TAKE
THE TIME TO LOOK AT IT.

302
00:13:30,833 --> 00:13:32,833
- YOU'RE SOME GUY, MAKONNEN.
- [CHUCKLES]

303
00:13:32,867 --> 00:13:34,533
[WOMAN ON RADIO]
LUNAR BASE 1 TO PEGASUS IV.

304
00:13:40,400 --> 00:13:44,300
SPACESHIP. NOW WITH
GENTLE-GLIDE APPLICATOR.

305
00:13:44,333 --> 00:13:47,300
WHAT'S OUR ELAPSED TIME
FROM BASE?

306
00:13:47,333 --> 00:13:50,300
14 HOURS, 22 MINUTES,
AND 30 SECONDS.

307
00:13:50,333 --> 00:13:54,133
YOU COULD STAY UP HERE
ANOTHER 14 HOURS
AND STILL SEE NOTHING.

308
00:13:54,167 --> 00:13:56,367
- EVEN 1400 HOURS.
- EVEN 14 MILLION.

309
00:13:56,400 --> 00:13:58,033
THAT'S ABOUT ALL
WE CAN DO, THOUGH.

310
00:13:58,067 --> 00:14:00,167
ARE YOU SURE
WE'RE STILL ON COURSE?

311
00:14:00,200 --> 00:14:01,867
- WHY?
- WE'RE UNDERWATER.

312
00:14:01,900 --> 00:14:03,867
WELL, I HAVE AN IDEA.

313
00:14:03,900 --> 00:14:06,967
- TURN TO
2-7-8 DEGREES AZIMUTH--
- YOU'RE MAD!

314
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:08,867
...0-47 DEGREES ECLIPTIC.

315
00:14:08,900 --> 00:14:10,500
YES, SIR.

316
00:14:10,533 --> 00:14:12,667
CHANGING COURSE
TO 2-7-8 DEGREES AZIMUTH,

317
00:14:12,700 --> 00:14:14,800
- ...HOLD 4-7 DEGREES ECLIPTIC.
- [BEEPS]

318
00:14:14,833 --> 00:14:17,200
[IMITATES BEEP]

319
00:14:17,233 --> 00:14:19,333
LANSFIELD TELLS US
TO CHARTER THE SAME COURSE

320
00:14:19,367 --> 00:14:21,167
PEGASUS III TOOK.

321
00:14:21,200 --> 00:14:23,300
WELL, THAT'S FINE, BUT I
DON'T THINK WE'LL GET ANYWHERE.

322
00:14:23,333 --> 00:14:25,700
- KNOWING US.
- IF THIS STRANGE PLANET

323
00:14:25,733 --> 00:14:27,467
DASHES ABOUT
LIKE IT'S SUPPOSED TO,

324
00:14:27,500 --> 00:14:29,867
IT FIGURES WE WON'T FIND IT
AROUND HERE,

325
00:14:29,900 --> 00:14:32,533
SO WE'RE CHANGING COURSE.

326
00:14:32,567 --> 00:14:34,633
LIGHTNING NEVER STRIKES TWICE
IN THE SAME PLACE.

327
00:14:34,667 --> 00:14:36,800
PRECISELY. YOU WITH ME?

328
00:14:36,833 --> 00:14:38,833
- LIKE I SAID,
YOU'RE THE CAPTAIN.
- UNFORTUNATELY.

329
00:14:38,867 --> 00:14:41,167
- I LIKE THE NEW READING.
- THANKS, RAY.

330
00:14:41,200 --> 00:14:42,800
YOU KNOW, CAPTAIN,
EVERY YEAR,

331
00:14:42,833 --> 00:14:44,300
I THINK MORE AND MORE
OF THE GOODEST

332
00:14:44,333 --> 00:14:46,367
AND THE NICEST AND BESTEST
THAT WE CAN BE.

333
00:14:46,400 --> 00:14:48,300
YEAH, WHATEVER, RAY.

334
00:14:48,333 --> 00:14:50,533
HEY, IT'S AN ADULT ROCKET SHIP.

335
00:14:50,567 --> 00:14:52,033
[CHUCKLING]

336
00:14:53,667 --> 00:14:55,367
- YOU KNOW, CAPTAIN--
- SHUT UP, RAY!

337
00:14:55,400 --> 00:14:58,167
WE COULD GO NUTS OUT HERE
JUST WAITING FOR SOMETHING
TO HAPPEN.

338
00:14:58,200 --> 00:15:01,633
WANNA PLAY ASTEROIDS?

339
00:15:01,667 --> 00:15:04,367
- YOU SEEM PRETTY MUCH AT EASE.
- YOU KNOW, CAPTAIN--

340
00:15:04,400 --> 00:15:06,467
WELL, I FIGURE IT'S JUST
THE SAME AS FISHING.

341
00:15:06,500 --> 00:15:07,833
YOU GOTTA BE PATIENT
AND WAIT.

342
00:15:07,867 --> 00:15:09,667
DRINK LOTS OF BEER.

343
00:15:09,700 --> 00:15:11,133
[ALARM BEEPING]

344
00:15:11,167 --> 00:15:12,867
THE ELECTROSTATIC METER'S
GOING HAYWIRE.

345
00:15:12,900 --> 00:15:16,633
LUNAR BASE 1 TO PEGASUS IV.
CAN YOU READ ME? OVER.

346
00:15:16,667 --> 00:15:18,800
- WELL, HAVE YOU BEEN PUBLISHED?
- PEGASUS IV TO LUNAR BASE 1.

347
00:15:18,833 --> 00:15:21,200
WE READ YOU. OVER.

348
00:15:21,233 --> 00:15:23,633
YOU ARE COMPLETELY
OFF COURSE, PEGASUS IV.

349
00:15:23,667 --> 00:15:26,633
- CHECK YOUR POSITION
IMMEDIATELY.
- OR YOU'LL GET SUCH A SPANKING.

350
00:15:26,667 --> 00:15:28,967
- D COMPUTER AND SPECTROMETER
ARE OUT.
- [BEEPING CONTINUES]

351
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:31,133
PEGASUS IV TO LUNAR BASE 1.

352
00:15:31,167 --> 00:15:33,133
WE ARE AWARE
OF BEING OFF COURSE.

353
00:15:33,167 --> 00:15:35,133
CANNOT EXPLAIN AT PRESENT.

354
00:15:35,167 --> 00:15:37,333
WE'RE ENTERING
A HEAVY MAGNETIC FIELD.

355
00:15:37,367 --> 00:15:39,333
SEVERAL INSTRUMENTS ARE OUT,
AND I'M AFRAID OTHERS ARE GOING.

356
00:15:39,367 --> 00:15:42,000
- AND IT'S NOT MY FAULT.
- GIVE US OUR EXACT POSITION.

357
00:15:42,033 --> 00:15:43,633
OVER.

358
00:15:43,667 --> 00:15:44,967
PEGASUS IV, YOU ARE--
[STATIC]

359
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:46,533
COMPLETELY BONED.

360
00:15:46,567 --> 00:15:49,500
CANNOT HEAR YOU, LUNAR BASE 1.
OVER.

361
00:15:49,533 --> 00:15:51,967
- [STATIC CONTINUES]
- HE'S SO PRETTY.

362
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:53,800
CHANGING TO MANUAL CONTROL.

363
00:15:53,833 --> 00:15:55,467
THAT'S THE GOOD
AND BEAUTIFUL THING TO DO, SIR.

364
00:15:55,500 --> 00:15:56,533
[RAY]
METEORS!

365
00:15:56,567 --> 00:15:59,300
ACH!

366
00:15:59,333 --> 00:16:01,533
- SOMEONE ON THE MIR FLUSHED.
- OOH-HOO.

367
00:16:04,500 --> 00:16:07,033
YOU KNOW, CAPTAIN,
I'M SCARED!

368
00:16:07,067 --> 00:16:10,500
- BOY, THAT WAS CLOSE.
- YEAH. AND I'M AFRAID
IT ISN'T OVER YET.

369
00:16:10,533 --> 00:16:14,300
ROVING GANGS OF METEORS
TERRORIZE THE GALAXY.

370
00:16:14,333 --> 00:16:16,567
OUT OF THE WAY,
SPACESHIP PUNK!

371
00:16:18,200 --> 00:16:21,000
WE'RE ON A SEMI-CLOSING COURSE
WITH THEM.

372
00:16:21,033 --> 00:16:23,467
SCREEN ONE'S FADING FAST.
WHAT ABOUT
THE INFRARED DETECTOR?

373
00:16:23,500 --> 00:16:25,633
- THAT'S OUT TOO.
- THE ONLY THING WE CAN DO

374
00:16:25,667 --> 00:16:28,333
IS TURN IT 9-0 DEGREES
TO THE SHOWER'S PATH.

375
00:16:28,367 --> 00:16:30,200
MORE METEORS ARE COMING.
IT'S OUR ONLY CHANCE.

376
00:16:30,233 --> 00:16:33,833
THAT WILL BE
3-1-1 DEGREES AZIMUTH

377
00:16:33,867 --> 00:16:36,133
AND MINUS 1-2 DEGREES ECLIPTIC.

378
00:16:36,167 --> 00:16:40,000
YEAH, FINE.
JUST TURN LEFT.

379
00:16:40,033 --> 00:16:41,500
- HERE THEY COME.
- PREPARE THE MILK.

380
00:16:41,533 --> 00:16:43,033
THIS IS IT.

381
00:16:44,867 --> 00:16:46,800
- [EXPLOSION]
- DOH!

382
00:16:46,833 --> 00:16:49,300
I FILLED MY PANTS, SIR.
IN FACT, I THINK I FILLED
YOURS TOO.

383
00:16:49,333 --> 00:16:50,867
[CHUCKLES]

384
00:16:54,067 --> 00:16:57,367
SUCKERS! WE'LL BE BACK!

385
00:16:57,400 --> 00:16:59,867
LOOKS LIKE THE WORST IS OVER.

386
00:16:59,900 --> 00:17:01,700
I SEE A LOT OF SPOTS.

387
00:17:01,733 --> 00:17:03,967
THOSE ARE IONIZED TRAILS.
THEY'LL PERSIST FOR AWHILE.

388
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:06,633
WELL, LET'S HOPE
THERE'S NO STRAGGLERS.

389
00:17:06,667 --> 00:17:08,800
WITH THESE INSTRUMENTS OUT,

390
00:17:08,833 --> 00:17:11,133
THERE WON'T BE ANY WAY
TO TELL IF THEY'RE COMING
FROM ANOTHER DIRECTION.

391
00:17:11,167 --> 00:17:12,967
TRICK NOW IS TO GET BACK
TO THE MOON.

392
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:15,200
PERMISSION TO TALK
IN FLOWERY PROSE AGAIN, SIR?

393
00:17:15,233 --> 00:17:17,200
- I THINK WE'LL MAKE IT.
- YEAH.

394
00:17:17,233 --> 00:17:19,467
I KNOW YOU THINK THAT.

395
00:17:19,500 --> 00:17:21,300
OKAY, RAY, LET'S GO THROUGH
A TYPE-B CHECK.

396
00:17:21,333 --> 00:17:23,033
- ALL RIGHT.
- HOP UP ON THE TABLE.

397
00:17:23,067 --> 00:17:25,800
- CABIN PRESSURE.
- 20, COMING UP.

398
00:17:25,833 --> 00:17:29,133
- RETRO PORT.
- 20 PORT, SIR.

399
00:17:29,167 --> 00:17:32,133
- POSITIVE.
- RETRO STARBOARD.

400
00:17:32,167 --> 00:17:34,467
- POSITIVE.
- MAIN CIRCUIT ONE.

401
00:17:34,500 --> 00:17:37,867
- GOOD AND BEAUTIFUL.
- CHECK.

402
00:17:37,900 --> 00:17:39,800
- NEGATIVE.
- HE LOOKS SO HURT.

403
00:17:39,833 --> 00:17:42,967
- MAIN TWO.
- NEGATIVE.

404
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:47,300
- HOW CAN HE SAY THAT TO ME?
- LET'S TRY THE AUXILIARIES.

405
00:17:47,333 --> 00:17:50,300
- MAIN ONE.
- NEGATIVE.

406
00:17:50,333 --> 00:17:53,467
- MAIN TWO.
- COOL, HUH,
WATCHING THEM CHECK THINGS

407
00:17:53,500 --> 00:17:56,033
OF WHICH WE DON'T KNOW
WHAT THEY ARE?

408
00:17:57,367 --> 00:17:59,300
IT'S NOT IN THE CIRCUITS?

409
00:17:59,333 --> 00:18:01,800
NO. THE METEORS MUST'VE SMACKED
INTO THE PROPULSION ELEMENTS.

410
00:18:01,833 --> 00:18:05,367
- THE FEED LINES?
- YEAH, IF WE'RE LUCKY.

411
00:18:05,400 --> 00:18:08,533
WELL, THERE'S ONLY ONE WAY
TO FIND OUT.

412
00:18:08,567 --> 00:18:11,667
- LOOKS LIKE IT.
- YEAH. STRIP DOWN, OIL UP.

413
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:16,633
- YOU KNOW--
- OH, BOY. WHAT?

414
00:18:16,667 --> 00:18:18,633
- ...THERE'S ONE THING SURE.
- WHAT'S THAT?

415
00:18:18,667 --> 00:18:20,500
THEY KNEW WHAT THEY WERE DOING
WHEN THEY FORCED US

416
00:18:20,533 --> 00:18:22,967
TO GO THROUGH THOSE SPACE DRILLS
DOZENS OF TIMES.

417
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:25,133
IF I REMEMBER CORRECTLY,
YOU HAD A DIFFERENT OPINION.

418
00:18:25,167 --> 00:18:26,967
- [CHUCKLES]
- DON'T RUB IT IN.

419
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:29,500
THAT WAS A BAD AND UNBEAUTIFUL
THING TO SAY, SIR.

420
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:32,967
WOULD IT BE REALLY
THAT MUCH OF A PROBLEM

421
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:35,700
TO HAVE HUMAN-SIZED DOORS?

422
00:18:35,733 --> 00:18:38,167
LIPSTICK OF THE GODS.

423
00:18:43,200 --> 00:18:45,133
MAN, WHEN HE STARTS TALKING
ABOUT HIS STAMP COLLECTION,

424
00:18:45,167 --> 00:18:48,500
I JUST GOTTA GET OUTSIDE.

425
00:18:48,533 --> 00:18:51,233
LOOK. THERE'S THE PROBLEM.
THE DRYER'S LEAKING.

426
00:18:53,700 --> 00:18:56,833
IN OR OUT, KIDS? WHAT, ARE WE
HEATING THE WHOLE UNIVERSE?

427
00:18:58,533 --> 00:19:01,300
I GOTTA GET THE MODEL NUMBER
FOR THE REPAIRMAN.

428
00:19:01,333 --> 00:19:05,533
I MISS THE EARTH SO MUCH.
I MISS MY WIFE.

429
00:19:05,567 --> 00:19:08,867
UH, COULD YOU GET YOUR BUTT
OUT OF MY FACE, RON?

430
00:19:10,667 --> 00:19:13,033
GOOD THING THERE'S
SO MUCH GRAVITY OUT IN SPACE.

431
00:19:13,067 --> 00:19:14,467
♪♪ [AMBIENT SOUNDTRACK MUSIC]

432
00:19:14,500 --> 00:19:17,233
SOUNDTRACK BY PERCY FAITH
AND HIS ORCHESTRA.

433
00:19:19,533 --> 00:19:21,833
HMM, THAT TOWEL WE STUFFED
IN THAT CRACK

434
00:19:21,867 --> 00:19:24,300
REALLY ISN'T DOING THE TRICK.

435
00:19:24,333 --> 00:19:26,000
I CAN'T BELIEVE YOU LEFT
YOUR TETHER ROPES

436
00:19:26,033 --> 00:19:28,500
AT LLOYD'S CABIN.

437
00:19:28,533 --> 00:19:30,500
UM, I'M NOT GOOD AT THIS, SIR.

438
00:19:30,533 --> 00:19:33,667
I'M ONLY GOOD AT FRUITY,
PHILOSOPHICAL SPEECHES.

439
00:19:36,233 --> 00:19:40,533
DON'T MOVE, RON.
THERE ARE TWO GIANT EYEBALLS
ON YOUR BACK.

440
00:19:40,567 --> 00:19:44,067
AHH. YOU SMELL GOOD, SIR.
LIKE VITALIS AND BACON.

441
00:19:47,667 --> 00:19:50,133
DOH-HO-HO!
DOH, STANLEY!

442
00:19:50,167 --> 00:19:52,133
IT'S A SPERM WHALE-POWERED SHIP,
SIR.

443
00:19:52,167 --> 00:19:53,633
YOU HAVE TO WATCH OUT
FOR HIS GLOW-HOLE.

444
00:19:53,667 --> 00:19:55,133
[LAUGHTER]

445
00:19:55,167 --> 00:19:57,033
YOU'RE TERRIBLE ASTRONAUTS.

446
00:19:59,833 --> 00:20:02,167
OH, LOOK.
IT'S THE INTERIOR OF OUR ROCKET.

447
00:20:02,200 --> 00:20:04,700
COOL. YOU CAN SEE
WHERE WE SIT.

448
00:20:04,733 --> 00:20:06,967
THIS LOOKS LIKE IT.

449
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:09,233
THE RETRO ROCKET FEED LINES
MUST BE CUT.

450
00:20:11,833 --> 00:20:14,500
THE GUY ON THE LEFT
HAS A CURVY PUCKEREDESQUE BUTT.

451
00:20:16,500 --> 00:20:19,800
MOSQUITOES ARE BAD TONIGHT.

452
00:20:19,833 --> 00:20:23,300
YEAH, IT USED TO BE GREAT
WHEN YOU COULD FIX
THOSE ROCKETS YOURSELF

453
00:20:23,333 --> 00:20:25,967
WITH JUST A CRESCENT WRENCH
BEFORE ALL THAT COMPUTER STUFF.

454
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:27,000
YEAH.

455
00:20:29,067 --> 00:20:31,467
FRANK, YOUR AIR LINE'S BROKEN.
FRANK!

456
00:20:31,500 --> 00:20:34,133
- ♪ MOTION IN THE OCEAN ♪
- ♪ EWWW ♪

457
00:20:34,167 --> 00:20:36,633
- ♪ HIS AIR HOSE BROKE ♪
- ♪ EW, OH ♪

458
00:20:36,667 --> 00:20:38,667
COME ON, CAPTAIN LOAD.

459
00:20:38,700 --> 00:20:40,533
[CHUCKLES]

460
00:20:43,033 --> 00:20:45,000
[MIKE, AS IF OVER RADIO]
I'M COMING, ELIZABETH.
[STATIC]

461
00:20:45,033 --> 00:20:47,167
ELIZABETH, I'M COMING.
OVER.

462
00:20:47,200 --> 00:20:49,000
IT'S BLACK BART AND HIS GANG.

463
00:20:49,033 --> 00:20:51,967
GET AWAY FROM THAT ROCKET,
YA VARMINTS!

464
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:53,633
OKAY. BREAK.
BACK TO POSITION ONE.

465
00:20:53,667 --> 00:20:55,867
AND WRESTLE.

466
00:20:55,900 --> 00:20:57,867
SINCE YOU'RE GONNA
DIE ANYWAY, RON,

467
00:20:57,900 --> 00:21:00,233
I'M GONNA STICK YOU
RIGHT IN THE MEAT LOCKER, OKAY?

468
00:21:03,167 --> 00:21:07,333
UHH! UHH!
WELL, I'M GLAD YOU'RE SAFE, SIR,
BUT COULD YOU LEND ME--

469
00:21:07,367 --> 00:21:10,200
OH, NEVER MIND. I'M FINE.
IT'S OKAY. I'LL HANDLE IT.

470
00:21:10,233 --> 00:21:13,033
YEP. JUST GOT TO, UH--
I'M FINE.

471
00:21:13,067 --> 00:21:15,033
IF YOU COULD JUST PROP
THE DOOR OPEN--

472
00:21:15,067 --> 00:21:17,667
NOPE. THAT'S-- THAT'S FINE.

473
00:21:17,700 --> 00:21:21,133
COULD YOU JUST GIVE A MESSAGE
TO MY WIFE AND KIDS,
IF YOU HAVE THE TI--

474
00:21:21,167 --> 00:21:23,667
WELL, NEVER MIND.

475
00:21:23,700 --> 00:21:28,633
OUR FATHER WHO ART IN HEAVEN,

476
00:21:28,667 --> 00:21:30,700
HALLOWED BY THY NAME...

477
00:21:42,533 --> 00:21:44,500
- HEY, SERVO--
- YOU KNOW, MIKE,

478
00:21:44,533 --> 00:21:46,300
EVERY YEAR OF MY LIFE,

479
00:21:46,333 --> 00:21:48,300
I GROW MORE
AND MORE CONVINCED

480
00:21:48,333 --> 00:21:51,167
THAT THE WISEST AND THE BEST
IS TO FIX OUR ATTENTION

481
00:21:51,200 --> 00:21:53,467
ON THE GOOD
AND THE BEAUTIFUL,

482
00:21:53,500 --> 00:21:55,800
IF YOU'LL JUST TAKE THE TIME
TO LOOK AT IT.

483
00:21:55,833 --> 00:21:57,300
WHICH IS WHAT I'M DOING
RIGHT NOW.

484
00:21:57,333 --> 00:21:59,333
I'M FIXING MY ATTENTION
ON A NUT GOODY

485
00:21:59,367 --> 00:22:01,467
AND A PICTURE
OF ANNA NICOLE SMITH.

486
00:22:01,500 --> 00:22:03,667
- RIGHT. THE GOOD
AND THE BEAUTIFUL. SURE.
- RIGHT.

487
00:22:03,700 --> 00:22:05,800
- AND HOW'S IT GOING?
- WELL, NOT GOOD, MIKE.

488
00:22:05,833 --> 00:22:08,500
I'M UNCONVINCED THAT
THE SMITH-GOODY COMBINATION

489
00:22:08,533 --> 00:22:12,000
REPRESENTS THE PERFECT BALANCE
BETWEEN THE GOOD
AND THE BEAUTIFUL.

490
00:22:12,033 --> 00:22:14,133
YEAH. I SEE YOUR POINT.
WHAT IF, UH--

491
00:22:14,167 --> 00:22:17,200
WHAT IF I SUBSTITUTED
A PICTURE OF TAWNY KITAEN
FOR THE BEAUTIFUL?

492
00:22:17,233 --> 00:22:18,667
- GOOD IDEA.
- HOW WOULD THAT WORK OUT?

493
00:22:18,700 --> 00:22:21,000
- LET'S TRY IT OUT HERE.
- HMM. UH, YEAH.

494
00:22:21,033 --> 00:22:24,467
NO. NO, NO, NO, NO.
TAWNY KITAEN IS ALL RIGHT,

495
00:22:24,500 --> 00:22:26,867
BUT NOW THE GOOD LOOKS,
WELL, KIND OF SCRAWNY.

496
00:22:26,900 --> 00:22:29,633
OKAY. I SEE YOUR POINT.
BUT WHAT IF I SUBSTITUTED

497
00:22:29,667 --> 00:22:31,800
THIS PLATE OF SAUERBRATEN
FOR THE GOOD?

498
00:22:31,833 --> 00:22:34,300
- GOOD AND SUBSTANTIAL.
- LET'S GIVE IT A WHIRL.

499
00:22:34,333 --> 00:22:36,833
- WHAT DO YOU THINK?
- YES. YES. YES. YES.

500
00:22:36,867 --> 00:22:39,700
YES, YES, YES, YES, YES,
YES, YES, YES, YES, YES!

501
00:22:39,733 --> 00:22:42,333
I THINK IT'S THE PERFECT BALANCE
OF GOOD AND BEAUTIFUL.

502
00:22:42,367 --> 00:22:44,300
- YEAH. YOU KNOW WHAT?
- WHAT?

503
00:22:44,333 --> 00:22:46,000
EVEN I GROW MORE
AND MORE CONVINCED

504
00:22:46,033 --> 00:22:48,300
THAT THE WISEST AND THE BEST

505
00:22:48,333 --> 00:22:51,633
IS TO FIX OUR ATTENTION
ON THE GOOD AND THE BEAUTIFUL.

506
00:22:51,667 --> 00:22:54,200
REPRESENTED BY A PLATE
OF SAUERBRATEN AND PICTURE
OF TAWNY KITAEN.

507
00:22:54,233 --> 00:22:56,500
RIGHT. UH,
WE'LL BE RIGHT BACK.

508
00:22:56,533 --> 00:22:59,367
YOU WOULDN'T WANNA TRY
TIFFANI AMBER THIESSEN
AND EGGS FLORENTINE, WOULD YOU?

509
00:22:59,400 --> 00:23:01,200
MM. THAT'S A LITTLE
OUT THERE FOR ME.

510
00:23:01,233 --> 00:23:02,833
YOU GOT THE SPINACH
AND THE THIESSEN.

511
00:23:02,867 --> 00:23:04,333
- IT'S A LITTLE WILD.
- I'M NOT SURE THAT WOULD WORK.

512
00:23:09,567 --> 00:23:12,467
♪♪ [HUMMING]

513
00:23:12,500 --> 00:23:14,167
AH.

514
00:23:16,833 --> 00:23:19,133
OH, MAN! I BURNED A PAN
OF MAC AND CHEESE

515
00:23:19,167 --> 00:23:20,967
AND FELL ASLEEP
IN THE T.V. ROOM AGAIN.

516
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:23,033
I HATE IT WHEN I DO THAT.

517
00:23:24,733 --> 00:23:27,967
THE U.S.S. PEN CAP.

518
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:30,033
AN EVEN SHORTER DOOR.

519
00:23:30,067 --> 00:23:32,400
WHAT, DID THEY DESIGN THIS SHIP
FOR DANNY DeVITO?

520
00:23:34,367 --> 00:23:36,367
I GUESS I COULD'VE HELPED HIM
WHEN HE WAS FLOATING AWAY,

521
00:23:36,400 --> 00:23:38,367
BUT I WAS JUST SO BEAT.

522
00:23:38,400 --> 00:23:40,300
[GROANS]

523
00:23:40,333 --> 00:23:44,133
- RAY...
- MY TUMMY'S FEELING BETTER.

524
00:23:44,167 --> 00:23:47,200
- RAY...
- COULD I HAVE SODA CRACKERS
AND 7UP?

525
00:23:48,533 --> 00:23:50,867
[MOCK GROANING]

526
00:23:50,900 --> 00:23:53,333
LIEUTENANT MAKONNEN...

527
00:23:53,367 --> 00:23:57,133
I'M GONNA PUKE,
AND IT'S GONNA FLOAT AROUND.

528
00:23:57,167 --> 00:24:00,500
THE HEADREST IS MADE
OF HOT DOG BUNS.

529
00:24:00,533 --> 00:24:02,633
OKAY, LET'S TAKE ROLL CALL.

530
00:24:02,667 --> 00:24:03,967
ME. HERE!

531
00:24:04,000 --> 00:24:05,667
RAY. DEAD!

532
00:24:05,700 --> 00:24:07,967
OKAY. GOOD.
THAT'S CLEARER NOW.

533
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:10,367
WELL, I HAVE ALL THE TANG
FOR MYSELF.
[CHUCKLES]

534
00:24:12,033 --> 00:24:14,667
A DROPPING'S
HEADED RIGHT FOR HIM.

535
00:24:19,233 --> 00:24:21,800
GOOD MORNING, MR. ODD-FACE.

536
00:24:21,833 --> 00:24:24,867
♪♪ [EERIE AMBIENT
SOUNDTRACK MUSIC]

537
00:24:24,900 --> 00:24:26,800
♪♪ [IMITATING
SOUNDTRACK MUSIC]

538
00:24:26,833 --> 00:24:29,533
- HE REALLY PITTED OUT
HIS FACE HERE.
- THIS IS CAPTAIN FRANK CHAPMAN,

539
00:24:29,567 --> 00:24:32,033
THE PILOT OF PEGASUS IV.

540
00:24:32,067 --> 00:24:34,300
MY SHIP IS BEING DRAWN
TOWARD AN ASTEROID.

541
00:24:34,333 --> 00:24:36,633
WELL, I LET MY SHIP BE DRAWN
TO AN ASTEROID.

542
00:24:36,667 --> 00:24:39,633
INSTRUMENTS COMPLETELY
OUT OF OPERATION.

543
00:24:39,667 --> 00:24:42,333
NAVIGATOR MAKONNEN... LOST.

544
00:24:42,367 --> 00:24:43,967
WELL, I LOST HIM.

545
00:24:44,000 --> 00:24:46,300
I CANNOT READ MY POSITION.

546
00:24:46,333 --> 00:24:48,333
I'M GONNA TRY TO LAND.

547
00:24:48,367 --> 00:24:50,667
I DON'T THINK I'LL MAKE IT.

548
00:24:50,700 --> 00:24:53,300
IF I DO,
I'LL CONTINUE RECORDING.

549
00:24:53,333 --> 00:24:56,633
IN SHORT, I FAILED.

550
00:24:56,667 --> 00:24:59,167
HEY, LOOK.
YOU CAN SEE THE ROCKET'S FUSE.

551
00:25:01,333 --> 00:25:04,700
THERE'S A FRENCH-BURNT PEANUT
OFF THE PORT BOW.

552
00:25:08,333 --> 00:25:10,133
IT'S EXTRA CRISPY.

553
00:25:10,167 --> 00:25:13,300
NO, WAIT.
IT'S ORIGINAL RECIPE.

554
00:25:13,333 --> 00:25:17,167
OH, NO.
IT COMES WITH SLAW.

555
00:25:17,200 --> 00:25:19,800
- OH, MY CONTACTS.
- OOH, MY CONTACTS TOO.

556
00:25:19,833 --> 00:25:22,167
[MIKE]
IT'S THE MOVIE. YOU GUYS DON'T
EVEN WEAR CONTACTS.

557
00:25:22,200 --> 00:25:24,633
OH. SORRY.

558
00:25:24,667 --> 00:25:28,367
WHO KNEW THAT HALLS VAPOR ACTION
COULD BE SO POWERFUL?

559
00:25:28,400 --> 00:25:30,200
OOH.

560
00:25:30,233 --> 00:25:32,867
MAYBE THEY'LL RUN INTO
WALLACE AND GROMIT
ON A CHEESE TOUR.

561
00:25:32,900 --> 00:25:34,067
YEAH.

562
00:25:35,567 --> 00:25:37,200
GEEZ,
HOW DID I MANAGE TO LAND

563
00:25:37,233 --> 00:25:39,300
WITHOUT THAT MINCING
LITTLE COPILOT

564
00:25:39,333 --> 00:25:41,400
JABBERING ABOUT THE GOOD
AND THE BEAUTIFUL?

565
00:25:43,667 --> 00:25:46,500
BETTER DEPLOY MY RUGGED,
HANDSOME INDEPENDENCE NOW.

566
00:25:50,333 --> 00:25:52,700
WHERE'S THE HOOKUP
FOR MY AIRSTREAM?

567
00:25:54,167 --> 00:25:57,167
SCYLLA AND CHARYBDIS.
ACTUAL FOOTAGE.

568
00:26:01,333 --> 00:26:05,300
OOPS! MY KEYS ARE STILL
IN THE-- DOH!

569
00:26:05,333 --> 00:26:08,833
I CLAIM THIS LAND
FOR STRANGE-LOOKING
BLOND MEN EVERYWHERE.

570
00:26:09,900 --> 00:26:12,300
HE NEEDS A POSTURE PAL.

571
00:26:12,333 --> 00:26:15,000
[IMITATING CHIMPANZEE
CHITTERING]

572
00:26:18,200 --> 00:26:20,667
[GROANS]
TURNS OUT IT'S NOT FUNNY AT ALL

573
00:26:20,700 --> 00:26:22,067
WHEN YOU FART
IN A SPACESUIT.

574
00:26:26,167 --> 00:26:29,000
♪ OH, WHAT A BEAUTIFUL MORNING ♪

575
00:26:29,033 --> 00:26:31,167
♪ OH, WHAT A BEAUTIFUL DAY ♪

576
00:26:31,200 --> 00:26:33,533
IT'S ONE SMALL STEP FOR MAN,
ONE GIANT LEAP FOR MAN--

577
00:26:33,567 --> 00:26:34,800
OW!

578
00:26:34,833 --> 00:26:36,833
IT'S A SPAZ-TRONAUT.

579
00:26:39,167 --> 00:26:42,167
MAN, I AM SO FAR
FROM THE TERMINAL.

580
00:26:44,233 --> 00:26:46,533
I'VE LANDED
IN A SEA-MONKEY BOWL.

581
00:26:48,367 --> 00:26:50,367
AH. OH, YEAH.
DON'T FALL DOWN.

582
00:26:50,400 --> 00:26:53,800
I JUST REMEMBERED THAT
FROM ASTRONAUT TRAINING.

583
00:26:53,833 --> 00:26:56,333
IS HE WAITING FOR TRIPLE-A
TO COME HELP HIM?

584
00:26:59,033 --> 00:27:02,000
THAT'S A HELL OF A SAND TRAP
TO BE STUCK IN.

585
00:27:04,167 --> 00:27:06,833
AH, YES.
FOSTER BROOKS IN OUTER SPACE.

586
00:27:08,500 --> 00:27:11,367
WOW. THIS PLACE IS GREAT
FOR MY SINUSES.

587
00:27:11,400 --> 00:27:13,800
[CHAPMAN'S VOICE]
WE SEEM TO BE ENTERING
A HEAVY MAGNETIC FIELD.

588
00:27:13,833 --> 00:27:15,800
SOME OF THE INSTRUMENTS ARE OFF
AND OTHERS ARE GOING.

589
00:27:15,833 --> 00:27:17,833
[RAY'S VOICE]
METEORS!

590
00:27:17,867 --> 00:27:19,633
[WOMAN'S VOICE]
YOU'RE COMPLETELY OFF COURSE,
PEGASUS IV.

591
00:27:19,667 --> 00:27:21,200
CHECK YOUR POSITION
IMMEDIATELY.

592
00:27:21,233 --> 00:27:23,867
CONGRATULATIONS, MRS. ASTRONAUT.
IT'S A BOY, BOY, BOY, BOY.

593
00:27:23,900 --> 00:27:25,133
- [RAY] FRANK--
- WAKE UP, FRANK.

594
00:27:25,167 --> 00:27:26,867
YOU WET THE BED, BED, BED.

595
00:27:26,900 --> 00:27:29,633
FRANK, YOU'LL HAVE TO TAKE
THIRD GRADE AGAIN-GAIN-GAIN.

596
00:27:29,667 --> 00:27:31,833
- [VOICES CONTINUE]
- FRANK, THIS IS NORTHWEST
COLLECTION AGENCY.

597
00:27:31,867 --> 00:27:33,967
DO YOU VALUE YOUR CREDIT RATING?

598
00:27:34,000 --> 00:27:36,467
I'M AFRAID YOU'RE NOT
7-ELEVEN TIMBER,
FRANK, FRANK, FRANK.

599
00:27:36,500 --> 00:27:39,467
FRANK, YOU'RE THE WORST
PARTY CLOWN WE EVER HAD,
HAD, HAD.

600
00:27:39,500 --> 00:27:40,833
[RAY'S VOICE]
I WISH IT WERE.

601
00:27:43,167 --> 00:27:46,167
- COME OUT, COME OUT.
- [GIGGLING]

602
00:27:48,500 --> 00:27:51,300
ARE YOU A GOOD SPACEMAN
OR A BAD SPACEMAN?

603
00:27:51,333 --> 00:27:54,067
LET'S PUT SHAVING CREAM
IN HIS HAND AND TICKLE HIS NOSE.

604
00:27:55,733 --> 00:27:57,867
COME ON. I TOOK CARE
OF THAT GULLIVER CLOWN.

605
00:28:00,400 --> 00:28:02,833
I'M JUST GONNA BEAT UP
HIS LEFT EYE.

606
00:28:05,000 --> 00:28:07,833
ABRASIVE, MICROSCOPIC ORDERLIES.

607
00:28:10,333 --> 00:28:12,167
BOY, I'M HUNGRY,
AND THEY'RE RIGHT THERE,

608
00:28:12,200 --> 00:28:14,967
AND THEY'RE SNACK SIZE.

609
00:28:15,000 --> 00:28:18,533
SIR, YOU LANDED
ON OUR HOSPITAL.

610
00:28:18,567 --> 00:28:20,533
UH, HANG ON.
LET ME JUST, UH,

611
00:28:20,567 --> 00:28:23,000
ADJUST YOUR CONTACT LENS HERE.

612
00:28:24,567 --> 00:28:27,800
- NO! A COLONY OF TINY MIMES!
- AGH!

613
00:28:27,833 --> 00:28:30,033
IF HIS ZIT POPS,
WE'RE ALL DEAD.

614
00:28:34,867 --> 00:28:36,533
- [THUD]
- OW, MY CORNEA!

615
00:28:36,567 --> 00:28:40,467
- CUT IT OUT.
- [THUDDING]

616
00:28:40,500 --> 00:28:42,467
- HEY, STEVE, DO "WIPE OUT."
- [FRANK INHALES]

617
00:28:42,500 --> 00:28:45,333
- [GASPS]
- HE'S GONNA SNEEZE!

618
00:28:45,367 --> 00:28:49,500
♪♪ [STRING INSTRUMENT:
HARSH, DISCORDANT TONES]

619
00:28:49,533 --> 00:28:53,300
WOW. HE'S GOT A SHAPE
LIKE DR. BEVERLY CRUSHER.

620
00:28:53,333 --> 00:28:57,633
HE OUGHT TO TRY
AN ULTRA-RELAXED-FIT SPACESUIT.

621
00:28:57,667 --> 00:29:00,300
- YOU ARE THE GREAT
GOD WIDE-HIP.
- [CHUCKLES]

622
00:29:00,333 --> 00:29:04,000
♪♪ [CONTINUES]

623
00:29:04,033 --> 00:29:07,200
UH, SIR, YOU NEED
A ZANTAC OR SOMETHING?

624
00:29:07,233 --> 00:29:10,667
SOMEBODY RUBBING A CAT
AGAINST A ZITHER?

625
00:29:10,700 --> 00:29:13,867
WHAT IS THAT?

626
00:29:13,900 --> 00:29:17,167
WE'VE GOT TO START
A BASKETBALL TEAM, YOU GUYS.

627
00:29:19,167 --> 00:29:21,700
I COULD USE ONE OF YOU GUYS
TO PICK MY TEETH.
THAT OKAY?

628
00:29:23,200 --> 00:29:26,000
- MOMMY!
- AAHHH!

629
00:29:28,200 --> 00:29:30,300
- ♪♪ [CONTINUES]
- ♪♪ [IMITATING
SOUNDTRACK MUSIC]

630
00:29:30,333 --> 00:29:32,700
HEY, GRAB HIS VISA
AND CHARGE TINY THINGS.

631
00:29:32,733 --> 00:29:35,033
RUN UP A HUGE TINY BILL.

632
00:29:36,667 --> 00:29:39,300
WELL, WE COULD HOLLOW HIM OUT
AND MAKE CONDOS OUT OF HIM.

633
00:29:39,333 --> 00:29:40,800
[MAN]
LOOK. HIS HELMET IS OPEN.

634
00:29:40,833 --> 00:29:42,300
[MAN #2]
THE GIANT IS GETTING SMALLER.

635
00:29:42,333 --> 00:29:43,967
[MAN #3]
WILL HE BECOME OUR SIZE?

636
00:29:44,000 --> 00:29:45,300
[MIKE]
FINALLY, I'M A SIZE EIGHT.

637
00:29:45,333 --> 00:29:47,500
OOPS. NO. A SIZE SIX.

638
00:29:47,533 --> 00:29:50,467
SIZE THREE.
OH, THAT'S TOO SMALL NOW.

639
00:29:50,500 --> 00:29:52,800
WELL, IF YOU CHUG TEN BOXES
OF SLIM-FAST,

640
00:29:52,833 --> 00:29:54,700
THAT'S WHAT YOU CAN DO.

641
00:29:58,000 --> 00:30:01,967
WHAT WERE THESE GUYS DOING
BEFORE HE ARRIVED?

642
00:30:02,000 --> 00:30:05,667
HELP! I'M BEING SMOTHERED
IN MY OWN JOCKEY SHORTS!

643
00:30:05,700 --> 00:30:07,500
HELP!

644
00:30:07,533 --> 00:30:09,200
WHAT'S HE DOING IN THERE?
STOP IT!

645
00:30:09,233 --> 00:30:10,533
EW!

646
00:30:15,000 --> 00:30:17,467
OH, WHY DID THAT HAVE TO SHRINK

647
00:30:17,500 --> 00:30:19,800
TWICE AS MUCH AS THE REST OF ME?

648
00:30:19,833 --> 00:30:21,633
YESTERDAY I WAS
A BOLD ASTRONAUT,

649
00:30:21,667 --> 00:30:25,167
TODAY I'M A 12-COUNT
PARTY SHRIMP.

650
00:30:25,200 --> 00:30:28,167
OH, YEAH. JUST PUT ME
IN YOUR CRASH AND IGNORE ME.

651
00:30:30,833 --> 00:30:33,167
RON, WHY DON'T YOU GO IN THERE
AND MOP UP FOR US, HUH?

652
00:30:35,167 --> 00:30:38,300
ATHOL FUGARD IS SCARED.

653
00:30:38,333 --> 00:30:40,000
[MEEKLY]
I'M A GIANT. ROAR.

654
00:30:42,833 --> 00:30:46,000
I HOPE THIS PLANET IS TOLERANT
OF NUDE PEOPLE.

655
00:30:47,367 --> 00:30:51,367
HEY. HEY, BUDDY.
WHERE'S YOUR V-NECK SMOCK, HUH?

656
00:30:51,400 --> 00:30:54,633
- LET'S GO IN AND GET HIM.
- OPTION. FLOOD THE ZONE
ON THREE. GO.

657
00:30:54,667 --> 00:30:56,833
- HE COULD HAVE A WEAPON.
- [MAN] HE SHOULD STAND TRIAL.

658
00:30:56,867 --> 00:30:59,133
[MAN #3]
WE MUST TAKE HIM TO SESSOM.

659
00:30:59,167 --> 00:31:02,167
MAN, IT STINKS IN HERE.
IT SMELLS LIKE SWEAT
AND HAIR OIL. OOH!

660
00:31:05,000 --> 00:31:06,500
[MIKE]
AH! HELP!

661
00:31:06,533 --> 00:31:09,033
SOMETHING FLESHY'S TOUCHING
MY LOWER BACK.

662
00:31:11,700 --> 00:31:14,733
I JUST WANTED TO BORROW
A CUP OF SAND.

663
00:31:19,200 --> 00:31:22,300
[TOM SERVO]
HE IS AN ALIEN.
HE ONLY HAS ONE.

664
00:31:22,333 --> 00:31:24,567
WE MUST BRING HIM TO PILOT.

665
00:31:25,900 --> 00:31:27,000
I COULD'VE TOOK HIM.

666
00:31:33,533 --> 00:31:36,300
- WE WILL BEGIN THE TRIAL.
- YES, SESSOM.

667
00:31:36,333 --> 00:31:38,467
WE MUST COMMAND THE FIRE--
WAIT.

668
00:31:38,500 --> 00:31:41,167
- NO.
- THAT'S THE WRONG MOVIE.

669
00:31:41,200 --> 00:31:44,467
ALOHA AND WELCOME TO HAWAII.

670
00:31:44,500 --> 00:31:46,300
[MAN]
THANK YOU, SESSOM.

671
00:31:46,333 --> 00:31:48,500
BRING IN THE JURORS.

672
00:31:48,533 --> 00:31:51,567
OR THE COCKTAIL WAITRESSES.
WHICHEVER YOU PREFER.

673
00:31:53,167 --> 00:31:55,333
MAN, YOU CAN JUST BRING IN
JURORS ALL DAY

674
00:31:55,367 --> 00:31:57,000
- ...AS FAR AS I'M CONCERNED.
- YES!

675
00:31:57,033 --> 00:31:58,967
WILL IPSALATA STEP FORWARD?

676
00:31:59,000 --> 00:32:02,200
LAURA PETRIE,
YOU ARE CHARGED WITH TREASON.

677
00:32:04,000 --> 00:32:06,000
HERE'S MY TOENAIL CLIPPINGS.

678
00:32:07,733 --> 00:32:09,533
EVERYONE GETS ONE SKITTLE.

679
00:32:09,567 --> 00:32:10,967
ONE, DEBBIE.

680
00:32:11,000 --> 00:32:12,700
HERE, NANETTE FABRAY.

681
00:32:12,733 --> 00:32:14,200
LILY TAYLOR.

682
00:32:14,233 --> 00:32:15,700
KITTY CARLISLE.

683
00:32:15,733 --> 00:32:17,133
KATE WINSLET.

684
00:32:17,167 --> 00:32:19,700
ELIZABETH MONTGOMERY.

685
00:32:19,733 --> 00:32:21,967
CALL THE PRISONER.

686
00:32:22,000 --> 00:32:23,867
BRING IN THE PRISONER!

687
00:32:23,900 --> 00:32:26,867
♪♪ [BASS DRUM]

688
00:32:26,900 --> 00:32:30,033
♪♪ [IMITATING BEGINNING
OF THE OLYMPIC ANTHEM]

689
00:32:35,333 --> 00:32:38,800
STAND HERE.
IN FRONT OF OUR LEADER
AND OUR JUDGE.

690
00:32:38,833 --> 00:32:40,700
- YOU MEAN THE OLD GUY
IN A DRESS?
- [CHUCKLES]

691
00:32:40,733 --> 00:32:43,367
IS THE PRISONER
FROM ANOTHER WORLD

692
00:32:43,400 --> 00:32:46,367
READY TO HEAR THE CHARGES
AGAINST HIM?

693
00:32:46,400 --> 00:32:49,533
CHARGES? WHAT CHARGES?

694
00:32:49,567 --> 00:32:51,467
- YEAH, THE CHARGES AGAINST YOU.
- I WILL ASK THE QUESTIONS.

695
00:32:51,500 --> 00:32:53,967
- SO BITE DOWN, MISTER.
- ARE YOU READY TO STAND TRIAL?

696
00:32:54,000 --> 00:32:56,867
IT SEEMS I HAVE NO CHOICE.

697
00:32:56,900 --> 00:32:59,533
ROSE AND VALERIE
SCREAMING FROM THE GALLERY.

698
00:32:59,567 --> 00:33:02,000
BUT FIRST I WANNA KNOW
WHAT I'M CHARGED WITH.

699
00:33:02,033 --> 00:33:03,867
EYES FRONT, MR. HORNY PANTS.

700
00:33:03,900 --> 00:33:06,500
[MAN]
WE'LL LET YOU KNOW IN TIME.
WHAT ARE YOU CALLED?

701
00:33:06,533 --> 00:33:09,667
- CHAPMAN. FRANK CHAPMAN.
- CHAP STICK CHAPMAN.

702
00:33:09,700 --> 00:33:12,800
WHAT IS YOUR OCCUPATION IN
THE WORLD FROM WHICH YOU COME?

703
00:33:12,833 --> 00:33:15,300
I'M A CAPTAIN IN THE AIR FORCE
OF THE UNITED STATES,

704
00:33:15,333 --> 00:33:18,000
A COUNTRY ON EARTH,
SPACE EXPLORATION WING.

705
00:33:18,033 --> 00:33:19,633
- OOH, EXPLORATION.
- YES.

706
00:33:19,667 --> 00:33:23,333
BUT YOU MUST KNOW ABOUT US.
YOU SPEAK OUR LANGUAGE.

707
00:33:23,367 --> 00:33:25,833
- WE DO NOT SPEAK IT--
- WE BELCH IT.

708
00:33:25,867 --> 00:33:27,467
...BUT HERE ON RHETON--

709
00:33:27,500 --> 00:33:29,300
RHETON?

710
00:33:29,333 --> 00:33:32,333
YES, RHETON,
THE NAME OF OUR PLANET.

711
00:33:32,367 --> 00:33:33,633
RHETON CHONG.

712
00:33:33,667 --> 00:33:36,133
HERE WE ARE ABLE TO TRANSLATE
ALL LANGUAGES

713
00:33:36,167 --> 00:33:38,367
THROUGH VOICE TONE WAVES.

714
00:33:38,400 --> 00:33:40,467
WHY ALL THESE EXPLANATIONS?

715
00:33:40,500 --> 00:33:43,300
- LET'S JUST STOMP HIM!
- LET US GO ON WITH THE CHARGES.

716
00:33:43,333 --> 00:33:46,300
YOU'RE RIGHT, HERRON.
THIS IS NO TIME
FOR EXPLANATIONS.

717
00:33:46,333 --> 00:33:49,300
- LET ME EXPLAIN--
- MAN FROM EARTH,

718
00:33:49,333 --> 00:33:53,967
YOU ARE ACCUSED
OF CAUSING INJURY
TO ONE OF OUR PEOPLE.

719
00:33:54,000 --> 00:33:56,633
I THOUGHT I WAS BEING ATTACKED,
AND I DEFENDED MYSELF.

720
00:33:56,667 --> 00:33:58,333
WITH COURAGE AND NUDENESS.

721
00:33:58,367 --> 00:34:00,700
I DIDN'T WANNA COME
TO YOUR WORLD.

722
00:34:00,733 --> 00:34:03,033
I LOST CONTROL OF MY SHIP.

723
00:34:03,067 --> 00:34:06,000
IT WAS LIKE BEING PULLED
TOWARD YOUR PLANET

724
00:34:06,033 --> 00:34:08,667
BY AN ENORMOUS
GRAVITATIONAL FORCE.

725
00:34:08,700 --> 00:34:12,800
- THANK YOU.
- YOU WERE. WHEN YOU CAME INTO
OUR PATH OF TRAVEL.

726
00:34:12,833 --> 00:34:14,467
PATH OF TRAVEL...

727
00:34:14,500 --> 00:34:17,467
UH, IS THAT THE PATH
YOU TRAVEL ON?

728
00:34:17,500 --> 00:34:19,300
PHANTOM PLANET...

729
00:34:19,333 --> 00:34:23,033
WE MANAGED, JUST IN TIME,
TO CONTROL YOUR LANDING

730
00:34:23,067 --> 00:34:26,200
BY RELEASING THE PRESSURE
IN OUR SPACE WARP.

731
00:34:26,233 --> 00:34:28,167
I DON'T UNDERSTAND.

732
00:34:28,200 --> 00:34:31,000
THERE ARE MANY THINGS
YOU WILL NOT UNDERSTAND HERE.

733
00:34:31,033 --> 00:34:32,367
BIG AND OBVIOUS DOORKNOB.

734
00:34:32,400 --> 00:34:34,467
MAYBE IN TIME, YOU SHALL.

735
00:34:34,500 --> 00:34:36,033
IN TIME?

736
00:34:36,067 --> 00:34:37,800
THAT IS CORRECT.

737
00:34:37,833 --> 00:34:39,800
THE JURY WILL NOW VOTE

738
00:34:39,833 --> 00:34:42,467
AND FIND YOU GUILTY
OR NOT GUILTY

739
00:34:42,500 --> 00:34:46,700
FOR INFLICTING INJURY
ON A RHETON MAN.

740
00:34:46,733 --> 00:34:50,133
WE FIND HIM GUILTY, GUILTY!
G-U-I-L-T-Y.

741
00:34:50,167 --> 00:34:52,000
GUILTY, GUILTY!
G-U-I-L-T-Y.

742
00:34:52,033 --> 00:34:54,967
WHOO! YAY!

743
00:34:55,000 --> 00:34:59,533
THE GUILTY PARTY WILL RECEIVE
A DREAM TRIP TO SUNNY CANCUN.

744
00:34:59,567 --> 00:35:02,967
- INHERIT THE WOW!
- THE VERDICT, JUDGE.

745
00:35:03,000 --> 00:35:06,000
WE WROTE IT OUT
ON OUR EYEBROW PENCIL SHAVINGS.

746
00:35:07,533 --> 00:35:12,133
UH, I'LL TAKE A PEPPERMINT ONE,
I GUESS.

747
00:35:12,167 --> 00:35:15,333
- I FIND YOU GUILTY AS CHARGED.
- HMM?

748
00:35:15,367 --> 00:35:17,700
YOU ARE NOW A FREE SUBJECT
OF RHETON.

749
00:35:17,733 --> 00:35:20,633
THE JURY IS DISMISSED.

750
00:35:20,667 --> 00:35:22,200
THAT IS ALL.

751
00:35:22,233 --> 00:35:24,133
YOU JUST SIMMER DOWN, MISTER.

752
00:35:24,167 --> 00:35:26,667
YOU ARE NOW A FREE SUBJECT
OF RHETON.

753
00:35:26,700 --> 00:35:28,367
THAT IS NOT ALL.

754
00:35:28,400 --> 00:35:30,367
LISTEN, I DON'T KNOW
WHAT KIND OF A PLACE THIS IS,

755
00:35:30,400 --> 00:35:32,467
BUT YOU MUST HAVE SOME KIND
OF LAW HERE.

756
00:35:32,500 --> 00:35:34,300
THIS PLANET PULLED ME TO IT.

757
00:35:34,333 --> 00:35:36,200
I DIDN'T COME HERE BY CHOICE.

758
00:35:36,233 --> 00:35:40,633
BY BEING HERE, YOU CANNOT
BE PERMITTED TO LEAVE IT.

759
00:35:40,667 --> 00:35:44,300
WE MUST KEEP OUR SECURITY
AT ANY COST,

760
00:35:44,333 --> 00:35:47,800
SO I MUST PRONOUNCE YOU GUILTY.

761
00:35:47,833 --> 00:35:49,200
YEAH, WHAT DAD SAYS.

762
00:35:49,233 --> 00:35:53,300
NO PENALTIES WILL BE LODGED
AGAINST YOU.

763
00:35:53,333 --> 00:35:55,967
BUT YOU MUST BECOME
A SUBJECT OF RHETON.

764
00:35:56,000 --> 00:35:58,467
YOU GET A DRESS LIKE MINE.

765
00:35:58,500 --> 00:36:00,133
TRIAL IS CONCLUDED.

766
00:36:00,167 --> 00:36:02,367
NOTHING IS CONCLUDED.

767
00:36:02,400 --> 00:36:04,033
WHAT IS THIS?
FIRST I'M FOUND GUILTY

768
00:36:04,067 --> 00:36:06,333
OF SOMETHING
THAT'S NOT MY FAULT,
AND THEN I'M SET FREE.

769
00:36:06,367 --> 00:36:09,500
WELL, FREE TO GO WHERE?
BACK TO MY WORLD
SIX INCHES TALL?

770
00:36:09,533 --> 00:36:12,467
DON'T WORRY.
NO HARM WILL COME TO YOU.

771
00:36:12,500 --> 00:36:15,133
JUST DON'T STEP
IN OUR MANY BEAR TRAPS.

772
00:36:15,167 --> 00:36:18,000
- I'M LIARA, SESSOM'S DAUGHTER.
- OOH.

773
00:36:18,033 --> 00:36:20,300
- I'LL SHOW YOU
TO YOUR QUARTERS.
- [IMITATING ROBOTIC WHIRRING]

774
00:36:20,333 --> 00:36:21,667
COME.
WE'LL TALK ON THE WAY.

775
00:36:26,400 --> 00:36:29,967
AND WEDNESDAY ADDAMS
IS CRESTFALLEN.

776
00:36:30,000 --> 00:36:31,633
WHAT HAS HAPPENED TO ME?

777
00:36:31,667 --> 00:36:33,533
YOU MEAN YOUR SIZE?

778
00:36:33,567 --> 00:36:36,633
WELL, OUR ATMOSPHERE,
TOGETHER WITH SOME ACCELERATION

779
00:36:36,667 --> 00:36:39,500
FROM OUR GRAVITATIONAL CONTROL,
HAS REDUCED YOU TO NORMAL.

780
00:36:39,533 --> 00:36:41,867
- NORMAL?
- NORMAL FOR US.

781
00:36:41,900 --> 00:36:45,000
YOU SEE, EVERYTHING HERE
IS IN PROPORTION
TO OUR PLANET'S SIZE.

782
00:36:45,033 --> 00:36:47,300
- REALLY?
- WE KNOW SEVERAL WORLDS

783
00:36:47,333 --> 00:36:49,633
THAT HAVE CREATURES
LARGER OR SMALLER

784
00:36:49,667 --> 00:36:51,200
ACCORDING TO THE SIZE
OF THEIR WORLD.

785
00:36:51,233 --> 00:36:52,800
YOU'RE EXPLAINING IT
TO A GARDEN SLUG.

786
00:36:52,833 --> 00:36:54,467
DO YOU FEEL ANY DIFFERENT?

787
00:36:54,500 --> 00:36:56,300
NO, BUT IT'S NOT
EXACTLY FUNNY TO THINK

788
00:36:56,333 --> 00:36:58,167
THAT SOMEONE ON EARTH
COULD CARRY ME ABOUT
IN THEIR POCKET.

789
00:36:58,200 --> 00:37:00,167
OH, WELL,
THAT WOULD NEVER HAPPEN.

790
00:37:00,200 --> 00:37:02,500
YOU SEE,
OXYGEN IN YOUR ATMOSPHERE

791
00:37:02,533 --> 00:37:04,633
WOULD RESTORE YOU IMMEDIATELY
TO YOUR REGULAR SIZE.

792
00:37:04,667 --> 00:37:06,667
- SO PEOPLE ARE JUST BALLOONS?
- YES.

793
00:37:06,700 --> 00:37:08,667
BUT EITHER WAY,
IT WOULDN'T MATTER.

794
00:37:08,700 --> 00:37:11,200
YOU'LL NEVER SEE
YOUR WORLD AGAIN.

795
00:37:11,233 --> 00:37:14,367
HA-HA! BURNED YOU GOOD,
ASTRO BOY.

796
00:37:14,400 --> 00:37:17,000
HEY, YOUR DARK-HAIRED FRIEND
SEEING ANYONE?

797
00:37:18,900 --> 00:37:20,533
MAN, THERE'S NO HAM LEFT.

798
00:37:20,567 --> 00:37:22,033
NOTHING YET?

799
00:37:22,067 --> 00:37:23,967
NO, SIR.
NO CONTACT FOR TWO DAYS.

800
00:37:24,000 --> 00:37:25,467
LUNCH IS RUINED.

801
00:37:25,500 --> 00:37:27,633
I'LL WAIT ANOTHER 24 HOURS.

802
00:37:27,667 --> 00:37:32,300
THEN, WITH OR WITHOUT ORDERS,
I'M SENDING OUT A SEARCH PARTY.

803
00:37:32,333 --> 00:37:35,133
[MIKE IMITATING SESSOM]
AND THAT'S WHY I'M DRESSED
AS QUENTIN CRISP.

804
00:37:35,167 --> 00:37:37,133
- YOU WANTED TO SEE ME?
- NO.

805
00:37:37,167 --> 00:37:41,667
YES. WILL YOU EXCUSE ME?

806
00:37:41,700 --> 00:37:44,867
THERE SEEMS TO BE A PROBLEM
WITH YOUR CREDIT CARD, SIR.

807
00:37:44,900 --> 00:37:47,667
- WE MUST TALK
ABOUT YOUR FUTURE.
- PLASTICS, BENJAMIN.

808
00:37:47,700 --> 00:37:49,300
YOUR FUTURE ON RHETON.

809
00:37:49,333 --> 00:37:51,533
MY FUTURE ON RHETON?

810
00:37:51,567 --> 00:37:55,300
I WANNA TALK ABOUT
GETTING BACK TO MY WORLD.
BACK TO EARTH.

811
00:37:55,333 --> 00:37:58,300
I'M AFRAID THAT IS IMPOSSIBLE.

812
00:37:58,333 --> 00:38:00,667
YOU MIGHT AS WELL ACCEPT
YOUR FATE.

813
00:38:00,700 --> 00:38:02,700
YOUR FATE OF BEING
ONE OF US.

814
00:38:02,733 --> 00:38:04,667
AND BEING ONE OF US,

815
00:38:04,700 --> 00:38:07,633
YOU MUST BE PRODUCTIVE
IN ONE WAY OR ANOTHER.

816
00:38:07,667 --> 00:38:09,633
WELL, WHAT IS IT
YOU WANT ME TO DO?

817
00:38:09,667 --> 00:38:13,167
YOU MUST HELP US TO KEEP
SPACESHIPS FROM YOUR WORLD
FROM LANDING HERE.

818
00:38:13,200 --> 00:38:15,800
BUT THAT'S MY ONLY HOPE
OF GETTING BACK.

819
00:38:15,833 --> 00:38:17,833
- DON'T GO THERE, MAN.
- FORGET ABOUT IT.

820
00:38:19,233 --> 00:38:21,000
SESSOM RULES US,
AND WE ARE CONTENT.

821
00:38:21,033 --> 00:38:22,967
WE'RE FILLED WITH JOY! OKAY?

822
00:38:23,000 --> 00:38:25,533
NOW, CAN'T WE GET ON
WITH THIS, SESSOM?

823
00:38:25,567 --> 00:38:27,533
HERRON IS HASTY.

824
00:38:27,567 --> 00:38:29,300
WE ALL ARE.

825
00:38:29,333 --> 00:38:33,000
OUR LIVES HAVE BEEN CHANGED
SO MUCH.

826
00:38:33,033 --> 00:38:35,500
- I WOULD LIKE YOU
TO BECOME ACQUAINTED WITH--
- HERBALIFE.

827
00:38:35,533 --> 00:38:36,967
...OUR WAYS.

828
00:38:37,000 --> 00:38:38,467
LATER, YOU MAY CHOOSE A WIFE.

829
00:38:38,500 --> 00:38:40,133
WIVES ARE MEN HERE, BY THE WAY.

830
00:38:40,167 --> 00:38:42,500
- [SESSOM] LIARA OR ZETHA.
- MM.

831
00:38:42,533 --> 00:38:46,500
ZETHA CANNOT SPEAK,
BUT SHE IS A FINE WOMAN.

832
00:38:46,533 --> 00:38:50,133
WELL, BETWEEN THE TWO,
IT WOULD BE DIFFICULT
TO MAKE A CHOICE.

833
00:38:50,167 --> 00:38:51,300
- CHOOSE HER!
- CHOOSE HER!

834
00:38:51,333 --> 00:38:53,800
- [SESSOM] IT IS NO PROBLEM.
- TRY BOTH.

835
00:38:53,833 --> 00:38:55,700
YOU MAY TAKE YOUR TIME.

836
00:38:55,733 --> 00:38:58,133
BUT ONCE YOU'VE MADE
YOUR CHOICE, REMEMBER--

837
00:38:58,167 --> 00:38:59,500
IF YOU TOUCH THEM,
THEY EXPLODE.

838
00:38:59,533 --> 00:39:02,467
...IT MUST NOT
BE TAKEN LIGHTLY.

839
00:39:02,500 --> 00:39:04,800
YOU MUST BE HUNGRY.
COME WITH ME.

840
00:39:04,833 --> 00:39:06,967
LIARA...

841
00:39:07,000 --> 00:39:10,633
GO NOW AND LEARN OUR WAYS,

842
00:39:10,667 --> 00:39:13,633
AND PERHAPS YOU MAY HELP US
WITH OUR PROBLEMS.

843
00:39:13,667 --> 00:39:15,800
YOU CAN DECIDE ABOUT THIS LATER.

844
00:39:15,833 --> 00:39:17,367
NOW YOU NEED TO EAT AND REST.

845
00:39:17,400 --> 00:39:19,700
BUT I WANNA STAY
AND LISTEN TO THE OLD GUY.

846
00:39:19,733 --> 00:39:21,667
[CHUCKLES]

847
00:39:21,700 --> 00:39:23,833
OOH, THAT'S HER PERSONAL RECORD
FOR GETTING NUDE.

848
00:39:23,867 --> 00:39:25,467
THAT'S AMAZING! WHOO!

849
00:39:25,500 --> 00:39:27,167
LET HER GO.

850
00:39:36,033 --> 00:39:38,233
[NO AUDIBLE DIALOGUE]

851
00:39:42,000 --> 00:39:44,200
YEAH, IT'S ALL FINISHED.
NOW IT'S JUST TIME
FOR THE DECALS.

852
00:39:44,233 --> 00:39:46,500
- SO COOL, MAN!
- YEAH, IT IS, ISN'T IT?

853
00:39:46,533 --> 00:39:48,500
WOW. WHAT DO YOU--
OH, PEARL'S CALLING.

854
00:39:48,533 --> 00:39:52,333
AAH! UH, MIKE!
PEARL'S CALLING!

855
00:39:52,367 --> 00:39:54,800
- WHERE THE HECK IS HE ANYWAY?
- I DON'T KNOW. I--

856
00:39:54,833 --> 00:39:57,800
OH, WAIT A MINUTE.
I WAS SUPPOSED TO HELP HIM
WITH SOMETHING, WASN'T I?

857
00:39:57,833 --> 00:39:59,633
- I DON'T KNOW.
- I CAN'T REMEMBER.

858
00:39:59,667 --> 00:40:01,700
- WELL, I'M SURE
HE'LL COVER FOR ME.
- HE USUALLY DOES.

859
00:40:01,733 --> 00:40:04,167
- ANYWAY, I'M GONNA PUT ON
SOME FLAMES MAYBE.
- COOL!

860
00:40:04,200 --> 00:40:06,300
- I WAS THINKING
OF PUTTING ON A SKULL.
- OH, YEAH!

861
00:40:06,333 --> 00:40:08,033
- "DOUBLE-F INTO TRIPLE ZED"--
- THAT'S THE ONE THAT GOES...

862
00:40:08,067 --> 00:40:10,367
I SIMPLY DON'T UNDERSTAND THAT.
THIS IS LIKE--

863
00:40:10,400 --> 00:40:11,967
- HELLO, TOYS.
- OH.

864
00:40:12,000 --> 00:40:13,967
AS YOU CAN SEE,

865
00:40:14,000 --> 00:40:16,633
OUR DOOMSDAY DEVICE
IS COMING ALONG QUITE NICELY,

866
00:40:16,667 --> 00:40:19,200
AND SOON THE WORLD
WILL KNEEL BEFORE ME...

867
00:40:19,233 --> 00:40:22,633
[GHOSTLY VOICE WAILING,
CHAIN RATTLING]

868
00:40:22,667 --> 00:40:24,800
- WHAT WAS THAT?
- I-I DON'T KNOW.

869
00:40:24,833 --> 00:40:27,000
- IT SOUNDS LIKE...
- [GHOSTLY VOICE,
CHAIN RATTLING CONTINUES]

870
00:40:27,033 --> 00:40:29,800
IT SOUNDS LIKE SOME HORRIBLE
DISEMBODIED SPIRIT.

871
00:40:29,833 --> 00:40:31,200
[GHOSTLY VOICE,
CHAIN RATTLING INTENSIFIES]

872
00:40:31,233 --> 00:40:33,367
IT'S GETTING CLOSER.

873
00:40:33,400 --> 00:40:35,700
THIS HAUNTED TOMB OF A CASTLE
HAS PRODUCED

874
00:40:35,733 --> 00:40:38,633
SOME ANCIENT,
HELLISH HELL SPAWN

875
00:40:38,667 --> 00:40:41,867
TO-- TO WREAK VENGEANCE ON US
FOR OUR WICKED WAYS.

876
00:40:41,900 --> 00:40:43,500
I'M NOT READY TO DIE.

877
00:40:43,533 --> 00:40:46,633
I JUST WANNA RULE THE WORLD.
IS THAT WRONG?

878
00:40:46,667 --> 00:40:48,000
OH, IT IS AMONG US.

879
00:40:48,033 --> 00:40:50,333
- OH, PEARL, HOLD ME.
- AAH!

880
00:40:50,367 --> 00:40:53,300
EMBRACE ME
IN THIS MOMENT OF OBLIVION.

881
00:40:53,333 --> 00:40:55,533
- OH-HO-HO, WE'RE DOOMED.
- [MUTTERING]

882
00:40:55,567 --> 00:40:58,533
OH, MAN, AM I TIRED.
[LAUGHS]

883
00:40:58,567 --> 00:41:01,833
I FEEL LIKE I'M DRAGGING A SAFE.
I NEED A NAP.

884
00:41:01,867 --> 00:41:04,300
WHAT THE HELL IS THIS?

885
00:41:04,333 --> 00:41:05,467
[LAUGHS]

886
00:41:05,500 --> 00:41:07,033
AIN'T THAT THE BERRIES!

887
00:41:07,067 --> 00:41:09,700
I'VE BEEN DRAGGING THIS CHAIN
ALL OVER THE DANG CASTLE.

888
00:41:09,733 --> 00:41:11,700
WHOO! NO WONDER I'M SO TIRED.

889
00:41:11,733 --> 00:41:14,467
[LAUGHING]

890
00:41:14,500 --> 00:41:15,667
OHH!

891
00:41:15,700 --> 00:41:18,633
OH!
[MUTTERS]

892
00:41:18,667 --> 00:41:22,033
- BRAIN GUY.
- MADAM.

893
00:41:22,067 --> 00:41:25,867
GET THE PIPE WRENCH,
AND THEN MURDER BOBO, WON'T YOU?

894
00:41:25,900 --> 00:41:28,800
[BOBO SNORING]

895
00:41:28,833 --> 00:41:30,467
GLAD TO.

896
00:41:30,500 --> 00:41:32,667
THANK YOU.

897
00:41:32,700 --> 00:41:34,967
WHAT ARE YOU LOOKING AT?

898
00:41:35,000 --> 00:41:37,000
GET BACK INTO THAT THEATER, YOU!

899
00:41:37,033 --> 00:41:39,867
YEAH. THEN I'M GONNA THROW ON
SOME BABY MOON HUBCAPS.

900
00:41:39,900 --> 00:41:41,667
- OH, MAN, THAT'LL BE SO--
- IT'S GONNA LOOK SO COOL.

901
00:41:41,700 --> 00:41:44,133
- WHAT, WHAT, WHAT?
- THERE'S MIKE! HE'S OUT THERE!

902
00:41:44,167 --> 00:41:46,967
DOH! OH, YEAH. THAT'S RIGHT.
I WAS SUPPOSED TO KEEP
AN EYE ON HIM.

903
00:41:47,000 --> 00:41:48,667
- [LAUGHING]
- [LAUGHS] YOU!

904
00:41:48,700 --> 00:41:51,133
- [ALARM BLARING]
- OH, HEY, MIKE,
BETTER GET YOUR CAN IN HERE!

905
00:41:51,167 --> 00:41:53,733
- IT'S MOVIE TIME!
- YEAH, STOP MESSING AROUND,
MIKE! COME ON!

906
00:42:07,033 --> 00:42:09,133
HE'S EATING THE WALL.

907
00:42:09,167 --> 00:42:11,500
THIS IS GOOD.
WHAT IS IT?

908
00:42:11,533 --> 00:42:14,800
I THINK IT'S THE EQUIVALENT
OF YOUR BREADFRUIT.

909
00:42:14,833 --> 00:42:18,133
WE MADE IT CHEMICALLY FOR YOU
SINCE NOTHING GROWS HERE
ON THIS PLANET.

910
00:42:18,167 --> 00:42:19,967
- HI, MIKE.
- OH, MAN.

911
00:42:20,000 --> 00:42:22,133
- HERE. DRINK THIS.
IT'S GOOD FOR YOU.
- [MIKE MUTTERING]

912
00:42:22,167 --> 00:42:24,167
- IT'LL HELP MAKE YOU REST.
- THANKS, YOU GUYS.

913
00:42:24,200 --> 00:42:25,967
- YOU NEED IT.
- YOU SAY NOTHING GROWS HERE.

914
00:42:26,000 --> 00:42:28,700
- OKAY.
- THEN HOW DO YOU EXIST?

915
00:42:28,733 --> 00:42:30,700
WELL, OUR BODIES
ARE SO CONSTRUCTED

916
00:42:30,733 --> 00:42:33,967
THAT WE NEED VERY LITTLE FOOD
BECAUSE OF THE AIR WE BREATHE.

917
00:42:34,000 --> 00:42:36,833
NEXT SCENE. GO!

918
00:42:36,867 --> 00:42:39,800
- FEELING BETTER NOW?
- WELL, MY NECK'S A LITTLE SORE.

919
00:42:39,833 --> 00:42:43,700
- I HOPE SO.
- YES. BUT I'D LIKE
TO GET OUT OF HERE.

920
00:42:43,733 --> 00:42:46,367
COULD YOU UNTIE MY LEGS?

921
00:42:46,400 --> 00:42:49,300
YOU'RE A STRANGE ONE,
FRANKCHAPMAN.

922
00:42:49,333 --> 00:42:51,467
- I'M A STRANGE ONE?
- YOU'RE A GIRL.

923
00:42:51,500 --> 00:42:54,133
WHAT ABOUT EVERYBODY ELSE?

924
00:42:54,167 --> 00:42:56,300
AND DON'T CALL ME FRANKCHAPMAN.

925
00:42:56,333 --> 00:42:59,033
MY NAME IS FRANK CHAPMAN.
TWO WORDS.

926
00:42:59,067 --> 00:43:00,800
FIRST WORD SOUNDS LIKE, UM...

927
00:43:00,833 --> 00:43:04,633
YES. FRANK CHAPMAN.

928
00:43:04,667 --> 00:43:07,367
OH, I'M SORRY.
I DIDN'T MEAN TO BE SO ROUGH.

929
00:43:07,400 --> 00:43:09,033
IT'S JUST THAT
THIS IS SO NEW TO ME.

930
00:43:09,067 --> 00:43:10,833
LADIES AND WORDS AND STUFF.

931
00:43:10,867 --> 00:43:13,333
YOU KNOW WHAT I'D LIKE TO DO
IF I HAD A CHOICE?

932
00:43:13,367 --> 00:43:15,633
- WHAT?
- I'D LIKE TO RETURN
TO MY SHIP.

933
00:43:15,667 --> 00:43:17,167
YEAH, WELL,
RETURN TO MY BUTT.

934
00:43:17,200 --> 00:43:19,467
WELL, THAT'S IMPOSSIBLE.

935
00:43:19,500 --> 00:43:22,367
- THEN, YOU SEE,
I'M STILL A PRISONER.
- NOT AT ALL.

936
00:43:22,400 --> 00:43:24,333
YOU'RE FREE TO GO
ANYWHERE HERE ON RHETON.

937
00:43:24,367 --> 00:43:26,867
- ALL 50 FEET.
- EXCEPT TO MY SHIP.

938
00:43:26,900 --> 00:43:29,833
YOUR ROCKET IS NO LONGER
ON THIS PLANET.

939
00:43:29,867 --> 00:43:31,467
IT WAS TOWED.

940
00:43:31,500 --> 00:43:34,467
IT WAS SENT OFF LAST NIGHT
WHILE YOU WERE SLEEPING.

941
00:43:34,500 --> 00:43:36,167
WORDS ARE JUST
BOUNCING OFF HIS SKULL.
[CHUCKLES]

942
00:43:38,900 --> 00:43:40,300
[CHATTER OVER RADIO]

943
00:43:40,333 --> 00:43:42,467
THE RESCUE SHIP
IS IN THE COUNTDOWN PHASE, SIR.

944
00:43:42,500 --> 00:43:44,200
THEY'RE WAITING FOR
YOUR FINAL OPERATION ORDERS.

945
00:43:44,233 --> 00:43:46,467
IS HE LISTENING
TO THE BALL GAME?

946
00:43:46,500 --> 00:43:48,700
PUT ME THROUGH TO THE CAPTAIN
OF THE RESCUE SHIP ON LAUNCHING.

947
00:43:48,733 --> 00:43:51,467
- YES, SIR.
- GOD, I LOVE CARAMEL.

948
00:43:51,500 --> 00:43:54,200
- BEECHER, THIS IS LANSFIELD.
- SO?

949
00:43:54,233 --> 00:43:55,633
YES, COLONEL.

950
00:43:55,667 --> 00:43:57,300
BEECHER,
YOUR FINAL INSTRUCTIONS

951
00:43:57,333 --> 00:43:59,133
ARE BEING TELETYPED
ON YOUR RECORDERS.

952
00:43:59,167 --> 00:44:01,333
- YES, SIR.
- AS YOU KNOW,

953
00:44:01,367 --> 00:44:04,467
SOMETHING UNUSUAL
MUST'VE HAPPENED
TO CHAPMAN AND MAKONNEN.

954
00:44:04,500 --> 00:44:06,800
- THE ROCKET TIPPED OVER, SIR.
- AND I DON'T MIND TELLING YOU

955
00:44:06,833 --> 00:44:09,033
THAT IT'S
OF GREATEST IMPORTANCE
TO SPACE TRAVEL

956
00:44:09,067 --> 00:44:10,700
THAT WE FIND OUT
EXACTLY WHAT HAPPENED

957
00:44:10,733 --> 00:44:12,533
TO THESE TWO MEN.

958
00:44:12,567 --> 00:44:15,300
SO BLAST OFF AND GOOD LUCK.

959
00:44:15,333 --> 00:44:16,867
WE'LL DO OUR BEST, COLONEL.

960
00:44:16,900 --> 00:44:19,800
- DON'T TELL HIM THAT!
- [CHUCKLES]

961
00:44:19,833 --> 00:44:24,467
ANONYMOUS SIMILAR GUYS, AWAY!

962
00:44:24,500 --> 00:44:28,333
SO WHICH PART OF THE UNIVERSE
YOU WANNA SEARCH FIRST?

963
00:44:30,833 --> 00:44:33,967
WOW. THIS IS ALMOST AS GOOD
AS 2001...

964
00:44:34,000 --> 00:44:35,967
NAILS DRIVEN INTO YOUR EYES!

965
00:44:36,000 --> 00:44:38,467
- [CHUCKLES]
- [SCOFFS]

966
00:44:38,500 --> 00:44:41,833
YOU KNOW, OTHER CAPTAIN,
EVERY YEAR, I BECOME
MORE AND MORE CONVINCED--

967
00:44:41,867 --> 00:44:44,000
- SHUT UP.
- SORRY.

968
00:44:46,500 --> 00:44:49,333
WOW. NO ONE TOLD ME
ABOUT THE BLACK ICE
OUT HERE IN SPACE.

969
00:44:49,367 --> 00:44:51,533
[IMITATING ROCKET WHIRRING]

970
00:44:51,567 --> 00:44:53,167
[WHIRRING STOPS]

971
00:44:57,033 --> 00:44:58,800
[MOCK GASPING]

972
00:44:58,833 --> 00:45:01,167
OH, SORRY ABOUT
DEPRESSURIZING THE CABIN.

973
00:45:01,200 --> 00:45:03,167
NEXT TIME, I'LL WARN YOU.

974
00:45:03,200 --> 00:45:05,633
[CHUCKLES]

975
00:45:05,667 --> 00:45:08,800
I CAN'T BELIEVE ALL NASA FLIGHTS
ARE NONSMOKING NOW.

976
00:45:08,833 --> 00:45:10,867
[SCOFFS]

977
00:45:14,667 --> 00:45:16,500
OOPS. EXCUSE ME.
THOSE LENTILS.

978
00:45:18,000 --> 00:45:19,800
SPACE BATCH!

979
00:45:19,833 --> 00:45:22,000
OPEN THE DOOR!
OPEN THE DOOR!

980
00:45:22,033 --> 00:45:24,000
- [IMITATES CLANK]
- OH!

981
00:45:27,900 --> 00:45:31,967
HEY, COLLECTING
FOR THE MARCH OF DIMES
IS COMPLICATED IN SPACE.

982
00:45:32,000 --> 00:45:34,500
- HEY, THEY HAVE
A NICE MUD ROOM.
- ♪♪ [AMBIENT SOUNDTRACK MUSIC]

983
00:45:34,533 --> 00:45:38,800
- ♪ SOME GUYS IN SPACE ♪
- ♪♪ [HUMMING ALONG]

984
00:45:38,833 --> 00:45:42,167
♪ SOME GUYS IN SPACE ♪

985
00:45:42,200 --> 00:45:44,833
DENISE, COME ON.
THE CAR'S RUNNING.

986
00:45:44,867 --> 00:45:48,133
[CHAPMAN]
I CANNOT READ MY POSITION.
I'M GONNA TRY TO LAND.

987
00:45:48,167 --> 00:45:49,333
DENISE, COME ON!

988
00:45:49,367 --> 00:45:51,367
I DON'T THINK I'LL MAKE IT.

989
00:45:51,400 --> 00:45:54,333
IF I DO,
I'LL CONTINUE RECORDING.

990
00:45:54,367 --> 00:45:55,800
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

991
00:45:55,833 --> 00:45:57,667
[SNIFFS]
OH, IT'S LIKE A GARBAGE SHIP
IN HERE.

992
00:45:57,700 --> 00:45:59,633
THIS IS CAPTAIN FRANK CHAPMAN,

993
00:45:59,667 --> 00:46:01,167
THE PILOT OF PEGASUS IV.

994
00:46:01,200 --> 00:46:02,467
AND CREW KILLER.

995
00:46:02,500 --> 00:46:05,333
MY SHIP IS BEING DRAWN
TOWARD AN ASTEROID.

996
00:46:05,367 --> 00:46:06,967
INSTRUMENTS COMPLETELY
OUT OF OPERATION.

997
00:46:07,000 --> 00:46:09,633
SORRY. I RAN HERE.

998
00:46:09,667 --> 00:46:13,333
MAN, ARITHMETIC IS JUST HARD.

999
00:46:13,367 --> 00:46:15,167
UM, SUM...

1000
00:46:15,200 --> 00:46:17,467
I CAN'T WORK
UNDER THESE CONDITIONS.

1001
00:46:17,500 --> 00:46:20,533
GORGEOUS WOMEN WAITING
TO SERVE MY EVERY WHIM.

1002
00:46:20,567 --> 00:46:23,000
I MUST KNOW MORE ABOUT
THE DIRECTIONAL FLIGHT MACHINE.

1003
00:46:23,033 --> 00:46:25,800
- WHEN THE TIME COMES.
- WELL, THE TIME HAS COME.

1004
00:46:25,833 --> 00:46:29,133
- THE WALRUS SAID.
- I WANT TO SPEAK TO SESSOM,
AND RIGHT NOW.

1005
00:46:29,167 --> 00:46:30,833
STUPID LEACH WOMAN.

1006
00:46:30,867 --> 00:46:33,167
- VERY WELL.
- HEY.

1007
00:46:33,200 --> 00:46:36,133
LOOKS LIKE SOM
IS RAPIDLY APPROACHING NON.

1008
00:46:36,167 --> 00:46:38,800
MM-HMM.

1009
00:46:38,833 --> 00:46:41,833
[IMITATING SESSOM]
BUT I THINK BELTED AT THE WAIST
GIVES ME A SLIMMER LOOK.

1010
00:46:41,867 --> 00:46:43,033
- DON'T YOU AGREE?
- [CLEARS THROAT]

1011
00:46:43,067 --> 00:46:44,133
OH.

1012
00:46:44,167 --> 00:46:45,700
FATHER...

1013
00:46:45,733 --> 00:46:48,667
FRANK CHAPMAN WISHES
TO SPEAK WITH YOU.

1014
00:46:48,700 --> 00:46:51,667
- DO YOU WANT TO TALK
ABOUT LIARA?
- MR. PRESIDENT.

1015
00:46:51,700 --> 00:46:54,200
THAT ISN'T WHAT I CAME HERE
TO DISCUSS.

1016
00:46:54,233 --> 00:46:58,200
MY WORK HAS REACHED A STAGE,
AND I NEED TO KNOW MORE
ABOUT YOUR GRAVITY CONTROL.

1017
00:46:58,233 --> 00:47:00,867
[QUIETLY]
ANYWAY, THE BLOUSE IS ON SALE
AT TALBOTS TODAY ONLY.

1018
00:47:00,900 --> 00:47:02,867
IT'S TOO SOON.
NOW, HOW DO WE KNOW

1019
00:47:02,900 --> 00:47:05,200
HE'S NOT A SPY
FOR THE SOLARITES?

1020
00:47:05,233 --> 00:47:07,967
YOU'RE TOO DISTRUSTING, HERRON.

1021
00:47:08,000 --> 00:47:09,633
ARE YOU A SPY FOR THE SOLARITES?

1022
00:47:09,667 --> 00:47:11,833
ALL RIGHT.
YOU MAY SEE IT.

1023
00:47:11,867 --> 00:47:14,133
ALTHOUGH I DON'T KNOW WHY
IN THE HELL YOU'D WANT TO.

1024
00:47:14,167 --> 00:47:17,700
LET ME JUST LIFT MY SKIRT.
THERE IT IS. TA-DA!

1025
00:47:19,533 --> 00:47:22,667
NOW WE SHALL DIVE
INTO THE MOSH PIT.

1026
00:47:27,200 --> 00:47:30,167
THIS CAME OUT
OF LYNDON JOHNSON'S GALLBLADDER.

1027
00:47:31,233 --> 00:47:33,200
- INCREDIBLE.
- EDIBLE.

1028
00:47:33,233 --> 00:47:35,033
BUT HOW?

1029
00:47:35,067 --> 00:47:36,967
THE HIGH DENSITY OF OUR PLANET

1030
00:47:37,000 --> 00:47:39,533
MADE IT POSSIBLE FOR US
TO ADVANCE GRAVITY

1031
00:47:39,567 --> 00:47:42,633
AND, THEREFORE,
ANTIGRAVITY THEORIES.

1032
00:47:42,667 --> 00:47:44,633
IT'S BEYOND ME.

1033
00:47:44,667 --> 00:47:46,800
EINSTEIN WAS WORKING
ON THIS PROBLEM,

1034
00:47:46,833 --> 00:47:48,800
BUT HE DIED BEFORE
HE COULD COMPLETE
HIS INVESTIGATION.

1035
00:47:48,833 --> 00:47:50,200
I'M TRYING TO WORK HERE.

1036
00:47:50,233 --> 00:47:52,967
WHAT CAUSES RHETON'S
HIGH DENSITY?

1037
00:47:53,000 --> 00:47:56,167
THE ATOMS ON THIS PLANET
HAVE NARROWER
ELECTRONIC ORBITS--

1038
00:47:56,200 --> 00:47:58,833
- UHHH...
- ...THAN THE ATOMS
ON MOST OTHER PLANETS.

1039
00:47:58,867 --> 00:48:00,800
THE SMALLER THEY BECOME,

1040
00:48:00,833 --> 00:48:02,833
THE EASIER IT IS
FOR US TO CONTROL

1041
00:48:02,867 --> 00:48:06,367
AND TAKE ADVANTAGE OF POSITIVE
AND NEGATIVE GRAVITY.

1042
00:48:06,400 --> 00:48:09,200
WHY IS RHETON GETTING SMALLER?

1043
00:48:09,233 --> 00:48:11,800
THIS PLANET IS SLOWLY
USING UP THE ENERGY

1044
00:48:11,833 --> 00:48:14,167
THAT HOLDS
THE ATOMIC PARTICLES TOGETHER.

1045
00:48:14,200 --> 00:48:17,000
- OH.
- YOU MEAN YOU MIGHT
DISINTEGRATE INTO NOTHING?

1046
00:48:17,033 --> 00:48:19,467
- YES, SOMEDAY--
- WHEN YOU'RE OLDER.

1047
00:48:19,500 --> 00:48:21,633
...BUT IT WILL NOT BE
IN OUR TIME.

1048
00:48:21,667 --> 00:48:23,833
- AH.
- WELL, I GUESS IT'S
THE SAME AS ON EARTH.

1049
00:48:23,867 --> 00:48:25,467
WE DON'T SEEM TO WORRY
THAT OUR SUN

1050
00:48:25,500 --> 00:48:27,467
MIGHT BE COOLING OFF
IN MANY MILLIONS OF YEARS.

1051
00:48:27,500 --> 00:48:29,667
YEAH, BUT DANGER FOR US
IS THAT SUDDEN BURSTS

1052
00:48:29,700 --> 00:48:32,133
OF CONCENTRATED HEAT
DIRECTED ON RHETON--

1053
00:48:32,167 --> 00:48:33,800
OH, SURE. YOU'RE GONNA
GET THAT. OH, YEAH.

1054
00:48:33,833 --> 00:48:36,333
...MIGHT SUDDENLY SPEED UP
THE PROCESS OF TIME.

1055
00:48:36,367 --> 00:48:38,333
YOU THINK THAT'S POSSIBLE?

1056
00:48:38,367 --> 00:48:40,500
WE HAVE ENEMIES WHO WANT
OUR KNOWLEDGE OF GRAVITY

1057
00:48:40,533 --> 00:48:42,500
AND WHO KNOW OUR WEAKNESS.

1058
00:48:42,533 --> 00:48:44,333
YOU'RE EXPECTING AN ATTACK?

1059
00:48:44,367 --> 00:48:47,133
WHEN YOU HAVE ENEMIES,
YOU ALWAYS EXPECT AN ATTACK.

1060
00:48:47,167 --> 00:48:49,633
UH, QUIET DOWN. I'M PUTTING
MY HANDS OVER THINGS HERE.

1061
00:48:49,667 --> 00:48:50,833
[CHUCKLES]

1062
00:48:52,567 --> 00:48:54,900
STUD SERVICE!

1063
00:48:56,867 --> 00:48:58,000
[HIGH-PITCHED VOICE]
EEEE!

1064
00:48:58,033 --> 00:48:59,900
SORRY.

1065
00:48:59,933 --> 00:49:02,533
HE'S JUST OUT
FOR HIS MORNING SWAGGER.

1066
00:49:02,567 --> 00:49:03,867
♪♪ [HUMMING]

1067
00:49:03,900 --> 00:49:06,033
HUH? OH, YEAH.
TAKE IT OFF.

1068
00:49:06,067 --> 00:49:08,367
OH. SORRY, SIR.
[CHUCKLES]

1069
00:49:08,400 --> 00:49:11,500
SLEEPING ON A BIG SLAB
OF TUNA STEAK HERE.

1070
00:49:11,533 --> 00:49:13,500
HELLO.

1071
00:49:13,533 --> 00:49:16,200
WE'RE CLOSED.

1072
00:49:16,233 --> 00:49:19,033
HOW DO YOU SIGN
"BEAT IT, LOSER"?

1073
00:49:21,867 --> 00:49:24,800
I'M SORRY MY WAIST
IS SO BIG FOR YOU.

1074
00:49:24,833 --> 00:49:27,800
YOU WANNA PLAY?
I GOT A BANANA-SEAT BIKE.

1075
00:49:27,833 --> 00:49:29,467
I'M GONNA TAKE A WALK.

1076
00:49:29,500 --> 00:49:30,867
STIR-FRY SOME VEGETABLES.

1077
00:49:30,900 --> 00:49:32,500
WILL YOU JOIN ME?

1078
00:49:32,533 --> 00:49:33,667
WE COULD LICK SOME WALLS.

1079
00:49:33,700 --> 00:49:35,300
COME ON.

1080
00:49:35,333 --> 00:49:37,000
WELL, I WAS KIND OF
DOING SOME STUFF.

1081
00:49:37,033 --> 00:49:38,667
I GOT A LOT--
WELL, OKAY.

1082
00:49:38,700 --> 00:49:41,833
I'LL TAKE A WALK WITH YOU.

1083
00:49:41,867 --> 00:49:45,000
YOU KNOW, THIS IS THE FIRST TIME
I'VE HAD A CHANCE
TO TALK TO YOU ALONE.

1084
00:49:45,033 --> 00:49:46,800
IT'S ALMOST LIKE YOU'VE BEEN
AVOIDING ME OR SOMETHING.

1085
00:49:46,833 --> 00:49:49,167
LET'S JUST WALK OVER HERE
TO THE OTHER END OF THE PLANET.

1086
00:49:50,333 --> 00:49:52,300
SO, DO YOU LIKE ANYTHING?

1087
00:49:52,333 --> 00:49:55,300
OR DO YOU KNOW THINGS OR...

1088
00:49:55,333 --> 00:49:58,567
HEY, HIS HELMET IS NOW
A MAJOR MAKE-OUT SPOT
ON THE PLANET.

1089
00:50:00,667 --> 00:50:02,500
HOW IS IT YOU'RE MORE DIFFERENT
THAN THE OTHERS?

1090
00:50:02,533 --> 00:50:04,333
OR LESS THE SAME,
IS WHAT I'M SAYING.

1091
00:50:04,367 --> 00:50:06,333
I DON'T MEAN YOUR SILENCE.
I--

1092
00:50:06,367 --> 00:50:09,500
I MEAN, YOU'RE WARMER,
MORE SENSITIVE.

1093
00:50:09,533 --> 00:50:11,800
I LIKE POTATOES!

1094
00:50:11,833 --> 00:50:14,700
THAT WASN'T REALLY A QUESTION,
'CAUSE I KNOW YOU CAN'T ANSWER.

1095
00:50:14,733 --> 00:50:16,633
SO I'LL KEEP TALKING
AND TALKING.

1096
00:50:16,667 --> 00:50:19,500
I JUST WANTED YOU TO KNOW
HOW I FEEL.

1097
00:50:19,533 --> 00:50:20,867
STRANGE WORLD...

1098
00:50:20,900 --> 00:50:22,500
ANYWAY, LET'S GET BUSY!

1099
00:50:22,533 --> 00:50:24,867
I DON'T WANNA HURT, LIARA.

1100
00:50:24,900 --> 00:50:27,300
- YOU DON'T EITHER.
- YES, I DON'T.

1101
00:50:27,333 --> 00:50:28,667
NO, I DO. WHAT?

1102
00:50:28,700 --> 00:50:30,800
I LIKE YOU.

1103
00:50:30,833 --> 00:50:32,633
AND YOU CAN'T SAY
YOU DON'T LIKE ME.

1104
00:50:32,667 --> 00:50:34,133
[CHUCKLES]

1105
00:50:34,167 --> 00:50:36,667
LET'S GO CHECK OUT MY ARMPITS.

1106
00:50:38,667 --> 00:50:40,300
HEH-HEH-HEH.

1107
00:50:40,333 --> 00:50:43,367
I JUST SMEARED ATOMIC BOMB
IN HIS UNDERPANTS.

1108
00:50:45,333 --> 00:50:48,033
LOOK AT THIS GUY.
GEORGE SHULTZ
IS MORE EXPRESSIVE.

1109
00:50:50,667 --> 00:50:52,967
I HAVE CHARGES TO MAKE
AGAINST THE EARTHMAN CHAPMAN.

1110
00:50:53,000 --> 00:50:54,633
OLD GUY'S STONED
ON BETA-BLOCKERS.

1111
00:50:54,667 --> 00:50:57,133
HE IS IMPOSING HIMSELF
BOTH ON LIARA, YOUR DAUGHTER,

1112
00:50:57,167 --> 00:50:59,300
AND THE MUTE GIRL, ZETHA.

1113
00:50:59,333 --> 00:51:01,000
NOW, THIS IS AN INSULT
TO LIARA--

1114
00:51:01,033 --> 00:51:02,833
YOU KNOW I LOVE HER--

1115
00:51:02,867 --> 00:51:05,167
AND A DIRECT INSULT TO ME.

1116
00:51:05,200 --> 00:51:07,833
- I AM ASKING-- RATHER--
- BLANDLY.

1117
00:51:07,867 --> 00:51:11,633
...I AM DEMANDING
YOUR PERMISSION
TO CHALLENGE HIM TO THE DUEL.

1118
00:51:11,667 --> 00:51:13,700
HEY, BETTY AND VERONICA.

1119
00:51:17,333 --> 00:51:20,167
THESE TWO ARE BOTHERING ME
WITH THEIR LADY THINGS.

1120
00:51:22,700 --> 00:51:24,667
YOU SENT FOR ME?

1121
00:51:24,700 --> 00:51:29,500
YES. I HAVE REPORTS ABOUT YOU
THAT ARE NOT GOOD--

1122
00:51:29,533 --> 00:51:31,333
THAT YOU'RE CAUSING
MUCH TROUBLE.

1123
00:51:31,367 --> 00:51:33,833
WHAT AM I SUPPOSED
TO HAVE DONE NOW?

1124
00:51:33,867 --> 00:51:36,300
YOU ARE FORCING YOUR ATTENTIONS
ON LIARA,

1125
00:51:36,333 --> 00:51:37,833
AND THEN ON THE MUTE GIRL,
ZETHA.

1126
00:51:37,867 --> 00:51:39,867
THAT'S NOT TRUE.
WHY DON'T YOU ASK THEM?

1127
00:51:39,900 --> 00:51:41,667
- HE LIES!
- SILENCE.

1128
00:51:41,700 --> 00:51:43,500
- I'M THE ONE
IN THE VELVET DRESS.
- IS IT TRUE?

1129
00:51:43,533 --> 00:51:47,533
HAS HE FORCED HIMSELF
OR HIS ATTENTIONS UPON YOU?

1130
00:51:47,567 --> 00:51:49,667
[MIKE]
THAT MEANS "YES, OH, YES,
PLEASE HELP ME."

1131
00:51:49,700 --> 00:51:51,300
WHY WOULD SHE ADMIT IT?

1132
00:51:51,333 --> 00:51:53,333
PERHAPS SHE'S AFRAID OF HIM.

1133
00:51:53,367 --> 00:51:55,867
BEING MUTE,
SHE'S UNABLE TO DEFEND HERSELF.

1134
00:51:55,900 --> 00:51:57,633
[VOICE SIMILAR TO HENRY FONDA'S]
MAYBE SHE'S PROTECTING ME.

1135
00:51:57,667 --> 00:51:59,367
HENRY FONDA.

1136
00:51:59,400 --> 00:52:01,667
LISTEN, I'M NOT GONNA
BE PUT ON TRIAL OR QUESTIONED

1137
00:52:01,700 --> 00:52:04,467
BY YOU OR ANYONE ELSE
FOR SOMETHING I HAVEN'T DONE.

1138
00:52:04,500 --> 00:52:06,700
YOU KNOW, BUDDY,
I DON'T LIKE YOU.

1139
00:52:06,733 --> 00:52:09,133
MAYBE IT'S A CARRYOVER
FROM EARTH AND NOT GOOD TASTE,

1140
00:52:09,167 --> 00:52:10,700
BUT I'D LIKE TO HANG ONE ON YOU.

1141
00:52:10,733 --> 00:52:13,467
- CHAPMAN--
- WOULD YOU HANG ONE ON ME?

1142
00:52:13,500 --> 00:52:17,033
...HERRON HAS CHALLENGED YOU
TO THE DUEL OF RHETON.

1143
00:52:17,067 --> 00:52:19,300
DO YOU ACCEPT HIS CHALLENGE?

1144
00:52:19,333 --> 00:52:22,833
A DUEL FOR WHAT?
WHAT KIND OF A DUEL?

1145
00:52:22,867 --> 00:52:25,000
THIS GUY DOESN'T LOOK
VERY HONEST TO ME.

1146
00:52:25,033 --> 00:52:27,800
A DUEL OF BRAVERY.

1147
00:52:27,833 --> 00:52:29,800
YEAH. FINE, LIARA.
ANYWAY--

1148
00:52:29,833 --> 00:52:31,967
YOU KNOW, MR. SESSOM,

1149
00:52:32,000 --> 00:52:34,300
MAYBE THIS DUEL BUSINESS
IS A GOOD IDEA.

1150
00:52:34,333 --> 00:52:36,500
- MIGHT CLEAR THE AIR A LITTLE.
- LACQUER HAIR.

1151
00:52:36,533 --> 00:52:38,967
SO HOW DO WE GO ABOUT IT?

1152
00:52:39,000 --> 00:52:41,800
LATER, THEY WENT ABOUT IT.

1153
00:52:41,833 --> 00:52:44,667
UH, YOU DIDN'T NEED
TO TAKE YOUR SHIRTS OFF.

1154
00:52:44,700 --> 00:52:46,867
- HERRON--
- YOU'RE A BLUE WATERFOWL.

1155
00:52:46,900 --> 00:52:49,800
...YOU KNOW THE RULES
FOR THE DUEL OF RHETON.

1156
00:52:49,833 --> 00:52:51,800
BUT FOR HIM,
I'LL HAVE TO EXPLAIN

1157
00:52:51,833 --> 00:52:53,800
AND SHOW THE RESULTS.

1158
00:52:53,833 --> 00:52:55,500
CHAPMAN, COME HERE.

1159
00:52:55,533 --> 00:52:59,633
HE'S SHOWING OFF
HIS RAY BOLGER PHYSIQUE.

1160
00:52:59,667 --> 00:53:02,333
THOSE ARE GRAVITY PLATES
THAT WE'VE HAD PLACED HERE.

1161
00:53:02,367 --> 00:53:04,300
THEIR INTENSITY IS SO HIGH

1162
00:53:04,333 --> 00:53:06,800
THAT ANY OBJECT
OR ANY PERSON

1163
00:53:06,833 --> 00:53:09,033
PLACED ON ANY ONE OF THEM

1164
00:53:09,067 --> 00:53:11,133
WOULD IMMEDIATELY DISINTEGRATE.

1165
00:53:11,167 --> 00:53:12,800
KIND OF A DUMB PURCHASE, REALLY.

1166
00:53:12,833 --> 00:53:15,667
- HERE. LET ME SHOW YOU.
- LET ME JUST DRY
MY HANDS FIRST.

1167
00:53:15,700 --> 00:53:17,400
[WHIRRING]

1168
00:53:19,200 --> 00:53:21,467
THIS IS A MEAT LOAF
WE JUST MADE.

1169
00:53:21,500 --> 00:53:22,667
[WHIRRING CONTINUES]

1170
00:53:22,700 --> 00:53:25,700
THE AUDIENCE IS HEMORRHAGING.

1171
00:53:25,733 --> 00:53:28,000
[MOCK GASPING]

1172
00:53:28,033 --> 00:53:31,533
THE LINOLEUM TILE OF DOOM!

1173
00:53:31,567 --> 00:53:33,467
[SCOFFS]
SO? MY DAD HAS ONE OF THOSE.

1174
00:53:33,500 --> 00:53:36,867
THE DUEL OF RHETON
IS ONE OF PHYSICAL STRENGTH

1175
00:53:36,900 --> 00:53:39,000
AND SKILL.

1176
00:53:39,033 --> 00:53:41,833
- YOU WILL USE THIS ROD--
- THE ROD, PLEASE.

1177
00:53:41,867 --> 00:53:44,200
...AND ATTEMPT
TO PUSH YOUR OPPONENT

1178
00:53:44,233 --> 00:53:47,300
ON TOP OF ONE OF
THE GRAVITY PLATES.

1179
00:53:47,333 --> 00:53:49,300
YOU SAW WHAT HAPPENED
TO THE ROCK.

1180
00:53:49,333 --> 00:53:51,333
[IMITATING SEAN CONNERY]
I STARRED IN IT
WITH NICHOLAS CAGE.

1181
00:53:51,367 --> 00:53:53,967
SUCK IT IN, TINY.

1182
00:53:54,000 --> 00:53:55,533
GET READY.

1183
00:53:55,567 --> 00:53:59,233
WHAT I'M SAYING IS,
LET'S GET READY TO RUMBLE!

1184
00:54:01,333 --> 00:54:03,533
PUT THE COMBAT ROD
IN POSITION.

1185
00:54:03,567 --> 00:54:06,033
GEEZ! THE OLD GUY
CALLS IT HIS "COMBAT ROD"?

1186
00:54:06,067 --> 00:54:08,033
- I CAN'T BELIEVE IT.
IT'S DISGUSTING.
- NO.

1187
00:54:08,067 --> 00:54:09,667
- [MIKE MUTTERING]
- OH, WAIT.

1188
00:54:09,700 --> 00:54:11,867
- IS THAT WHAT
HE'S TALKING ABOUT?
- MAYBE NOT.

1189
00:54:15,167 --> 00:54:17,467
YOU ALSO HAVE TO FIGHT
AROUND OUR BIKE RACK.

1190
00:54:17,500 --> 00:54:19,800
THEY STOLE THAT
FROM AL PACINO'S FOOTBALL FIELD.

1191
00:54:19,833 --> 00:54:21,000
[CHUCKLES]

1192
00:54:23,367 --> 00:54:27,133
UH, WE'RE JUST GONNA
POUR SOME CONCRETE
WHILE YOU'RE FIGHTING.

1193
00:54:27,167 --> 00:54:30,800
WANNA JUST
INDIAN WRESTLE INSTEAD?

1194
00:54:30,833 --> 00:54:32,867
YOU KNOW IN A FEW MINUTES,
THEY'LL BE THE BEST OF FRIENDS,

1195
00:54:32,900 --> 00:54:36,300
SLUGGING BACK TRANYA.

1196
00:54:36,333 --> 00:54:38,533
THEY REALLY GOTTA COOPERATE
TO KILL EACH OTHER.

1197
00:54:38,567 --> 00:54:39,800
[CHUCKLES]

1198
00:54:39,833 --> 00:54:41,167
TIME! GOOD MATCH.

1199
00:54:41,200 --> 00:54:43,233
AT MY SIGNAL,
YOU WILL START THE DUEL.

1200
00:54:45,700 --> 00:54:47,967
THERE CAN BE NO QUARTER CALLED
AND NO QUARTER GIVEN.

1201
00:54:48,000 --> 00:54:49,467
WE NEED THEM FOR THE LAUNDRY.

1202
00:54:49,500 --> 00:54:51,300
- THE FATE OF THE VICTIM--
- [WHISPERS] SORRY.

1203
00:54:51,333 --> 00:54:53,300
...IS IN THE HANDS
OF THE VICTOR.

1204
00:54:53,333 --> 00:54:55,867
THE MOMENT HAS COME.

1205
00:54:55,900 --> 00:54:59,667
AT MY LIGHT SIGNAL,
YOU WILL PROCEED.

1206
00:54:59,700 --> 00:55:01,167
- [BEEPING]
- UH, WAS THAT THE SIGNAL?

1207
00:55:01,200 --> 00:55:03,000
IT WAS KIND OF DIM.

1208
00:55:04,567 --> 00:55:05,967
- PUSH.
- PUSH.

1209
00:55:06,000 --> 00:55:06,967
HEY, BOYS.

1210
00:55:07,000 --> 00:55:08,533
[ALL]
PUUUSH!

1211
00:55:08,567 --> 00:55:10,667
- PUSH.
- PUSH.

1212
00:55:10,700 --> 00:55:15,133
YEAH, THIS'LL BE ON T.V.
IF THEY EVER HAVE ESPN 6.

1213
00:55:15,167 --> 00:55:17,967
YOU CAN STILL SEE COMBAT ROD
FIGHTS IN MEXICO CITY.

1214
00:55:18,000 --> 00:55:20,167
HUH?

1215
00:55:22,833 --> 00:55:25,033
AND NOW, FLOOD THE ARENA.
DID WE TELL YOU ABOUT THAT?

1216
00:55:27,333 --> 00:55:29,533
YOU KNOW, COMBAT ROD
USED TO BE GREAT.

1217
00:55:29,567 --> 00:55:31,300
NOW THERE'S JUST
TOO MUCH MONEY IN IT.

1218
00:55:31,333 --> 00:55:32,467
- YEAH, IT'S JUST
A BUSINESS NOW.
- YEAH.

1219
00:55:32,500 --> 00:55:34,000
TOO BAD.

1220
00:55:35,667 --> 00:55:37,033
[MEN GRUNTING]

1221
00:55:37,067 --> 00:55:38,200
♪♪ [HUMMING "CHARGE" FANFARE]

1222
00:55:38,233 --> 00:55:39,867
PUSH HIM ON THE GRAVITY PLATE!

1223
00:55:39,900 --> 00:55:41,033
♪♪ [HUMMING "CHARGE" FANFARE]

1224
00:55:41,067 --> 00:55:43,967
PUSH HIM ON THE GRAVITY PLATE!

1225
00:55:44,000 --> 00:55:45,700
- [WOMEN SHOUTING] KILL HIM!
- EARLY CHEESEHEADS.

1226
00:55:45,733 --> 00:55:49,300
[SHOUTING CONTINUES]

1227
00:55:49,333 --> 00:55:51,633
I'M SHIRTLESS,
AND IT'S DRIVING THEM MAD.

1228
00:55:51,667 --> 00:55:54,000
ICE THE PIG.

1229
00:55:59,833 --> 00:56:01,867
- THERE, THERE.
- [CHUCKLES]

1230
00:56:03,667 --> 00:56:06,633
- I DON'T WANNA KILL YOU.
- SO CAN YOU DO IT?

1231
00:56:06,667 --> 00:56:09,533
- I NEVER DID.
- EXCEPT THAT TIME YOU ATE
THE LAST SYNTHESIZED BREADFRUIT.

1232
00:56:09,567 --> 00:56:12,500
THAT REALLY CHEESED ME OFF.

1233
00:56:12,533 --> 00:56:14,867
THE TOTALS ON THE BOARD
ARE CORRECT-RECT-RECT.

1234
00:56:14,900 --> 00:56:16,867
THANK YOU FOR ATTENDING
PLATE AND SKIRT DAY

1235
00:56:16,900 --> 00:56:19,067
HERE AT COMBAT ROD PARK,
PARK, PARK.

1236
00:56:20,867 --> 00:56:23,367
YOU'RE GONNA PUT
YOUR SHIRT BACK ON. YAY!

1237
00:56:23,400 --> 00:56:25,633
HEY, GIRLS, YOU WANNA MAKE
A ME SANDWICH?

1238
00:56:25,667 --> 00:56:27,000
HUH?

1239
00:56:29,533 --> 00:56:30,967
WOW.
[MUTTERS]

1240
00:56:31,000 --> 00:56:32,800
ADD THAT TO THE KAMA SUTRA.

1241
00:56:32,833 --> 00:56:35,633
NEITHER ONE OF THEM
ARE TOUCHING THE GROUND.
HOLY COW.

1242
00:56:35,667 --> 00:56:38,333
WELL, LET ME SHOW YOU
THE CHINA PATTERN
I REGISTERED FOR.

1243
00:56:38,367 --> 00:56:40,633
AND YOU'RE GONNA LOVE
THE KITCHEN BORDER I PICKED OUT.

1244
00:56:40,667 --> 00:56:42,633
WHY DIDN'T YOU KILL HIM?

1245
00:56:42,667 --> 00:56:45,833
I DIDN'T WANT TO.
I DON'T BELIEVE IN IT.

1246
00:56:45,867 --> 00:56:48,000
IN THIS CASE, KILLING HIM
WOULD'VE ACCOMPLISHED NOTHING.

1247
00:56:48,033 --> 00:56:50,300
BUT HERRON WOULDN'T HAVE
SHOWN YOU MERCY.

1248
00:56:50,333 --> 00:56:53,467
HE'D HAVE KILLED YOU
BECAUSE HE WANTS ME.

1249
00:56:53,500 --> 00:56:56,700
BUT I DON'T LOVE HIM.
I LOVE YOU.

1250
00:56:56,733 --> 00:56:59,167
IF YOU'D FELT ANYTHING
FOR EITHER ONE OF US,

1251
00:56:59,200 --> 00:57:01,467
YOU COULD'VE STOPPED THIS DUEL.

1252
00:57:01,500 --> 00:57:03,467
- WHAT?
- YOU KNOW WHAT I THINK?

1253
00:57:03,500 --> 00:57:05,967
I THINK YOU WERE WAITING TO SEE
WHICH ONE OF US WON,

1254
00:57:06,000 --> 00:57:07,967
AND THEN TAKE THE ONE
THAT WAS LEFT OVER.

1255
00:57:08,000 --> 00:57:09,800
NO, LIARA, I DON'T LOVE YOU.

1256
00:57:09,833 --> 00:57:11,367
I DON'T EVEN KNOW
IF I LIKE YOU.

1257
00:57:11,400 --> 00:57:12,867
YOU GET ME GOING
AND ALL, BUT--

1258
00:57:12,900 --> 00:57:14,700
LET ME TELL YOU THIS.

1259
00:57:14,733 --> 00:57:17,633
YOU CAN'T MAKE SOMEONE LOVE YOU.

1260
00:57:17,667 --> 00:57:19,467
IT'S GOT TO COME NATURALLY.

1261
00:57:19,500 --> 00:57:21,133
YOU CAN'T FORCE IT,
YOU CAN'T COMMAND IT.

1262
00:57:21,167 --> 00:57:22,700
THAT'S WHAT THE JUDGE TOLD ME.

1263
00:57:22,733 --> 00:57:24,200
IF YOU DO THAT,
YOU'LL NEVER FIND IT.

1264
00:57:24,233 --> 00:57:26,200
CHICKEN DROPPINGS FOR THE SOUL.

1265
00:57:26,233 --> 00:57:29,000
THIS WHOLE THING
IS LIKE A NIGHTMARE TO ME.

1266
00:57:29,033 --> 00:57:33,367
I MISS MY PEOPLE.
I'VE GOT TO MAKE SOME ATTEMPT
TO GET BACK.

1267
00:57:33,400 --> 00:57:35,967
AND IF YOU FEEL ANYTHING FOR ME,
YOU'LL TRY TO HELP ME.

1268
00:57:36,000 --> 00:57:38,133
I FEEL INDIFFERENCE
TINGED WITH DISGUST.

1269
00:57:38,167 --> 00:57:39,633
WELL, PERHAPS YOU'RE RIGHT.

1270
00:57:39,667 --> 00:57:42,633
YOU ARE CORRECT, STRANGE-FACED
LILLIPUTIAN ASTRO BOY.

1271
00:57:42,667 --> 00:57:44,633
[CHUCKLES]

1272
00:57:44,667 --> 00:57:46,700
MAYBE I CAN HELP YOU.

1273
00:57:46,733 --> 00:57:48,700
TRUST ME COMPLETELY.

1274
00:57:48,733 --> 00:57:51,067
[MOCK SINISTER LAUGHTER]

1275
00:57:52,500 --> 00:57:55,033
[LAUGHTER CONTINUES]

1276
00:57:55,067 --> 00:57:56,667
OKAY, NOW.

1277
00:57:56,700 --> 00:57:58,333
WELL, THAT WENT REALLY WELL.

1278
00:57:58,367 --> 00:58:00,533
I THINK.

1279
00:58:00,567 --> 00:58:03,367
SMELL THIS. DOES IT SMELL
KIND OF FISHY TO YOU?

1280
00:58:06,167 --> 00:58:08,167
HEY, DID YOU USE THIS
TO SHAVE YOUR LEGS?

1281
00:58:08,200 --> 00:58:11,000
[CHUCKLES]

1282
00:58:11,033 --> 00:58:13,367
AS YOU SAID,
I DON'T WANNA KILL YOU.

1283
00:58:13,400 --> 00:58:17,033
JUST THOUGHT I'D WAKE YOU UP
AND TELL YOU THAT. 'NIGHT.

1284
00:58:17,067 --> 00:58:19,800
YOU KNOW,
I THINK I COULD UNDERSTAND
YOUR SOMEWHAT QUAINT LANGUAGE

1285
00:58:19,833 --> 00:58:21,700
IF I WERE ON YOUR EARTH
A LITTLE.

1286
00:58:21,733 --> 00:58:24,000
- WHY DON'T YOU KILL ME?
- I'M A LOSER, BABY.

1287
00:58:24,033 --> 00:58:26,133
YOU DIDN'T KILL ME,
AND YOU HAD THE CHANCE.

1288
00:58:26,167 --> 00:58:27,967
WHAT ABOUT THE KNIFE?

1289
00:58:28,000 --> 00:58:31,167
THIS ISN'T EXACTLY
WHAT I'D CALL A FRIENDLY VISIT.

1290
00:58:31,200 --> 00:58:32,633
OW, OW, OW.

1291
00:58:32,667 --> 00:58:34,633
IS THIS A SCENE
BETWEEN TWO CEMENT BLOCKS?

1292
00:58:34,667 --> 00:58:35,967
OH, NO. THEY'RE HUMAN,
AREN'T THEY?

1293
00:58:36,000 --> 00:58:38,133
IF YOU HELP ME,

1294
00:58:38,167 --> 00:58:40,800
I HAVE A PLAN WHERE I MIGHT
HELP YOU TO LEAVE OUR PLANET.

1295
00:58:40,833 --> 00:58:42,700
PERHAPS IT WILL WORK.

1296
00:58:42,733 --> 00:58:45,633
I DON'T SEE
HOW THIS IS POSSIBLE.
WHAT ABOUT MY SIZE?

1297
00:58:45,667 --> 00:58:48,000
YOU CAN BE
A BOWLING TROPHY MODEL.

1298
00:58:48,033 --> 00:58:50,667
I INSPECTED YOUR GIANT SUIT,

1299
00:58:50,700 --> 00:58:53,467
AND THE OXYGEN TANK HOLDS AIR
FROM YOUR OWN WORLD.

1300
00:58:53,500 --> 00:58:55,300
- ISN'T THAT RIGHT?
- YES, OF COURSE. BUT--

1301
00:58:55,333 --> 00:58:57,167
NO. NEVER MIND THAT.
THAT'S NOT IMPORTANT.

1302
00:58:57,200 --> 00:58:59,000
DON'T TROUBLE YOUR ODD-SHAPED
LITTLE HEAD ABOUT IT.

1303
00:58:59,033 --> 00:59:01,833
YOU SEE, THE WHOLE PLAN
IS BASED ON A THEORY

1304
00:59:01,867 --> 00:59:04,633
THAT YOUR PEOPLE
ARE SEARCHING FOR YOU.

1305
00:59:04,667 --> 00:59:07,633
NOW, I MUST GET YOU BACK
BEFORE THEY ATTEMPT
TO FIND YOU HERE.

1306
00:59:07,667 --> 00:59:10,333
I KNOW THEY'VE BEEN SEARCHING
AND WILL EVENTUALLY
ZERO IN ON THIS PLANET.

1307
00:59:10,367 --> 00:59:12,633
JUST KEEP TELLING
YOURSELF THAT, YOU DOPE.

1308
00:59:12,667 --> 00:59:14,967
I THINK I CAN
GET YOU BACK IN TIME.

1309
00:59:15,000 --> 00:59:18,633
- YES, BUT, UH--
- LOOK, DO YOU WANNA
HOP IN WITH ME HERE?

1310
00:59:18,667 --> 00:59:22,300
YOU'RE DOING THIS
BECAUSE OF LIARA, AREN'T YOU?

1311
00:59:22,333 --> 00:59:24,500
YES, I AM.
I'M IN LOVE WITH HER.

1312
00:59:24,533 --> 00:59:27,300
I SHOW IT BY STALKING HER DAILY.

1313
00:59:27,333 --> 00:59:29,500
I DON'T THINK
SHE LOVES ME YET,

1314
00:59:29,533 --> 00:59:31,500
BUT PERHAPS WITH YOU GONE,

1315
00:59:31,533 --> 00:59:34,467
SHE WILL SEE THINGS IN A MORE
REALISTIC LIGHT IN TIME.

1316
00:59:34,500 --> 00:59:37,033
WELL, HOW CAN WE GET MY SUIT
INTO THE OPEN?

1317
00:59:37,067 --> 00:59:38,967
I HAVE SOME MEN I CAN TRUST.

1318
00:59:39,000 --> 00:59:40,633
- AND SESSOM?
- NO.

1319
00:59:40,667 --> 00:59:42,500
THIS MOVIE IS A FILIBUSTER!

1320
00:59:42,533 --> 00:59:44,467
HE MUST NEVER KNOW,

1321
00:59:44,500 --> 00:59:46,833
OTHERWISE WE BOTH
WILL BE PUT TO DEATH.

1322
00:59:53,333 --> 00:59:55,633
TWO NIGHTS A WEEK,
I'M ALONE

1323
00:59:55,667 --> 00:59:58,133
AND IN COMPLETE CHARGE
OF THE MASTER CONTROL CENTER.

1324
00:59:58,167 --> 00:59:59,700
- CAN ONE MAN HANDLE IT?
- YEAH.

1325
00:59:59,733 --> 01:00:02,200
- THEN WHY DON'T YOU DO IT?
- AND ON ONE OF THOSE NIGHTS

1326
01:00:02,233 --> 01:00:04,800
IN THE NEAR FUTURE
WHILE SESSOM IS SLEEPING,

1327
01:00:04,833 --> 01:00:08,033
I WILL MANEUVER RHETON
WITHIN A DISTANCE
OF YOUR EARTH'S MOON.

1328
01:00:08,067 --> 01:00:09,700
DO YOU THINK
THEY'LL BE ABLE TO SEE US?

1329
01:00:09,733 --> 01:00:11,333
PRECISELY.

1330
01:00:11,367 --> 01:00:13,367
THEY WILL INVESTIGATE
AND FIND YOU.

1331
01:00:13,400 --> 01:00:15,300
[HIGH-PITCHED, SUSTAINED TONE
ALARM SOUNDING]

1332
01:00:15,333 --> 01:00:18,033
OH, NO!
MY PET CICADA'S IN TROUBLE!

1333
01:00:18,067 --> 01:00:20,967
OH, MAN!
KENNY G'S AT IT AGAIN!

1334
01:00:21,000 --> 01:00:22,967
[ALARM CONTINUES]

1335
01:00:23,000 --> 01:00:24,667
GO WITH HER.

1336
01:00:24,700 --> 01:00:26,133
GO WITH WHO? WHAT?
WHAT DO YOU--

1337
01:00:26,167 --> 01:00:27,533
OH, WITH HER. OKAY.

1338
01:00:27,567 --> 01:00:30,300
[ALARM CONTINUES]

1339
01:00:30,333 --> 01:00:33,000
- WHAT IS THIS?
- OUR NETWORK IS DOWN.

1340
01:00:33,033 --> 01:00:34,833
WHAT'S HAPPENING?

1341
01:00:34,867 --> 01:00:37,033
THE SIREN MEANS
WE'RE BEING ATTACKED.

1342
01:00:37,067 --> 01:00:38,833
- ATTACKED BY WHOM?
- I'M NOT SAYING.

1343
01:00:38,867 --> 01:00:41,000
YOU'RE MEAN TO ME.

1344
01:00:41,033 --> 01:00:43,000
ATTACKED BY WHOM?

1345
01:00:43,033 --> 01:00:44,967
- THE SOLARITES.
- DUH!

1346
01:00:45,000 --> 01:00:47,133
WE'VE BEEN HERE TOO LONG.
THEY'VE DISCOVERED OUR POSITION.

1347
01:00:47,167 --> 01:00:50,133
- WHO ARE THE SOLARITES?
- I'VE NO TIME TO EXPLAIN.

1348
01:00:50,167 --> 01:00:52,300
- I MUST HELP SESSOM.
- GO BACK TO BED, CHAPMAN.

1349
01:00:52,333 --> 01:00:54,500
I'LL WAKE YOU
IF ANYTHING HAPPENS.

1350
01:00:54,533 --> 01:00:57,667
- WHAT WILL THIS DO
TO OUR PLANS?
- SHOULD I CALL THE SITTER?

1351
01:00:57,700 --> 01:01:00,167
WE MUST FIGHT THIS OFF,
OR NO ONE WILL HAVE ANY PLANS.

1352
01:01:00,200 --> 01:01:02,467
IS EVERYONE UNDERGROUND?

1353
01:01:02,500 --> 01:01:04,700
- YES.
- THEN WE GO.

1354
01:01:04,733 --> 01:01:06,533
[IMITATING SESSOM]
AND DON'T TALK ABOUT
YOUR SECRET PLANS

1355
01:01:06,567 --> 01:01:08,500
IN FRONT OF ME.

1356
01:01:10,667 --> 01:01:12,533
RELEASE THE HUSH PUPPY.

1357
01:01:15,500 --> 01:01:17,033
[GASPS]
HEMORRHOIDS!

1358
01:01:17,067 --> 01:01:20,000
GET THE TUCKS!

1359
01:01:20,033 --> 01:01:22,167
HE'S KOOL MOE GRANDPA.

1360
01:01:25,033 --> 01:01:27,200
OH, THAT HELPED.

1361
01:01:27,233 --> 01:01:29,633
- WE'RE SAFE FOR THE MOMENT.
- HEIL HITLER.

1362
01:01:29,667 --> 01:01:32,667
I FEAR THEY WON'T GIVE UP
SO EASILY.

1363
01:01:32,700 --> 01:01:34,667
SAFE FOR THE MOMENT?

1364
01:01:34,700 --> 01:01:37,300
WELL, WHO ARE
THESE SOLARITES ANYHOW?

1365
01:01:37,333 --> 01:01:39,500
- THEY ARE FROM A SUN SATELLITE.
- OH.

1366
01:01:39,533 --> 01:01:41,167
AND FOR GENERATIONS,
THEY'VE BEEN AFTER

1367
01:01:41,200 --> 01:01:43,867
OUR UNIVERSAL
GRAVITY CONTROL,

1368
01:01:43,900 --> 01:01:46,167
'CAUSE THEY WANT TO AVOID
BEING PULLED INTO THE SUN.

1369
01:01:46,200 --> 01:01:48,333
IF WE DON'T STOP THEM,

1370
01:01:48,367 --> 01:01:50,833
THEY'LL EVENTUALLY
ATTACK YOUR EARTH.

1371
01:01:50,867 --> 01:01:52,800
THEN LET'S SEE YOU LAUGH.

1372
01:01:52,833 --> 01:01:54,867
LIARA, SHOW HIM THE PRISONER.

1373
01:01:54,900 --> 01:01:56,467
- [CHAPMAN] PRISONER?
- COME.

1374
01:01:56,500 --> 01:01:58,467
WE'VE GOT ALL THE EPISODES
ON TAPE.

1375
01:01:58,500 --> 01:02:00,833
IT'S A GREAT SHOW.

1376
01:02:00,867 --> 01:02:02,967
THEY'RE JUST TAKING HIM
OFF TO DAYCARE

1377
01:02:03,000 --> 01:02:05,200
WHILE THEY STRAIGHTEN OUT
THEIR LITTLE WAR.

1378
01:02:07,167 --> 01:02:09,333
THE BEATLES ARE PLAYING
HERE TONIGHT.

1379
01:02:12,333 --> 01:02:15,000
- [IMITATING DOG WHINING]
- AW, PUPPY. AW.

1380
01:02:15,033 --> 01:02:17,633
[IMITATING DOG PANTING]

1381
01:02:17,667 --> 01:02:19,867
SO THAT'S A SOLARITE.

1382
01:02:19,900 --> 01:02:23,300
- YES. HE WAS CAPTURED
DURING THE LAST WAR.
- [IMITATING DOG WHINING]

1383
01:02:23,333 --> 01:02:26,667
THE ONLY ONE OF THEIR MONSTERS
THAT DIDN'T DIE IN THE ATTACK.

1384
01:02:26,700 --> 01:02:28,967
- WHEN DID THIS ATTACK
TAKE PLACE?
- SEVERAL YEARS AGO,

1385
01:02:29,000 --> 01:02:31,133
WHEN ZETHA WAS A LITTLE GIRL.

1386
01:02:31,167 --> 01:02:33,133
- THAT'S WHEN
SHE LOST HER VOICE.
- [GROWLS]

1387
01:02:33,167 --> 01:02:35,533
WHOO-HOO! YEAH!

1388
01:02:35,567 --> 01:02:37,533
WHAT MAKES
THOSE ROCKS DISINTEGRATE?

1389
01:02:37,567 --> 01:02:40,467
- [CRASHING SOUND]
- [SCOFFS] WEENIE.

1390
01:02:40,500 --> 01:02:42,467
[CHAPMAN]
IT'S AS IF THEY WERE HITTING
SOME INVISIBLE WALL.

1391
01:02:42,500 --> 01:02:45,033
THAT'S EXACTLY WHAT IT IS.

1392
01:02:45,067 --> 01:02:47,300
- THE MONSTER IS SO STRONG
- [WHOOPS]

1393
01:02:47,333 --> 01:02:49,300
THAT IT WOULD SMASH
ANY ORDINARY STRUCTURE.

1394
01:02:49,333 --> 01:02:51,700
AND WHAT YOU CALL
AN INVISIBLE WALL

1395
01:02:51,733 --> 01:02:55,167
IS REALLY ANOTHER WAY THAT WE
USE OUR GRAVITATIONAL CONTROL.

1396
01:02:55,200 --> 01:02:58,333
NOW, BY USING
A HIGH MAGNETIC FIELD,

1397
01:02:58,367 --> 01:03:00,967
WE CAN LOCK MOLECULES
SO CLOSELY TOGETHER

1398
01:03:01,000 --> 01:03:02,633
THAT THEY FORM A SOLID WALL.

1399
01:03:02,667 --> 01:03:03,967
WHATEVER. IT'S FINE.
[WHOOPS]

1400
01:03:04,000 --> 01:03:06,967
- A BIG HIT AT M.I.T.
- WHERE?

1401
01:03:07,000 --> 01:03:09,367
ONE OF EARTH'S MORE ADVANCED
CENTERS OF LEARNING.

1402
01:03:09,400 --> 01:03:11,467
A LOT OF POCKETED,
SHORT-SLEEVED SHIRTS.

1403
01:03:11,500 --> 01:03:15,667
I ONLY HOPE YOUR WALL
WILL HOLD HIM IN CHECK.

1404
01:03:15,700 --> 01:03:19,033
[LIARA]
YES. HE COULD KILL US ALL
IF HE ESCAPED.

1405
01:03:19,067 --> 01:03:21,033
- [IMITATING DOG WHINING]
- LIFE ON OTHER PLANETS...

1406
01:03:21,067 --> 01:03:22,667
[SCOFFS]
WHAT A CROCK!

1407
01:03:22,700 --> 01:03:24,467
AND WE WERE ALWAYS WONDERING
IF OURS

1408
01:03:24,500 --> 01:03:26,833
WAS THE ONLY ONE SO BLESSED.

1409
01:03:26,867 --> 01:03:29,200
THERE ARE MANY INHABITED WORLDS,

1410
01:03:29,233 --> 01:03:32,000
BUT ONLY THESE FIRE PEOPLE
BOTHER US.

1411
01:03:32,033 --> 01:03:35,500
WE JUST NEED A PLACE TO SCOOT.

1412
01:03:35,533 --> 01:03:37,500
HE'S JUST A SHAR-PEI
WITH A PARTED AFRO,

1413
01:03:37,533 --> 01:03:39,033
WEARING A PIZZA SLICER.

1414
01:03:41,233 --> 01:03:43,467
[MAN ON RADIO]
WE HAVE BEEN SIGHTED
BY THE ENEMY.

1415
01:03:43,500 --> 01:03:45,467
WE ARE FORMING
A CONCENTRATED ATTACK.

1416
01:03:45,500 --> 01:03:48,167
PATTERN 6, VERNIER INDEX 1-2.

1417
01:03:48,200 --> 01:03:49,633
PATTERN 6?

1418
01:03:49,667 --> 01:03:52,200
WE NEVER ATTACKED
ON THAT ONE BEFORE.

1419
01:03:52,233 --> 01:03:54,900
THEY'RE HURLING
FLAMING MILK-BONES AT THEM.

1420
01:03:57,400 --> 01:03:59,200
WHAT ARE WE GOING TO DO?

1421
01:03:59,233 --> 01:04:01,000
WE MUST TRY TO BREAK UP
THE ATTACK.

1422
01:04:01,033 --> 01:04:03,467
[SCOFFS]
THANKS, PATTON.

1423
01:04:03,500 --> 01:04:06,500
I DOUBT THE AUDIENCE WOULD ENJOY
LOOKING AT A LUMP.

1424
01:04:06,533 --> 01:04:08,167
[CHUCKLING]

1425
01:04:08,200 --> 01:04:11,967
THE WORST THEY'LL EVER DO
IS HUMP THEIR LEGS.

1426
01:04:12,000 --> 01:04:14,467
OH, MY ENGINE LIGHT IS ON.
I WONDER WHY.

1427
01:04:14,500 --> 01:04:16,833
[SOLARITE ROARING]

1428
01:04:16,867 --> 01:04:19,700
THEY ATTACK
IN FLAMING PET TAXIS.

1429
01:04:19,733 --> 01:04:21,833
[IMITATING SESSOM]
OH, I JUST FLOATED
AN AIR BISCUIT.

1430
01:04:21,867 --> 01:04:23,700
I'M OUT OF HERE.

1431
01:04:28,033 --> 01:04:30,800
- [CHANTS IN LATIN]
- [EQUIPMENT WHIRRING]

1432
01:04:30,833 --> 01:04:33,167
[IMITATING DOGS BARKING]

1433
01:04:35,500 --> 01:04:37,633
WELL, MAYBE IF THEY DIDN'T
DISGUISE THE PLANET

1434
01:04:37,667 --> 01:04:41,300
AS A CHICKEN McNUGGET,
THE DOGS WOULDN'T ATTACK IT.

1435
01:04:41,333 --> 01:04:43,167
[IMITATING GOOFY]
DON'T BE AFRAID.
WE ALL HAVE OUR SHOTS.

1436
01:04:43,200 --> 01:04:44,633
[GUFFAWS]

1437
01:04:44,667 --> 01:04:46,533
WHERE'S A FIRE EXTINGUISHER
ON THIS THING?

1438
01:04:49,233 --> 01:04:51,533
IT'S FANTASTIC.

1439
01:04:51,567 --> 01:04:53,333
WE CAN DO ONE OF TWO THINGS.

1440
01:04:53,367 --> 01:04:55,633
- SCREAM OR RUN.
- OUTRUN THEM OR FIGHT THEM.

1441
01:04:55,667 --> 01:04:57,967
BREAKING UP A FORMATION
IS ONE THING,

1442
01:04:58,000 --> 01:04:59,800
BUT HOW CAN YOU FIGHT THEM?

1443
01:04:59,833 --> 01:05:02,000
- DO YOU HAVE A CHANCE?
- WE HAVE TO SETTLE THAT

1444
01:05:02,033 --> 01:05:03,633
ONCE AND FOR ALL.

1445
01:05:03,667 --> 01:05:06,633
LIVING IN CONSTANT DANGER
ISN'T WORTHY OF US.

1446
01:05:06,667 --> 01:05:10,167
DON'T FORGET-- WE STILL HAVE
THE GRAVITY CONTROL.

1447
01:05:10,200 --> 01:05:14,000
THE GREATEST DANGER TO US
IS THE HIGH-INTENSITY HEAT BOMB.

1448
01:05:14,033 --> 01:05:15,533
- HE'S RIGHT.
- YEAH.

1449
01:05:15,567 --> 01:05:17,300
THEY HAVE ENOUGH
CONCENTRATED HEAT

1450
01:05:17,333 --> 01:05:19,300
TO BLOW UP
OUR PLANET INSTANTLY.

1451
01:05:19,333 --> 01:05:22,133
- WHAT WOULD YOU DO?
- YOU MAKE THE CALL.

1452
01:05:22,167 --> 01:05:24,867
- I WOULD FIGHT.
- AND YOU?

1453
01:05:24,900 --> 01:05:27,833
- UM, PASS.
- FIGHT.

1454
01:05:27,867 --> 01:05:31,167
RIGHT. THAT'S EXACTLY
MY DECISION.

1455
01:05:41,867 --> 01:05:43,700
OKAY. NOT QUITE BUT ALMOST.

1456
01:05:43,733 --> 01:05:45,533
- LET'S TRY IT AGAIN, SHALL WE?
- YEAH. OKAY.

1457
01:05:45,567 --> 01:05:46,700
- OKAY, OKAY.
- [CLEARING THROAT]

1458
01:05:46,733 --> 01:05:48,033
OKAY, OKAY.

1459
01:05:48,067 --> 01:05:50,133
- ♪♪
- ♪ TWINK ♪

1460
01:05:50,167 --> 01:05:52,300
UM... OH, YEAH.

1461
01:05:52,333 --> 01:05:54,800
- ♪ EL ♪
- ♪♪

1462
01:05:54,833 --> 01:05:56,967
- ♪ TWINK ♪
- ♪♪

1463
01:05:57,000 --> 01:05:59,500
UH, YEAH, YEAH. UH...

1464
01:05:59,533 --> 01:06:02,367
- ♪ EL ♪
- ♪♪

1465
01:06:02,400 --> 01:06:04,500
- ♪ LIT ♪
- ♪♪

1466
01:06:04,533 --> 01:06:06,500
UH... MM...

1467
01:06:06,533 --> 01:06:08,633
- ♪ EL ♪
- ♪♪

1468
01:06:08,667 --> 01:06:10,300
- ♪ STAR ♪
- ♪♪ [HIGH-PITCHED TONE]

1469
01:06:10,333 --> 01:06:12,200
- WHOA! [MUTTERS]
- [LAUGHS]

1470
01:06:12,233 --> 01:06:13,800
BUT, STILL,
WE GOT SEVEN NOTES IN.

1471
01:06:13,833 --> 01:06:15,300
- THAT'S A NEW RECORD.
- THAT'S PRETTY GOOD.

1472
01:06:15,333 --> 01:06:17,033
- HEY, GUYS, WHAT'S UP?
- HEY, MIKE,

1473
01:06:17,067 --> 01:06:19,500
TOM AND I SAW THOSE LITTLE
GLASS ARRANGEMENT DOOHICKYS

1474
01:06:19,533 --> 01:06:21,500
THEY USE TO CONTROL GRAVITY
IN THE MOVIE.

1475
01:06:21,533 --> 01:06:23,833
- YEAH.
- AND WE REMEMBERED WE SHARED
A TRUE PASSION

1476
01:06:23,867 --> 01:06:25,800
FOR WATER GLASS RIM MUSIC.

1477
01:06:25,833 --> 01:06:28,833
- OKAY.
- AND WE'VE GOTTEN PRETTY
DARN GREAT AT IT TOO.

1478
01:06:28,867 --> 01:06:31,867
HEY, MIKE,
YOU WANNA GIVE IT A TRY?
IT SURE IS CHALLENGING.

1479
01:06:31,900 --> 01:06:33,633
NO, NO, NO.
I'D JUST EMBARRASS MYSELF.

1480
01:06:33,667 --> 01:06:35,333
- OH, GO ON.
- COME ON.

1481
01:06:35,367 --> 01:06:37,300
I MEAN, WE'VE PRACTICED AND ALL.
THAT'S WHY WE'RE GOOD.

1482
01:06:37,333 --> 01:06:39,200
BUT WE WON'T JUDGE YOU
TOO HARSHLY.

1483
01:06:39,233 --> 01:06:41,667
- YEAH.
- I-- OH, OKAY.

1484
01:06:41,700 --> 01:06:43,967
- IF YOU PUT IT THAT WAY,
I'LL GIVE IT A SHOT.
- OKAY.

1485
01:06:44,000 --> 01:06:45,900
♪♪ [CLASSICAL PIECE]

1486
01:06:51,833 --> 01:06:53,033
HUH.

1487
01:06:54,667 --> 01:06:56,533
HUH.

1488
01:06:56,567 --> 01:06:58,833
♪♪ [CONTINUES]

1489
01:06:58,867 --> 01:07:00,833
- HUH.
- HUH.

1490
01:07:02,500 --> 01:07:04,033
UH-HUH.

1491
01:07:04,067 --> 01:07:05,800
[INHALES, EXHALES DEEPLY]

1492
01:07:05,833 --> 01:07:08,300
- YEAH. WELL...
- UH, UH-HUH...

1493
01:07:08,333 --> 01:07:11,300
AH, YOU KNOW, THAT'S, UH--
THAT'S ABOUT ALL I KNOW.

1494
01:07:11,333 --> 01:07:13,000
- YEAH.
- YOU'RE RIGHT, THOUGH.
IT'S REALLY FUN.

1495
01:07:13,033 --> 01:07:15,333
AND LATER ON, WOULD YOU GUYS
GIVE ME SOME MORE POINTERS?

1496
01:07:15,367 --> 01:07:17,333
- I'D APPRECIATE IT.
- YEAH, YEAH.
A LOT LATER, MIKE.

1497
01:07:17,367 --> 01:07:19,833
RIGHT NOW, WE HAVE TO, UH,
FEED THE CAT.

1498
01:07:19,867 --> 01:07:21,833
WELL, GET A CAT AND FEED IT.

1499
01:07:21,867 --> 01:07:23,200
OKAY, WELL,
I'LL SEE YOU LATER.

1500
01:07:23,233 --> 01:07:25,200
♪♪ [HUMMING CLASSICAL PIECE]

1501
01:07:25,233 --> 01:07:28,533
- [SCOFFING]
- HUH.

1502
01:07:28,567 --> 01:07:32,133
WELL, LET HIM TRY TACKLING
"TWINKLE, TWINKLE,
LITTLE STAR" SOMETIME, HUH?

1503
01:07:32,167 --> 01:07:33,700
- YEAH, THAT'S RIGHT!
- TRY THAT, HUH?

1504
01:07:33,733 --> 01:07:35,500
- ONE MORE TIME.
- YES. YES. LET'S DO IT.

1505
01:07:35,533 --> 01:07:36,967
- OKAY.
- UM...

1506
01:07:37,000 --> 01:07:38,567
- ♪♪
- ♪ TWINK ♪

1507
01:07:40,500 --> 01:07:41,667
- ♪ EL ♪
- ♪♪ [HIGH-PITCHED TONE]

1508
01:07:41,700 --> 01:07:43,367
- [EXCLAIMS]
- OH, DARN! GEEZ!

1509
01:07:50,200 --> 01:07:52,533
- PREPARE FOR BATTLE.
- [SIGHS]

1510
01:07:52,567 --> 01:07:54,967
- SHARP ACCELERATION
FOR ATTACK POSITION.
- [MIKE MUTTERING]

1511
01:07:55,000 --> 01:07:56,800
[GROANS]

1512
01:07:56,833 --> 01:08:00,967
SHAKE 'N BAKE,
AND I DEATH.

1513
01:08:01,000 --> 01:08:04,167
WOW, A TIGHT TURNING RADIUS
ON THAT CHICKEN THING THERE.

1514
01:08:07,000 --> 01:08:09,333
SO THEY'RE JUST USING
OLD SIX-SHOOTERS, HUH?

1515
01:08:09,367 --> 01:08:11,333
SHOOTIN' IRONS.

1516
01:08:11,367 --> 01:08:14,467
[IMITATING GUNSHOTS]

1517
01:08:14,500 --> 01:08:16,800
IT'S NO GOOD.
THEIR DEFENSE IS TOO CRISPY.

1518
01:08:16,833 --> 01:08:17,900
DANG.

1519
01:08:21,500 --> 01:08:23,500
PATHETIC, HUH?

1520
01:08:25,400 --> 01:08:29,033
OH, DON'T TELL ME.
I'M OUT OF ROCKS. DAMN.

1521
01:08:29,067 --> 01:08:32,333
I'LL GENTLY PAT THESE ROCKS
AS A SIGN OF PROTEST.

1522
01:08:36,000 --> 01:08:38,900
ON MY BARK. WOOF!

1523
01:08:42,533 --> 01:08:45,500
WE'VE GOT TO MARK THIS PLANET.

1524
01:08:48,400 --> 01:08:50,133
[IMITATING DOG WHINING]

1525
01:08:50,167 --> 01:08:52,200
- HUH?
- [EQUIPMENT WHIRRING]

1526
01:08:52,233 --> 01:08:55,967
ACTIVATE THE GRAVITY CURTAIN.

1527
01:08:56,000 --> 01:08:58,700
OR THE VENETIAN GRAVITY BLINDS.

1528
01:08:58,733 --> 01:09:00,133
GET OFF MY FOOT.

1529
01:09:00,167 --> 01:09:03,033
♪♪ [HUMMING]

1530
01:09:05,500 --> 01:09:08,067
REMEMBER THESE PEOPLE?
THEY'RE IN OUR FILM.

1531
01:09:10,400 --> 01:09:12,333
I'M WORKING MY MAGIC.

1532
01:09:17,733 --> 01:09:20,667
OH, IT WAS
A MAGNIFICENT VICTORY!

1533
01:09:20,700 --> 01:09:23,367
BUT I'M DEEPLY PLAGUED
WITH REGRET

1534
01:09:23,400 --> 01:09:25,533
- [LAUGHTER]
- ...WHEN I'M FORCED TO DESTROY.

1535
01:09:25,567 --> 01:09:27,867
- YEAH.
- IF IT WASN'T THEM,
IT WOULD'VE BEEN YOU.

1536
01:09:27,900 --> 01:09:29,633
PERHAPS YOU ARE RIGHT.

1537
01:09:29,667 --> 01:09:31,833
- YOU ARE WISE, CHAPMAN.
- [CHUCKLES]

1538
01:09:31,867 --> 01:09:34,967
- ONE DAY, YOU AND HERRON
WILL LEAD OUR PEOPLE.
- YES.

1539
01:09:35,000 --> 01:09:38,167
- I'M GRATEFUL, BUT--
- I WILL TEACH HIM
ALL HE NEEDS TO KNOW.

1540
01:09:38,200 --> 01:09:39,467
OH.

1541
01:09:39,500 --> 01:09:41,300
[IMITATING GOOFY]
OH, HEY, IT WORKED.

1542
01:09:41,333 --> 01:09:42,800
MAMA SOLARITE
DIDN'T RAISE NO DUMMIES.

1543
01:09:42,833 --> 01:09:44,067
[GUFFAWS]

1544
01:09:46,500 --> 01:09:49,167
GO ON. GO ON.

1545
01:09:51,000 --> 01:09:52,633
HE'S AN ELDERLY SOLARITE.

1546
01:09:52,667 --> 01:09:54,633
- HE HAS TROUBLE WITH STAIRS.
- YEAH.

1547
01:09:54,667 --> 01:09:56,200
WHERE'S ZETHA?

1548
01:09:56,233 --> 01:09:58,033
- SHE WENT TO SLEEP EARLY.
- [LAUGHTER]

1549
01:09:58,067 --> 01:10:01,133
SLEEP. I'M VERY TIRED.

1550
01:10:01,167 --> 01:10:04,800
PERHAPS THE BATTLE WAS TOO MUCH
OF A STRAIN ON ME.
GOOD NIGHT.

1551
01:10:04,833 --> 01:10:06,500
- GOOD NIGHT, FATHER.
- SLEEP WELL, SESSOM.

1552
01:10:06,533 --> 01:10:09,833
THERE'S A SUSTACAL
WITH MY NAME ON IT.

1553
01:10:09,867 --> 01:10:12,300
[IMITATING SESSOM]
I'M GONNA GO DRIVE AROUND
AND LEAVE THE BLINKER ON.

1554
01:10:12,333 --> 01:10:13,800
[CHUCKLES]

1555
01:10:13,833 --> 01:10:16,133
I'LL JUST HIDE OUT HERE

1556
01:10:16,167 --> 01:10:18,400
AT FRED AND WILMA'S HOUSE.

1557
01:10:22,333 --> 01:10:24,300
[SCOFFS]
MA'AM, COULD YOU QUIT WRITHING

1558
01:10:24,333 --> 01:10:26,067
ON THE COFFEE TABLE?

1559
01:10:28,200 --> 01:10:31,000
HUH. THEIR BED TECHNOLOGY
IS LIGHT YEARS BEHIND

1560
01:10:31,033 --> 01:10:33,500
THEIR SPACE-GOING CHICKEN
TECHNOLOGY.

1561
01:10:36,567 --> 01:10:38,667
UH, EXCUSE ME, MA'AM.
I DON'T MEAN TO BOTHER YOU.

1562
01:10:38,700 --> 01:10:42,467
DO YOU HAVE ANY LIV-A SNAPS
OR PERHAPS A BEGGIN' STRIP?

1563
01:10:42,500 --> 01:10:44,467
THINK HE'S BEEN BACKPACKING
THROUGH EUROPE?

1564
01:10:44,500 --> 01:10:46,000
[MUTTERS]

1565
01:10:47,700 --> 01:10:49,800
UH, MA'AM, I REALIZE
YOU DON'T KNOW ME,

1566
01:10:49,833 --> 01:10:52,500
BUT I REALLY NEED
TO GO WALKIES.

1567
01:10:55,167 --> 01:10:57,000
OH, HONEY,
YOU LOOK FLUSH.

1568
01:10:57,033 --> 01:10:59,467
LET ME FEEL YOUR NOSE.

1569
01:10:59,500 --> 01:11:01,200
OH. HMM.

1570
01:11:01,233 --> 01:11:03,367
OH, I BET YOU SHED.
I SHED.

1571
01:11:03,400 --> 01:11:05,533
DO YOU SHED?

1572
01:11:06,900 --> 01:11:08,533
LAST CALL, EVERYBODY.
LAST CALL.

1573
01:11:08,567 --> 01:11:10,467
COME ON.

1574
01:11:10,500 --> 01:11:12,833
OKAY, OKAY. HER HAIR
CONTROLS THE LIGHT SWITCH.

1575
01:11:12,867 --> 01:11:15,333
I TOUCH HER HAIR,
THE LIGHTS GO OUT. GOT IT.

1576
01:11:17,333 --> 01:11:20,033
I KNOW. I'LL TRY
SUBMISSIVE URINATION.

1577
01:11:22,667 --> 01:11:26,167
HE'S BASICALLY A CAULIFLOWER
WITH A HANDLE AND EYES.

1578
01:11:30,667 --> 01:11:33,633
EW, IT SMELLS
LIKE WET FUR IN HERE.

1579
01:11:33,667 --> 01:11:37,800
SHE FORGETS SHE'S MUTE
AND THINKS SHE'S BLIND.

1580
01:11:37,833 --> 01:11:39,333
♪♪ [HUMMING ALONG
WITH SOUNDTRACK]

1581
01:11:40,900 --> 01:11:43,167
YOU HAVE A KIND FACE.

1582
01:11:43,200 --> 01:11:45,467
♪♪ [MIKE HUMMING]

1583
01:11:45,500 --> 01:11:47,133
♪♪ [TOM SERVO
IMITATING DRUMBEATS]

1584
01:11:47,167 --> 01:11:50,300
YO. WORD.

1585
01:11:50,333 --> 01:11:53,167
HERE'S THE GINGER
YOU ORDERED, MA'AM.

1586
01:11:55,067 --> 01:11:58,500
UH, I CAN'T GET AWAY
FROM THE LUMBERING SLOW THING.

1587
01:11:58,533 --> 01:12:02,033
WHOA, SHE'S SCREAMING
HER FINGERS OFF RIGHT NOW.

1588
01:12:02,067 --> 01:12:04,667
I'M GONNA TERRIFY HER
WITH THE HAND THING.

1589
01:12:07,400 --> 01:12:09,800
I HAD SUCTION CUPS
PUT ON MY FINGERS.

1590
01:12:09,833 --> 01:12:11,067
SEEMED LIKE A GOOD IDEA
AT THE TIME.

1591
01:12:13,667 --> 01:12:17,133
SO, APPARENTLY WOMEN ARE DEVOID
OF THE FIGHT-OR-FLIGHT REFLEX.

1592
01:12:17,167 --> 01:12:18,833
YEAH, THEY ONLY HAVE
THE FAINTING REFLEX.

1593
01:12:18,867 --> 01:12:21,000
- [SCOFFS]
- WOMEN! [SCOFFS]

1594
01:12:23,033 --> 01:12:24,367
NO MORE FRISBEE CATCHING.

1595
01:12:24,400 --> 01:12:27,033
I'M ON A WHOLE
NOTHER LEVEL NOW.

1596
01:12:30,200 --> 01:12:33,167
THE MONSTER DRESSES
LIKE CAROL CHANNING.

1597
01:12:34,233 --> 01:12:36,533
UH, WAIT, WAIT.
DID I LEAVE ANY CLOTHES?

1598
01:12:36,567 --> 01:12:39,167
DOH! I PIDDLED IN THE CORNER.

1599
01:12:41,333 --> 01:12:44,067
COMMANDER SPOT
WILL BE VERY PLEASED.

1600
01:12:46,833 --> 01:12:49,800
WHERE THE HELL IS THE ELEVATOR?

1601
01:12:49,833 --> 01:12:53,000
SO I GOT HER NOW,
AND I HAVEN'T THE SLIGHTEST IDEA
WHAT TO DO WITH HER.

1602
01:12:53,033 --> 01:12:54,667
[GUFFAWS]

1603
01:12:56,667 --> 01:12:59,400
TSK. HANG ON.
I'M GONNA GET A TWO-WHEELER.

1604
01:13:03,233 --> 01:13:06,967
NURSE! NURSE!

1605
01:13:07,000 --> 01:13:09,467
OKAY, OKAY, OKAY.
EVERYTHING'S COOL.

1606
01:13:09,500 --> 01:13:11,367
I'M NOT GONNA BEAT MYSELF UP
OVER THIS.

1607
01:13:15,000 --> 01:13:16,367
- [IMITATING DINO FROM
THE FLINTSTONES BARKING]
- DINO, NO!

1608
01:13:16,400 --> 01:13:19,467
- WHAT WAS THAT?
- IT'S OVER THERE.

1609
01:13:19,500 --> 01:13:21,633
YEAH, I GUESS THEIR RAUCOUS
POSTWAR CELEBRATION

1610
01:13:21,667 --> 01:13:23,033
WILL HAVE TO WAIT.

1611
01:13:24,700 --> 01:13:26,867
YOU WASH MY FACE OFF
WITH SNOW.

1612
01:13:26,900 --> 01:13:29,200
THERE. FOUND MY MARK. GOOD.

1613
01:13:29,233 --> 01:13:31,333
- [SESSOM] HELP.
- SESSOM!

1614
01:13:31,367 --> 01:13:33,133
- OH, FATHER!
- HE LICKED ME ALL OVER!

1615
01:13:33,167 --> 01:13:34,700
OH, FATHER!

1616
01:13:34,733 --> 01:13:37,033
- WHAT HAPPENED TO HIM?
- I THINK IT WAS THE SOLARITE.

1617
01:13:37,067 --> 01:13:39,167
- ARE YOU ALL RIGHT?
- I...

1618
01:13:39,200 --> 01:13:42,133
- WHAT HAPPENED?
- I DON'T KNOW.

1619
01:13:42,167 --> 01:13:45,133
WAS IT THE SOLARITE?
DID YOU SEE HIM?

1620
01:13:45,167 --> 01:13:47,833
- IT WAS TERRIBLE.
- [CHUCKLES]

1621
01:13:47,867 --> 01:13:51,667
I PUSHED DOWN AN OLD GUY
FOR YOU, DARLING.

1622
01:13:51,700 --> 01:13:54,467
WE'LL BUILD A SPLIT-LEVEL
WITH A DOGGIE DOOR.

1623
01:13:54,500 --> 01:13:58,333
I'LL FETCH THE PAPER FOR YOU
EVERY DAY.

1624
01:13:58,367 --> 01:14:00,467
OKAY, I'M GONNA GO BARK
FOR NO REASON,

1625
01:14:00,500 --> 01:14:02,333
LICK MYSELF
AND EAT GRASS TILL I VOMIT,

1626
01:14:02,367 --> 01:14:05,967
THEN I'LL BE BACK.
[GUFFAWS]

1627
01:14:06,000 --> 01:14:07,367
[WHIRRING]

1628
01:14:07,400 --> 01:14:09,067
OKAY, WHAT'D I DO?

1629
01:14:11,167 --> 01:14:12,300
[WHIRRING]

1630
01:14:12,333 --> 01:14:15,800
WHOA. I'M WAY OUT
OF MY LEAGUE NOW.

1631
01:14:15,833 --> 01:14:17,633
[HERRON]
I'M GOING TO THE CONTROL ROOM.

1632
01:14:17,667 --> 01:14:19,867
[CHAPMAN]
NO, YOU STAY WITH LIARA.

1633
01:14:19,900 --> 01:14:22,300
- CHAPMAN!
- YES?

1634
01:14:22,333 --> 01:14:24,867
HOW FAR DO YOU THINK YOU'D BE
IF I HADN'T CALLED YOU BACK?

1635
01:14:24,900 --> 01:14:26,800
GO THROUGH THAT CORRIDOR.
IT'S SHORTER.

1636
01:14:26,833 --> 01:14:27,800
- RIGHT.
- BUT BE CAREFUL.

1637
01:14:27,833 --> 01:14:29,500
AND BUTTON YOUR BLOUSE.

1638
01:14:29,533 --> 01:14:31,633
- I'LL BE ALL RIGHT.
- OH, HERRON.

1639
01:14:31,667 --> 01:14:33,200
[SNIFFING]

1640
01:14:33,233 --> 01:14:35,533
OOH, THEY HAVE DOGS. EW.

1641
01:14:37,200 --> 01:14:39,633
ZETHA, ARE YOU ALL RIGHT?

1642
01:14:39,667 --> 01:14:41,167
UM, EXCUSE ME. I--
[CLEARS THROAT]

1643
01:14:41,200 --> 01:14:44,300
I HAVE THE ELEMENT OF,
UH, SURPRISE OVER YOU.

1644
01:14:44,333 --> 01:14:45,700
[ZETHA SCREAMS]

1645
01:14:45,733 --> 01:14:48,700
IT'S A GOOD GUARD DOG,
YOU HAVE TO ADMIT.

1646
01:14:48,733 --> 01:14:50,133
OKAY, HANG ON.

1647
01:14:50,167 --> 01:14:51,800
ON MY WAY.
BE RIGHT THERE.

1648
01:14:51,833 --> 01:14:53,467
HANG ON.
JUST A MINUTE.

1649
01:14:53,500 --> 01:14:55,200
NICE PUPPY.
[NERVOUS CHUCKLE]
GOOD DOG.

1650
01:14:55,233 --> 01:14:57,200
JUST LET ME TURN AROUND
AND PRESENT MY BUTT TO YOU.

1651
01:14:57,233 --> 01:15:00,333
I THINK YOU'LL FIND
EVERYTHING IN ORDER.
[NERVOUS CHUCKLE]

1652
01:15:00,367 --> 01:15:03,033
- HEY! WATCH THE PLATES!
- [SCREAMS]

1653
01:15:03,067 --> 01:15:05,800
ANYBODY COULD JUST DEMATERIALIZE
THEMSELVES BY ACCIDENT.

1654
01:15:05,833 --> 01:15:07,633
MAYBE THEY SHOULD
CORDON IT OFF OR SOMETHING.

1655
01:15:07,667 --> 01:15:09,833
YEAH.

1656
01:15:09,867 --> 01:15:13,967
THEY SHOULD SCRATCH HIS BELLY
TILL HIS LEG SHAKES
TO SUBDUE HIM.

1657
01:15:14,000 --> 01:15:15,667
YOU'RE IT!

1658
01:15:15,700 --> 01:15:17,533
COME ON!
I TAGGED YOU!

1659
01:15:17,567 --> 01:15:19,833
[SOLARITE GROWLING]

1660
01:15:19,867 --> 01:15:21,200
SORRY.

1661
01:15:23,067 --> 01:15:24,833
HANG ON. I'M NOT QUITE--
OKAY, THERE WE GO.

1662
01:15:24,867 --> 01:15:26,733
[SCREECHING]

1663
01:15:29,033 --> 01:15:32,000
GOOD NIGHT, EVERYBODY.
MINNEAPOLIS ROCKS.

1664
01:15:32,033 --> 01:15:34,167
BIG HAND FOR THE SOLARITE BAND.
COME ON.

1665
01:15:34,200 --> 01:15:37,833
♪ SHANNON IS GONE, I SEE ♪

1666
01:15:37,867 --> 01:15:41,467
HUH. NEXT TIME
WE'RE GETTING A CAT.

1667
01:15:41,500 --> 01:15:45,033
NOT A "DANGEROUS" SIGN?
ROPE IT OFF? ANYTHING?

1668
01:15:45,067 --> 01:15:47,300
NOPE.

1669
01:15:47,333 --> 01:15:49,900
ALL DOGS GO TO HELL.

1670
01:15:52,000 --> 01:15:53,800
WE'RE FRIENDS NOW. WHY?

1671
01:15:53,833 --> 01:15:55,500
HOW'S SESSOM?

1672
01:15:55,533 --> 01:15:57,133
HE WILL BE ALL RIGHT.
LIARA'S WITH HIM.

1673
01:15:57,167 --> 01:15:58,133
I'M GLAD.

1674
01:15:58,167 --> 01:16:00,300
YOU STILL WISH TO RETURN
TO YOUR WORLD?

1675
01:16:00,333 --> 01:16:02,467
- YES, BUT--
- WELL, THEN, TONIGHT'S
THE BEST TIME.

1676
01:16:02,500 --> 01:16:05,667
THE CHAOS OF BATTLE
HAS BROUGHT US CLOSER TO
YOUR MOON THAN WE'VE EVER BEEN.

1677
01:16:05,700 --> 01:16:08,133
- REALLY?
- IT'LL BE A SIMPLE TASK
TO MANEUVER RHETON SLOWLY

1678
01:16:08,167 --> 01:16:10,467
- ...AND STEADILY EVEN CLOSER,
AND THE RISK WILL NOT BE GREAT--
- IT WILL?

1679
01:16:10,500 --> 01:16:12,633
- ...BECAUSE THE TRAVEL TIME
WILL BE SHORT.
- THIS IS FASCINATING!

1680
01:16:12,667 --> 01:16:14,633
IT WILL BE WELL WITHIN
THE RANGE OF THE MOON'S RADAR?

1681
01:16:14,667 --> 01:16:16,967
- YES, BUT WE CANNOT
GO UNNOTICED.
- COME ON.

1682
01:16:17,000 --> 01:16:19,633
- NOW, AS SOON AS WE'RE WITHIN
RANGE OF YOUR MOON--
- OKAY.

1683
01:16:19,667 --> 01:16:22,467
- ...MY MEN WILL CARRY
YOUR SUIT OUT INTO THE OPEN.
- I GOTTA GO FOLD SOME SOCKS.

1684
01:16:22,500 --> 01:16:23,967
- IF YOUR PEOPLE COME
TO INVESTIGATE--
- THIS IS RIVETING!

1685
01:16:24,000 --> 01:16:26,000
...WE'LL PULL THEM
INTO OUR GRAVITY
AND DIRECT THEIR LANDING.

1686
01:16:26,033 --> 01:16:28,633
- MEANWHILE,
YOU WILL ENTER YOUR SUIT--
- WOW. NO!

1687
01:16:28,667 --> 01:16:31,800
...SEAL IT UP
SO THAT YOU'RE NOT EXPOSED
TO OUR ATMOSPHERE, AND...

1688
01:16:31,833 --> 01:16:33,667
- WELL, THE REST YOU KNOW.
- THIS IS FASCINATING!

1689
01:16:33,700 --> 01:16:35,467
- WHERE SHALL I MEET YOU?
- IN THE CONTROL CHAMBER.

1690
01:16:35,500 --> 01:16:38,000
- SOMEONE WILL COME FOR YOU.
- WOW.

1691
01:16:44,333 --> 01:16:46,833
I HOGGED OUT ON A BABY CARROT.

1692
01:16:46,867 --> 01:16:49,133
I NEED TO WALK IT OFF.

1693
01:16:49,167 --> 01:16:50,800
- HI.
- UH, GET ANY BETTER?

1694
01:16:50,833 --> 01:16:52,800
- ZETHA.
- NO.

1695
01:16:52,833 --> 01:16:54,167
IT'S YOU.

1696
01:16:54,200 --> 01:16:56,000
YES, FRANK CHAPMAN.

1697
01:16:56,033 --> 01:16:58,000
- BUT YOU CAN TALK.
- SON OF A...

1698
01:16:58,033 --> 01:17:00,633
- GREAT.
- FROM MY FRIGHT, WHEN I THOUGHT
YOU WERE GOING TO BE KILLED,

1699
01:17:00,667 --> 01:17:02,633
SOMETHING HAPPENED.

1700
01:17:02,667 --> 01:17:06,700
AND AFTER I SCREAMED,
I FOUND I WAS ABLE TO SPEAK.

1701
01:17:06,733 --> 01:17:09,000
- ZETHA...
- HEY, I'M TALKING HERE!

1702
01:17:09,033 --> 01:17:11,800
- I HAVE MANY THINGS TO SAY
TO YOU, FRANK CHAPMAN.
- LIKE "PICKLE."

1703
01:17:11,833 --> 01:17:14,367
IT'S SO WONDERFUL--
YOU BEING ABLE TO TALK.

1704
01:17:14,400 --> 01:17:16,367
AND I HAVE SO MANY THINGS
TO SAY TO YOU.

1705
01:17:16,400 --> 01:17:17,967
LIKE "I THINK
WE SHOULD BREAK UP."

1706
01:17:18,000 --> 01:17:19,633
OH, EVERYTHING
HAS BEEN TERRIBLE.

1707
01:17:19,667 --> 01:17:22,667
ESPECIALLY THAT LUNCH.
EW. IT WAS AWFUL.

1708
01:17:22,700 --> 01:17:24,667
YOU'RE SO LOVELY.

1709
01:17:24,700 --> 01:17:27,000
YOU HAVE SUCH
AN ADORABLE LITTLE FACE.

1710
01:17:27,033 --> 01:17:29,000
I THINK I'LL JAM
MY TONGUE INTO IT.

1711
01:17:31,000 --> 01:17:33,467
BOY, SHE IS EARNING COMBAT PAY.

1712
01:17:33,500 --> 01:17:35,467
- YEP.
- WHOO.

1713
01:17:35,500 --> 01:17:40,367
AND SHE'S HORRIFIED
BACK INTO MUTENESS.

1714
01:17:40,400 --> 01:17:43,467
- ISN'T IT STRANGE?
- YOU HAVEN'T CALLED
THE POLICE YET.

1715
01:17:43,500 --> 01:17:46,467
HERE IN THIS PLACE,
I HAVE FOUND PERHAPS

1716
01:17:46,500 --> 01:17:48,200
WHAT I'VE BEEN LOOKING FOR
ALL MY LIFE.

1717
01:17:48,233 --> 01:17:51,500
- PANCAKES.
- AND I MUST LEAVE.

1718
01:17:51,533 --> 01:17:54,300
ALTHOUGH EVERYTHING WITHIN ME
WANTS TO STAY.

1719
01:17:54,333 --> 01:17:56,833
ESPECIALLY MY SPLEEN.

1720
01:17:56,867 --> 01:17:59,000
IT'S MY SOLEMN DUTY TO LEAVE.

1721
01:17:59,033 --> 01:18:00,833
YOU UNDERSTAND THAT, DON'T YOU?

1722
01:18:00,867 --> 01:18:04,367
I'M SORRY. NOW I'M DEAF.

1723
01:18:04,400 --> 01:18:06,633
FRANK CHAPMAN,
I'VE BEEN IN LOVE WITH YOU

1724
01:18:06,667 --> 01:18:09,000
- ...SINCE THE FIRST TIME
I SAW YOU--
- EW.

1725
01:18:09,033 --> 01:18:11,500
...AND I'VE NEVER BEEN ABLE
TO SPEAK A WORD OF IT
UNTIL NOW.

1726
01:18:11,533 --> 01:18:13,967
IS HE A TURNIP
THAT GREW A FACE?

1727
01:18:14,000 --> 01:18:16,867
BUT AS I KNOW,
MY LOVE FOR YOU IS SO STRONG.

1728
01:18:16,900 --> 01:18:19,133
I CAN OVERCOME MY REVULSION.

1729
01:18:19,167 --> 01:18:22,833
SO I ALSO KNOW
THAT YOU WILL LEAVE.

1730
01:18:22,867 --> 01:18:25,133
I MUST LEAVE.

1731
01:18:25,167 --> 01:18:28,200
HANG ON.
I WANNA GET MY GUM BACK.

1732
01:18:28,233 --> 01:18:30,300
MM. WELL, I SEE
YOU'VE BEEN FLOSSING.

1733
01:18:30,333 --> 01:18:32,033
THAT'S GOOD.

1734
01:18:35,000 --> 01:18:38,467
THE WORD "LOVE"
MEANS DETEST, RIGHT?

1735
01:18:38,500 --> 01:18:40,167
WOW, THE FIRST THING
I EVER SAY IN MY LIFE,

1736
01:18:40,200 --> 01:18:43,167
AND I BLOW IT BIG-TIME.

1737
01:18:43,200 --> 01:18:44,800
LOOK, IT'S OVER.
LEAVE ME ALONE.

1738
01:18:44,833 --> 01:18:46,467
IT'S OVER!

1739
01:18:46,500 --> 01:18:48,067
[EQUIPMENT WHIRRING]

1740
01:18:50,500 --> 01:18:53,033
- GOOD. YOU'RE ON TIME.
- FOR ONCE.

1741
01:18:53,067 --> 01:18:55,533
- [HERRON] HERE WE GO.
- LET ME HEAR YOU SAY "YEAH."

1742
01:18:55,567 --> 01:18:57,533
- [WHIRRING INTENSIFIES]
- ANOTHER HOUR,

1743
01:18:57,567 --> 01:18:59,833
AND WE SHALL BE CLOSE ENOUGH
FOR YOU TO BE FOUND.

1744
01:18:59,867 --> 01:19:02,867
I'M JUST GONNA DROP YOU OFF
AT THE BUS STATION.
I HOPE THAT'S OKAY.

1745
01:19:02,900 --> 01:19:04,500
[WHIRRING CONTINUES]

1746
01:19:04,533 --> 01:19:07,000
DON'T. DON'T.
YOU'RE SMOTHERING ME.

1747
01:19:10,000 --> 01:19:12,700
DELIVERY FOR ROBERT DOWNEY, JR.

1748
01:19:15,200 --> 01:19:19,467
[WOMAN ON RADIO]
LUNAR BASE 1
TO ROCKET SHIP 380. OVER.

1749
01:19:19,500 --> 01:19:23,167
THIS IS ROCKET SHIP 380
TO LUNAR BASE 1. OVER.

1750
01:19:23,200 --> 01:19:26,800
RADAR HAS JUST PICKED UP
A GIANT ASTEROID.
IDENTITY UNKNOWN.

1751
01:19:26,833 --> 01:19:29,467
CANNOT FIND ANY RECORD OF IT
IN THE SPACE CHARTS.

1752
01:19:29,500 --> 01:19:31,300
THE PHANTOM PLANET.

1753
01:19:31,333 --> 01:19:33,867
GIVE US EXACT POSITION
OF ASTEROID.

1754
01:19:33,900 --> 01:19:36,333
NINE DEGREES
IN NORTHERN CLUSTER FIELD.

1755
01:19:36,367 --> 01:19:38,333
AND I HAVE AN ORDER
FROM COLONEL LANSFIELD.

1756
01:19:38,367 --> 01:19:40,367
YOU ARE TO LAND
ON THIS ASTEROID

1757
01:19:40,400 --> 01:19:42,300
AND SEND WHITE TO INVESTIGATE.

1758
01:19:42,333 --> 01:19:44,367
IMMEDIATELY, YOUNG MAN.

1759
01:19:44,400 --> 01:19:46,533
I--

1760
01:19:46,567 --> 01:19:49,967
I HOPE YOU WILL FIND HAPPINESS
BACK WITH YOUR PEOPLE.

1761
01:19:50,000 --> 01:19:53,300
YOU WOULD BE MY HAPPINESS...
IF YOU WERE THERE.

1762
01:19:53,333 --> 01:19:55,800
YOU WANNA LIVE IN MY HABITRAIL?

1763
01:19:55,833 --> 01:19:57,867
FRANK CHAPMAN, PLEASE...

1764
01:19:57,900 --> 01:19:59,867
YOU MUST TAKE THIS STONE.

1765
01:19:59,900 --> 01:20:01,633
AND RUB IT IN YOUR ARMPITS.

1766
01:20:01,667 --> 01:20:03,833
IT WILL BE A GOOD LUCK CHARM.

1767
01:20:03,867 --> 01:20:05,533
HOLD ON TO IT.

1768
01:20:05,567 --> 01:20:08,967
IT WILL HELP YOU TO GO BACK
SAFELY TO YOUR PEOPLE.

1769
01:20:09,000 --> 01:20:10,467
KEEP IT.

1770
01:20:10,500 --> 01:20:12,533
OH, SHE'S GONNA
"JUST FRIEND" HIM.

1771
01:20:12,567 --> 01:20:16,800
AND REMEMBER MY-- MY LOVE.

1772
01:20:16,833 --> 01:20:19,667
YES, ZETHA.
I'LL KEEP IT FOREVER.

1773
01:20:19,700 --> 01:20:21,167
IN MY JUNK DRAWER
IN THE BASEMENT.

1774
01:20:24,000 --> 01:20:25,800
I JUST CONFIRMED IT.

1775
01:20:25,833 --> 01:20:28,800
A ROCKET, SIMILAR TO YOURS,
IS HEADING IN OUR DIRECTION.

1776
01:20:28,833 --> 01:20:30,967
- I HOPE THEY WON'T CRASH.
- DON'T WORRY.

1777
01:20:31,000 --> 01:20:34,800
- IT WILL.
- I HAVE THE BEST MEN
ON GRAVITATION CONTROL.

1778
01:20:34,833 --> 01:20:36,800
AND I HAVE ANOTHER MAN
WHO'S COMING TO HELP ME

1779
01:20:36,833 --> 01:20:39,333
TURN ON THE OXYGEN TANKS
AS SOON AS YOU'RE IN YOUR SUIT.

1780
01:20:39,367 --> 01:20:42,300
- [TOM SERVO MUTTERS]
- THANK YOU, HERRON.

1781
01:20:42,333 --> 01:20:45,833
YOU KNOW,
WE'VE BECOME FRIENDS HERE.

1782
01:20:45,867 --> 01:20:49,033
- GOOD FRIENDS.
- WHICH IS WHY I BRING UP
MY MISSING WALLET.

1783
01:20:49,067 --> 01:20:51,500
WE WERE
TO BECOME FRIENDS ANYWHERE--

1784
01:20:51,533 --> 01:20:53,867
YOUR PLANET OR MY EARTH.

1785
01:20:53,900 --> 01:20:55,300
[GROANS]

1786
01:20:55,333 --> 01:20:57,133
I WISH YOU AND LIARA
MUCH HAPPINESS.

1787
01:20:57,167 --> 01:20:59,833
THIS IS LONGER THAN
A MINNESOTA GOOD-BYE.

1788
01:21:01,567 --> 01:21:03,533
UM, DON'T CALL,
'CAUSE I DON'T HAVE A PHONE,

1789
01:21:03,567 --> 01:21:05,467
AND DON'T WRITE
'CAUSE WE DON'T HAVE MAIL HERE.

1790
01:21:05,500 --> 01:21:06,867
AND I DON'T HAVE E-MAIL.

1791
01:21:06,900 --> 01:21:10,467
LOOK, I'M JUST REALLY HARD
TO GET AHOLD OF.

1792
01:21:10,500 --> 01:21:12,800
WHEW! I THOUGHT I WAS GONNA SEE
THAT GIANT PINK TONGUE

1793
01:21:12,833 --> 01:21:14,833
COMING AT ME AGAIN.

1794
01:21:17,000 --> 01:21:19,633
UH, A LOT OF ANIMALS
GOT IN HERE,
USED IT FOR THEIR TOILET.

1795
01:21:19,667 --> 01:21:22,367
WE TRIED TO CLEAN
MOST OF IT OUT.

1796
01:21:22,400 --> 01:21:24,200
OKAY, IN YOU GO. WHOA.

1797
01:21:24,233 --> 01:21:26,467
CHECK THIS OUT.
HE'S NUDE!

1798
01:21:26,500 --> 01:21:27,833
OH, MAN.

1799
01:21:29,367 --> 01:21:31,967
JUST ONE MORE PEEK. WOW.

1800
01:21:32,000 --> 01:21:35,133
WHEW. HE ALMOST STAYED.

1801
01:21:35,167 --> 01:21:37,133
OH-- OH, WAIT, WAIT, WAIT.

1802
01:21:37,167 --> 01:21:39,133
MY THUMB IS BENT BACK IN HERE.
OW! OOH!

1803
01:21:39,167 --> 01:21:41,833
MY LEG IS ALL TWISTED.
OW! OOH!

1804
01:21:43,500 --> 01:21:45,967
YEAH, THE MOVIE'S CIRCLING
THE DRAIN AT THIS POINT.

1805
01:21:46,000 --> 01:21:49,200
- YEP.
- I FIND YOU GUILTY AS CHARGED.

1806
01:21:49,233 --> 01:21:51,533
- [WOMEN SHOUTING] KILL HIM!
- [TOM SERVO MUTTERS]

1807
01:21:51,567 --> 01:21:53,633
YOU'LL NEVER SEE
YOUR WORLD AGAIN.

1808
01:21:53,667 --> 01:21:55,500
COME ON! WE DIDN'T LIKE
THESE SCENES THE FIRST TIME!

1809
01:21:55,533 --> 01:21:57,967
YEAH.

1810
01:21:58,000 --> 01:22:00,833
WHAT IF HIS FLASHBACKS
LAP THEMSELVES?

1811
01:22:02,833 --> 01:22:04,833
[IMITATING GOOFY]
CAN I GO OUT, PLEASE?

1812
01:22:07,200 --> 01:22:10,533
FRANK CHAPMAN,
I'VE BEEN IN LOVE WITH YOU
SINCE THE FIRST TIME I SAW YOU.

1813
01:22:10,567 --> 01:22:13,533
NO FAIR! YOU CAN'T FLASHBACK
TO STUFF WE SAW 10 SECONDS AGO!

1814
01:22:13,567 --> 01:22:15,200
YEAH.

1815
01:22:15,233 --> 01:22:17,200
CHAPMAN. CHAPMAN!

1816
01:22:17,233 --> 01:22:19,633
- YOU GOT ANY GUM?
- WHITE TO BEECHER.

1817
01:22:19,667 --> 01:22:21,633
COME IN, WHITE.

1818
01:22:21,667 --> 01:22:23,200
I FOUND CHAPMAN.
HE'S ALIVE.

1819
01:22:24,733 --> 01:22:27,800
BUT THERE'S NO TRACE
OF MAKONNEN.

1820
01:22:27,833 --> 01:22:29,800
WHERE'S MAKONNEN?

1821
01:22:29,833 --> 01:22:32,367
HE'S DEAD. HE'S GONE.

1822
01:22:32,400 --> 01:22:36,500
HE KEPT YAPPING ABOUT BEAUTY,
SO I SHOT HIM OUT THE AIR LOCK.

1823
01:22:36,533 --> 01:22:39,333
OH, I AM SO JAMMED UP
IN MY CUP RIGHT NOW.

1824
01:22:39,367 --> 01:22:41,000
OH!

1825
01:22:42,067 --> 01:22:44,700
WHERE ARE WE?

1826
01:22:44,733 --> 01:22:46,800
WHERE ARE THEY?

1827
01:22:46,833 --> 01:22:48,533
WHERE ARE THE OTHERS?

1828
01:22:48,567 --> 01:22:50,467
AND WHERE'S WALDO?
WHAT ABOUT THAT WHOLE ISSUE?

1829
01:22:50,500 --> 01:22:51,633
WHERE'S WHO?

1830
01:22:51,667 --> 01:22:52,867
ZETHA.

1831
01:22:52,900 --> 01:22:54,800
WHAT ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT?

1832
01:22:54,833 --> 01:22:58,300
SESSOM, HERRON...

1833
01:22:58,333 --> 01:23:00,300
MAN, YOU ARE NUTTIER
THAN AN OUTHOUSE RAT.

1834
01:23:00,333 --> 01:23:02,167
COME ON.
LET'S GET BACK TO THE SHIP.

1835
01:23:02,200 --> 01:23:03,800
HEY, YOU WANNA HEAR
SOMETHING FUNNY?

1836
01:23:03,833 --> 01:23:06,200
I FOUND
A LITTLE DARK-HAIRED WOMAN
ON THE BOTTOM OF MY SHOE.

1837
01:23:06,233 --> 01:23:07,367
[CHUCKLES]

1838
01:23:10,033 --> 01:23:11,833
WHITE TO BEECHER.

1839
01:23:11,867 --> 01:23:13,800
I'M BRINGING HIM IN.

1840
01:23:13,833 --> 01:23:15,467
HE SEEMS TO BE ALL RIGHT.

1841
01:23:15,500 --> 01:23:17,467
HE SAYS MAKONNEN IS DEAD.

1842
01:23:17,500 --> 01:23:19,300
HE KEEPS TALKING
ABOUT OTHER PEOPLE.

1843
01:23:19,333 --> 01:23:20,967
I THINK HE'S IN
A STATE OF SHOCK.

1844
01:23:21,000 --> 01:23:22,333
DO YOU NEED ASSISTANCE?

1845
01:23:22,367 --> 01:23:23,700
NO, CAPTAIN.
I CAN HANDLE HIM ALONE.

1846
01:23:23,733 --> 01:23:25,967
WELL, OKAY.

1847
01:23:26,000 --> 01:23:27,533
YOU KNOW, FRANK,
YOU'RE A LUCKY GUY.

1848
01:23:27,567 --> 01:23:29,800
YOU'RE GOING TO
A NICE FEDERAL PRISON.

1849
01:23:29,833 --> 01:23:32,033
THIS IS A WANDERING PLANET.
COULD'VE CARRIED YOU ANYWHERE.

1850
01:23:32,067 --> 01:23:34,533
EAST LANSING, CRAB NEBULA,
OXNARD.

1851
01:23:34,567 --> 01:23:36,167
I'M SURE GLAD WE FOUND YOU.

1852
01:23:36,200 --> 01:23:37,533
'CAUSE WE RAN OUT
OF UGLY GUYS.

1853
01:23:37,567 --> 01:23:39,067
ZETHA...

1854
01:23:40,700 --> 01:23:42,867
WHERE IS SHE?

1855
01:23:42,900 --> 01:23:44,867
WHAT YOU NEED IS REST.

1856
01:23:44,900 --> 01:23:47,333
AND A STERN LECTURE
ABOUT LETTING YOUR PARTNER DIE.

1857
01:23:48,733 --> 01:23:50,667
SO, WERE YOU SMALL
WHEN YOU WERE GONE?

1858
01:23:50,700 --> 01:23:53,000
'CAUSE YOU'RE ACTING
LIKE YOU WERE REALLY SMALL.

1859
01:23:55,000 --> 01:23:57,300
I JUST WANNA REMIND YOU
THIS IS A NORTHWEST FLIGHT,

1860
01:23:57,333 --> 01:23:59,300
SO WE'LL BE SITTING
ON THE TARMAC FOR AN HOUR

1861
01:23:59,333 --> 01:24:01,633
WITH NO BEVERAGES
AND AIR CONDITIONING,
AND WE'RE OUT OF MEALS,

1862
01:24:01,667 --> 01:24:03,633
AND THE FLIGHT ATTENDANTS
ARE OVERWORKED AND ABUSIVE,

1863
01:24:03,667 --> 01:24:05,867
AND IF YOU COMPLAIN,
WE'LL THROW YOU OFF THE FLIGHT.

1864
01:24:05,900 --> 01:24:08,033
[EQUIPMENT BEEPING]

1865
01:24:09,733 --> 01:24:11,700
PREPARE FOR IMMEDIATE TAKEOFF.

1866
01:24:11,733 --> 01:24:13,367
I AM PREPARING
FOR IMMEDIATE TAKEOFF.

1867
01:24:13,400 --> 01:24:16,800
YOU SEE ME PREPARING?
TAKING OFF AIR TANKS
IS PREPARING.

1868
01:24:16,833 --> 01:24:18,700
HOW DO YOU FEEL, CHAPMAN?

1869
01:24:18,733 --> 01:24:20,133
I DON'T KNOW.

1870
01:24:20,167 --> 01:24:22,300
I THINK I'M CARSICK.

1871
01:24:22,333 --> 01:24:24,133
I DON'T UNDERSTAND.

1872
01:24:24,167 --> 01:24:26,167
WHY CAN'T I HAVE MY SIPPY CUP?

1873
01:24:26,200 --> 01:24:28,633
IT'S UNBELIEVABLE.

1874
01:24:28,667 --> 01:24:31,633
[BEECHER]
WE'LL GET YOU BACK TO MOON BASE
FOR A THOROUGH EXAMINATION.

1875
01:24:31,667 --> 01:24:34,833
- AND SPANKING.
- [BEECHER]
DO YOU THINK YOU'RE HURT?

1876
01:24:34,867 --> 01:24:37,033
I DON'T THINK SO.

1877
01:24:37,067 --> 01:24:39,200
[BEECHER]
YOU MUST HAVE BEEN KNOCKED OUT
FOR QUITE A WHILE.

1878
01:24:39,233 --> 01:24:41,967
WE HIT YOU AS HARD
AS WE COULD.

1879
01:24:42,000 --> 01:24:44,200
I MUST HAVE BEEN DREAMING.

1880
01:24:44,233 --> 01:24:46,867
QUITE POSSIBLE
YOU WERE DELIRIOUS.

1881
01:24:46,900 --> 01:24:49,467
THE SHOCK OF THE CRASH-LANDING
OF YOUR SHIP.

1882
01:24:49,500 --> 01:24:50,833
RAY'S GONE.

1883
01:24:50,867 --> 01:24:53,300
WHY DON'T WE PLAY THE QUIET GAME
WHEN WE TAKE OFF, OKAY?

1884
01:24:53,333 --> 01:24:55,467
BUT I JUST LEFT
ZETHA AND HERRON.

1885
01:24:55,500 --> 01:24:57,367
THEY GAVE ME ROCKS AND STUFF.

1886
01:24:59,200 --> 01:25:02,333
WELL, I GOT A GRISHAM NOVEL.
I GOTTA GET STARTED ON THAT.

1887
01:25:05,033 --> 01:25:07,667
I SHOULD HAVE GOTTEN HER
A STICK.

1888
01:25:09,167 --> 01:25:11,033
SHE HAD SUCH
AN ADORABLE LITTLE FACE.

1889
01:25:11,067 --> 01:25:14,200
YEAH, WELL,
SO DOES PAUL WILLIAMS,
BUT YOU DON'T FRENCH-KISS HIM!

1890
01:25:14,233 --> 01:25:16,667
ALL ROCKETS READY FOR FIRING.
STAND BY FOR COUNTDOWN.

1891
01:25:16,700 --> 01:25:18,200
YOU GUYS WANNA SEE MY ROCK?

1892
01:25:18,233 --> 01:25:20,533
THE GRAVITY OF THIS PLANETOID
IS VERY STRONG.

1893
01:25:20,567 --> 01:25:22,967
WE'LL NEED EVERY BIT OF THRUST
FOR OUR TAKEOFF.

1894
01:25:23,000 --> 01:25:24,667
- DON'T WORRY.
- I'VE GOT EXTRA THRUST.

1895
01:25:24,700 --> 01:25:26,133
I KNOW WE'RE GONNA MAKE IT.

1896
01:25:26,167 --> 01:25:27,333
[BEECHER]
START YOUR COUNTDOWN.

1897
01:25:27,367 --> 01:25:29,333
- [WHITE] TEN, NINE--
- RIGHT.

1898
01:25:29,367 --> 01:25:30,967
- ...EIGHT--
- YEAH.

1899
01:25:31,000 --> 01:25:32,833
- ...SEVEN, SIX--
- LET'S GET ON WITH IT.

1900
01:25:32,867 --> 01:25:34,800
- MM-HMM.
- ...FIVE, FOUR--

1901
01:25:34,833 --> 01:25:37,500
- PI!
- ...THREE, TWO,

1902
01:25:37,533 --> 01:25:38,800
ONE, ZERO.

1903
01:25:38,833 --> 01:25:39,967
[ROCKET ENGINE BLASTS]

1904
01:25:40,000 --> 01:25:42,200
AND THEY DIE.

1905
01:25:42,233 --> 01:25:44,667
HOUSTON, WE HAVE A MORON.
OVER.

1906
01:25:47,700 --> 01:25:49,033
CUT OFF POWER.

1907
01:25:49,067 --> 01:25:50,667
IS THAT A GOOD IDEA, ROY?

1908
01:25:50,700 --> 01:25:52,000
POWER OFF.

1909
01:25:53,700 --> 01:25:55,667
THE REAR SCREEN.

1910
01:25:55,700 --> 01:25:57,333
REAR SCREEN.

1911
01:25:57,367 --> 01:26:01,000
FAREWELL, CHUNKED AND FORMED
LIGHT AND DARK MEAT.

1912
01:26:01,033 --> 01:26:04,300
A BIG CHUNK OF SEWA--
OH, NO, THAT'S HIS FACE.

1913
01:26:04,333 --> 01:26:06,167
I KNOW NOW
THEY'LL NEVER BELIEVE ME.

1914
01:26:06,200 --> 01:26:08,533
I'LL HAVE TO KILL THEM ALL.

1915
01:26:08,567 --> 01:26:10,200
EVEN WITH THIS,
THEY'LL NEVER BELIEVE ME.

1916
01:26:10,233 --> 01:26:11,500
AN OLD PIECE OF GUM?

1917
